hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Especially Merciful. Al-Hafiz Abu al-Qasim Zahir b. Tahir b. Muhammad al-Shahhami informed us, by recitation to him; Abu Sa'd Muhammad b. Abd al-Rahman b. Muhammad al-Janzarudhi informed us; he said: Abu Amr Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Hamdan al-Hiri the jurist informed us, by recitation to him; he said: the Imam Abu Ya'la Ahmad b. Ali b. al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us in Mosul in the year 306 AH, he said: Ali b. al-Ja'd narrated to us, Qays b. al-Rabi' narrated to us, Uthman b. al-Mughira narrated to us, from Ali b. Rabi'a, from Asma b. al-Hakam al-Fazari, from Ali, he said: Whenever I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah benefited me with whatever He willed of it, and when anyone else narrated to me I would not believe him unless he swore an oath, and when he swore I believed him; and Abu Bakr narrated to me, and Abu Bakr spoke the truth; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who commits a sin, then performs ablution and prays two rak'ahs, and seeks Allah's forgiveness, except that He forgives him."
"2","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Bishr b. Umar al-Zahrani narrated to us, Malik b. Anas narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Malik b. Aws b. al-Hadathan, from Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, Abu Bakr said: I am the successor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then you came, you and this one — meaning al-Abbas and Ali — you seeking your inheritance from your nephew, and this one seeking his wife's inheritance from her father; so Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited; whatever we leave is charity."
"3","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Bishr b. Umar narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Malik b. Aws b. al-Hadathan, from Umar b. al-Khattab, from Abu Bakr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited; whatever we leave is charity."
"4","Al-Harith b. Surayj Abu Umar narrated to us, Sufyan b. Uyayna narrated to us, Amr narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Malik b. Aws b. al-Hadathan, that he narrated to him, he said: Umar sent for me after the day had advanced, and gave me permission, so I entered upon him while he was on a bed of palm fiber, leaning his back on its frame, reclining on a leather pillow; he said to me: O Mal, a group of your people has arrived in haste, and I have ordered some property for them, so take it and distribute it among them; I said to him: O Commander of the Believers, I have no strength for that, so order someone else with it; he said: Take it and distribute it among them; he said: Then Yarfa came to him and said: O Commander of the Believers, do you wish to admit Uthman b. Affan, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, al-Zubayr, and Sa'd? He said: Yes, so he gave them permission and they entered; then he came to him again and said: O Commander of the Believers, do you wish to admit Ali and al-Abbas? He said: Yes; he said: So they entered, and al-Abbas was saying: O Commander of the Believers, judge between me and this one; Sufyan said: and he mentioned harsh words; the people said: O Commander of the Believers, judge between them and relieve each one of the other; Umar said to them: I adjure you by Allah, by Whose permission the heavens and the earth stand — do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited; whatever we leave is charity? They said: Yes; Umar said: Allah singled out His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with something He did not single out anyone else with, then he recited the verse: And whatever Allah restored to His Messenger from them, you did not press forward upon it with horse or camel, to the verse; Sufyan said: and I do not know whether he recited the verse after it or not; he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed among you the properties of Banu al-Nadir; by Allah, he did not keep it exclusively from you nor withhold it from you; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to take from it his and his family's maintenance for the year, and put the remainder toward horses and weapons as equipment in the path of Allah; then he said to them: I adjure you by the One by Whose permission the heaven and the earth stand — do you know that? They said: Yes; then he adjured Ali and al-Abbas with what he had adjured the people: Do you both know that? They said: Yes; he said: Then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, Abu Bakr was the successor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so you came, O Abbas, seeking your inheritance from your nephew, and Ali came seeking his wife's inheritance from her father; Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited; whatever we leave is charity; so you both considered me — while Allah knows he passed as righteous and rightly guided — withholding the truth; then when Abu Bakr passed away, I said: I am the successor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the successor of Abu Bakr; so you both considered me — while Allah knows I am truthful, righteous, rightly guided, following the truth — then you both came to me while your matter was one, and you asked me to hand it over to you; I said: If you wish I will hand it to you on condition that upon you is Allah's covenant that you will act in it as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to act in it; so you took it on that condition; he said to them: Is that so? They said: Yes; he said: Then you both came to me so I may judge between you; by Allah, I will not judge between you with other than that until the Hour rises; if you are unable, then return it to me."
"5","Musa b. Muhammad b. Hayyan narrated to us, Abd al-Samad b. Abd al-Warith informed us, Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi informed us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from his father, that Umar looked in upon Abu Bakr while he was pulling his tongue; he said: What are you doing, O successor of the Messenger of Allah? He said: This has brought me to ruinous places; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing of the body except that it complains of the sharpness of the tongue."
"6","Suwayd narrated to us, al-Walid b. Muhammad informed us, from al-Zuhri, Salim narrated to me, that he heard his father narrating that when Hafsa became widowed from Ibn Hudhafa, Umar said: I met Uthman and offered Hafsa to him; he said: I will consider my affair; I waited some nights, then he met me and said: It has occurred to me not to marry on this day of mine; Umar said: Then I met Abu Bakr and said: I will marry Hafsa to you, but he did not return anything to me, so I was angrier with him than with Uthman; I waited some nights, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to her, so I married her to him; Abu Bakr met me and said: Perhaps you were upset with me when you offered Hafsa? He said: Yes; he said: Nothing prevented me from responding to you except that I knew the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had mentioned her, so I would not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); had he left her I would have accepted her; Umar said: So I complained about Uthman to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who marries Hafsa is better than Uthman, and Uthman marries one better than Hafsa; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married him his daughter."
"7","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ya'qub b. Ibrahim informed us, my father informed us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, Salim b. Abd Allah informed us, that he heard Abd Allah b. Umar b. al-Khattab, when Hafsa daughter of Umar became widowed from Khunays b. Hudhafa al-Sahmi, and he was among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Umar said: I came to Uthman b. Affan and offered him Hafsa daughter of Umar; he said: I said: If you wish I will marry Hafsa to you; he said: I will consider my affair; I waited some nights, then he met me and said: It has occurred to me not to marry on this day of mine; Umar said: Then I met Abu Bakr al-Siddiq and said to him: If you wish I will marry Hafsa daughter of Umar to you; Abu Bakr remained silent and did not return anything to me, so I was angrier with him than with Uthman; I waited some days, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to her, so I married her to him; Abu Bakr met me and said: Perhaps you were upset with me when you offered Hafsa to me and I did not respond to you; he said: I said: Yes; he said: Nothing prevented me from responding to you regarding what you offered me except that I knew the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had mentioned her, so I would not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); had the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left her I would have accepted her."
"8","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, Salim b. Hayyan narrated to us, from Qatada, from Humayd b. Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, that Umar b. al-Khattab said: Abu Bakr stood as a preacher and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us last year and said: Nothing better than well-being after certainty has been apportioned among people; indeed truthfulness and righteousness are in Paradise; indeed lying and wickedness are in the Fire."
"9","Masruq b. al-Marzuban al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam informed us, from Abd Allah b. Bishr, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Uthman b. Affan, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, some of his Companions were confounded, and I was among those confounded; he said: Umar passed by me and greeted me but I did not return his greeting, so he complained of me to Abu Bakr; he said: So he came to us and said to me: Your brother greeted you and you did not return it to him; he said: I said: I did not know of his greeting, and I was preoccupied from it; he said: Why? I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has passed away and I did not ask him about the salvation of this matter; he said: But I did ask him; he said: So I stood to him and embraced him; he said: I said: May my father and mother be ransomed for you, you are more entitled to that; he said: I did ask him, and he said: Whoever accepts the word which I offered to my uncle, it is salvation for him."
"10","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ya'qub b. Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, a man of the Ansar, from the people of understanding, beyond accusation, narrated to me, that he heard Uthman b. Affan narrating: That some men among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, grieved for him until some of them were nearly confounded; Uthman said: And I was among them; while I was sitting in the shade of a fortress, Umar b. al-Khattab passed by me and greeted me, but I did not perceive that he passed or greeted; Umar went until he entered upon Abu Bakr and said: Shall I not tell you something astonishing? I passed by Uthman and greeted him, but he did not return the greeting to me; so Abu Bakr and Umar came — during Abu Bakr's rule — until they came and both greeted; then Abu Bakr said: Your brother Umar came to me claiming he passed by you and greeted, but you did not return the greeting; what carried you to that? I said: I did not do it; Umar said: Indeed you did, but it is your haughtiness, O Banu Umayya; Uthman said: So I said: By Allah, I did not perceive that you passed or greeted; he said: Abu Bakr said: Uthman speaks the truth; was something preoccupying you from that? He said: I said: Yes; he said: What is it? Uthman said: I said: Allah took His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before I asked him about the salvation of this matter; Abu Bakr said: I did ask him about that; Uthman said: So I said: May my father and mother be ransomed for you, you are more entitled to it; Abu Bakr said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the salvation of this matter? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever accepts from me the word which I offered to my uncle and he rejected it, it is salvation for him."
"11","Abd al-Wahid b. Ghiyath Abu Bahr narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Uthman b. al-Mughira, from Ali b. Rabi'a al-Asadi, from Asma b. al-Hakam al-Fazari, he said: Ali said: I was a man, when I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah benefited me with whatever He willed to benefit me, and when one of his Companions narrated to me I would ask him to swear; when he swore to me I believed him; and Abu Bakr narrated to me — and Abu Bakr spoke the truth — that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Any servant who commits a sin, then performs ablution and perfects it, then stands and prays, then seeks Allah's forgiveness, except that He forgives him; then he recited: And those who, when they commit immorality or wrong themselves."
"12","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' b. al-Jarrah narrated to us, Mis'ar and Sufyan narrated to us, from Uthman b. al-Mughira al-Thaqafi, from Ali b. Rabi'a al-Walibi, from Asma b. al-Hakam al-Fazari, from Ali, he said: Whenever I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah benefited me with whatever He willed of it, and when another narrated to me from him I would ask him to swear; when he swore to me I believed him; and Abu Bakr narrated to me, and Abu Bakr spoke the truth, that he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one who commits a sin, then performs ablution and perfects it — Mis'ar said: then prays; Sufyan said: prays two rak'ahs — then seeks forgiveness, except that He forgives him."
"13","Ubayd Allah b. Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Uthman b. al-Mughira al-Thaqafi, he said: I heard Ali b. Rabi'a, from a man of Banu Fazara called Asma, from Ali b. Abi Talib, he said: Whenever I heard something from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah benefited me with whatever He willed to benefit me of it; Abu Bakr narrated to me — and Abu Bakr spoke the truth — from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no servant — Shu'ba said: I think he said: Muslim — who commits a sin, then performs ablution, then prays two rak'ahs, then seeks Allah's forgiveness for that sin, except that He forgives him; Shu'ba said: And he recited one of these two verses: Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it; And those who, when they commit immorality or wrong themselves."
"14","Abu Khaythama narrated it to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Uthman b. al-Mughira, he said: I heard Ali b. Rabi'a — a man of Banu Asad — narrating from Asma — or Ibn Asma — of Banu Fazara, from Ali, he said: Whenever I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah benefited me with whatever He willed to benefit me of it; and Abu Bakr narrated to me — and Abu Bakr spoke the truth — that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned something similar."
"15","Ubayd Allah b. Umar al-Jushami narrated to us, Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan b. Sa'id al-Thawri narrated to us, Uthman b. al-Mughira al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: And Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Uthman b. al-Mughira, from Ali b. Rabi'a, from Asma b. al-Hakam al-Fazari, from Ali, he said: Whenever I was narrated a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I would ask its narrator to swear; when he swore to me I believed him; Abu Bakr narrated to me — and Abu Bakr spoke the truth — that he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who commits a sin, then performs ablution, prays two rak'ahs, and seeks Allah's forgiveness, except that He forgives him."
"16","Abu Kurayb Muhammad b. al-Ala narrated to us, Husayn b. Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'ida, Asim b. Abi al-Najud narrated to us, from Zirr, from Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed between Abu Bakr and Umar while Abd Allah was praying; he had begun Surat al-Nisa and dwelt long in it; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it with the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd; then he asked, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying: Ask, you will be given; ask, you will be given; among what he asked he said: O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not apostatize, bliss that does not end, and companionship of our Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the highest Garden of Eternity; Umar came to Abd Allah to give him glad tidings, but found Abu Bakr coming out having preceded him; he said: If you did, you are indeed foremost in good."
"17","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya b. Adam narrated to us, from Abu Bakr b. Ayyash, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abd Allah, he said: I was in the mosque praying; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered with Abu Bakr and Umar; I had begun Surat al-Nisa and recited it; when I finished I sat and began praising Allah and sending blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I supplicated for myself; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask, you will be given; then he said: Whoever wishes to recite the Qur'an fresh, let him recite it as Ibn Umm Abd recites it; he said: I returned to my house, and Abu Bakr came to me and said: Do you remember any of what you were supplicating? I said: Yes: O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not apostatize, bliss that does not end, and companionship of our Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the highest Garden of Eternity; then Umar came to Abd Allah to give him glad tidings, but found Abu Bakr coming out having preceded him; he said: If you did, you are indeed foremost in good."
"18","Surayj b. Yunus narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab b. Ata narrated to us, from Ziyad b. Abi Ziyad al-Jassas, from Ali b. Zayd, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn Umar said to his servant: Do not pass by me near Ibn al-Zubayr; the servant was heedless and passed by him; he raised his head and saw him and said: May Allah have mercy on you, I knew you only as fasting, praying, joining kinship; by Allah, I hope, along with the evils you did of sins, that He will not punish you; Mujahid said: Then he turned to me and said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it in this world."
"19","Al-Hasan b. Shabib narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Kawthar b. Hakim narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the salvation of this matter we are in? He said: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah alone, without partner, it is salvation for him."
"20","Abu Sa'id al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, Sufyan b. Husayn narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim b. Abd Allah b. Umar, from Ibn Umar, he said: When Hafsa became widowed, and she had been under Khunays b. Hudhafa, Umar came to Abu Bakr and offered her to him, but he was silent; then he came to Uthman and offered her to him, but Uthman said: I have no need of women; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to her and she was married to him; he met Abu Bakr and said: I had offered Hafsa to you and you were silent, so I was angrier with you than with Uthman, who rejected me; Abu Bakr said: There had been mention of her affair, but it was secret, so I disliked disclosing the secret."
"21","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Rawh b. Ubada narrated to us, Musa b. Ubayda narrated to us, the freedman of Ibn Siba' narrated to me, he said: I heard Abd Allah b. Umar narrating from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when this verse was revealed: Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it and will not find besides Allah any protector or helper; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Bakr, shall I recite to you a verse revealed to me? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah; he said: So he recited it to me; he said: I know only that I felt a break in my back, until I stretched for it in my back; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for you, O Abu Bakr, and your fellow believers, you will be recompensed for that in this world until you meet Allah with no sins upon you; as for the others, it will be gathered for them until they are recompensed for it on the Day of Resurrection."
"22","Ja'far b. Mihran al-Sabbak narrated to us, Abd al-A'la b. Abd al-A'la al-Sami narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, he said: Husayn b. Abd Allah narrated to me, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When they wanted to dig a grave for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah used to dig graves for the people of Mecca, while Abu Talha Zayd b. Sahl was the one who dug for the people of Medina, and he made a niche grave — al-Abbas called two men and said to one: Go to Abu Ubayda, and to the other: Go to Abu Talha; O Allah, choose for Your Messenger; the companion of Abu Talha found Abu Talha and brought him, so he made a niche grave for the Messenger of Allah; when they finished preparing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Tuesday, he was placed upon his bed; the Muslims had differed about his burial: one said: We bury him in his mosque; another said: Rather he is buried with his companions; Abu Bakr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No prophet was taken except that he is buried where he was taken; so the bed of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which he passed away was lifted, and a grave was dug for him beneath it; then the people were called to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pray over him in groups: the men, until when they finished, the women were admitted, until when the women finished, the children were admitted; and no one led the people in prayer over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was buried in the middle of the night, the night of Wednesday."
"23","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ya'qub b. Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, he said: Husayn b. Abd Allah narrated to me, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Bakr, he said: I heard him saying: No prophet was taken except that he is buried where he is taken."
"24","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Jarrah b. Makhlad al-Basri Abu Abd Allah narrated to us, Musa b. Dawud narrated to us, Husam b. Missak narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate meat from a shoulder, then prayed without performing ablution."
"25","Muhammad b. Musa al-Tusi narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd al-Salam b. Harb narrated to us, from Ata b. al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When: Perish the hands of Abu Lahab was revealed, the wife of Abu Lahab came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Abu Bakr was with him; when Abu Bakr saw her he said: O Messenger of Allah, she is a foul-tongued woman, and I fear she may harm you, so should you stand? He said: She will not see me; she came and said: O Abu Bakr, your companion has lampooned me; he said: He does not compose poetry; she said: You are truthful in my view; and she left; I said: O Messenger of Allah, she did not see you! He said: An angel kept shielding me from her with his wing."
"26","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya b. Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Sulayman al-A'mash, from Isma'il b. Raja, from Umayr the freedman of al-Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away and Abu Bakr succeeded him, al-Abbas disputed with Ali over things the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left to Abu Bakr; Abu Bakr said: Something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left and did not move — I will not move it."
"27","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Musa b. Abi A'isha, from Ubayd Allah b. Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas and A'isha: That Abu Bakr kissed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was dead."
"28","Wahb b. Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid — meaning Ibn Abd Allah — narrated to us, from Khalid — meaning al-Hadhdha — from Yusuf Abu Ya'qub, from Muhammad b. Hatib, or al-Harith, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr was mentioned, so he said: How long he coveted leadership; I said: What is that? He said: A thief was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered his killing; it was said: He stole; he said: Cut him; then he was brought after that to Abu Bakr having stolen, while his limbs had been cut; Abu Bakr said: I find nothing for you except what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed for you on the day he ordered your killing, for he knew you best; so he ordered his killing by young lads among the sons of the Emigrants, I among them; Ibn al-Zubayr said: Put me in command over you; so we put him in command over us, and we took him to al-Baqi' and killed him."
"29","Ghassan b. al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Layth b. Sa'd, from Yazid b. Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abd Allah b. Amr b. al-As, from Abu Bakr. [The report breaks off here; the supplication follows in the next reports.]"
"30","And Zuhayr b. Harb narrated to us, Hashim b. al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Layth b. Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Yazid b. Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abd Allah b. Amr, from Abu Bakr, he said: [The report breaks off here; the supplication follows in the next report.]"
"31","And Ubayd Allah b. Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hisham b. Abd al-Malik and Asim b. Ali narrated to us, they said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abd Allah b. Amr, from Abu Bakr — and the wording is that of Ghassan's hadith — that he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Teach me a supplication to supplicate with in my prayer; he said: O Allah, I have wronged myself much wrongdoing — and in al-Qawariri's hadith alone, from Asim: great — and none forgives sins but You, so forgive me with forgiveness from You, and have mercy on me; indeed You are the Most Forgiving, the Most Merciful. Abu Ya'la said: al-Layth said: from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, while Amr b. al-Harith said: from Abd Allah b. Amr, and did not go beyond him."
"32","Harun b. Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Wahb narrated to us, Amr b. al-Harith informed me, from Yazid b. Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, that he heard Abd Allah b. Amr b. al-As saying: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, teach me a supplication to supplicate with in my prayer and in my house; he said: Say: O Allah, I have wronged myself much wrongdoing, and none forgives sins but You, so forgive me with forgiveness from You, and have mercy on me; indeed You are the Most Forgiving, the Most Merciful."
"33","Abu Musa Muhammad b. al-Muthanna and Ahmad b. Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, they said: Rawh narrated to us, Sa'id b. Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from al-Mughira b. Subay', from Amr b. Hurayth, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq — and in Abu Musa's hadith, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us: That the Dajjal will emerge from a land toward the east called Khurasan; peoples will follow him as though their faces are hammered shields."
"34","Abu Musa Harun b. Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, al-Fazari — meaning Abu Ishaq — narrated to me, from Abd Allah b. Shawdhab. And al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ghaniyya, the son-in-law of Abu Ishaq, narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Abd Allah b. Shawdhab, from Abu al-Tayyah, from al-Mughira b. Subay', from Amr b. Hurayth, from Abu Bakr, he said: [The report breaks off here; its completion is in the next report.]"
"35","And al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Muhammad b. Kathir narrated to us, from Ibn Shawdhab, from Abu al-Tayyah, from al-Mughira b. Subay', from Amr b. Hurayth, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, that he fell ill, and when he recovered he said: O people, I have not spared you advice; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Dajjal will emerge from a land in the east called Khurasan; a people will follow him as though their faces are shields. And the wording is that of Ibn Kathir's hadith; Harun did not complete it as al-Dawraqi completed it."
"36","Abu Bakr b. Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muhammad b. Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Walid b. Jumay', from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: Fatima sent to Abu Bakr and said: What is with you, O successor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Did you inherit the Messenger of Allah, or his family? He said: No, rather his family; she said: Then what of the share of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard him saying: When Allah feeds a prophet some food then takes him to Himself, He makes it for the one who stands after him; so I considered — I after him — returning it to the Muslims; she said: You and what you heard from the Messenger of Allah."
"37","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, from Umar b. Sa'id b. Abi Husayn, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Uqba b. al-Harith, he said: I went out with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq from the Asr prayer, nights after the passing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with Ali walking beside him; he passed by al-Hasan b. Ali playing with the boys, so Abu Bakr carried him on his shoulder and said: May my father be ransomed for one resembling the Prophet, not resembling Ali! And Ali was laughing."
"38","Zuhayr b. Harb narrated to us, Qabisa narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Umar b. Sa'id b. Abi Husayn, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Uqba b. al-Harith, he said: I saw Abu Bakr carrying al-Hasan b. Ali and saying: May my father be ransomed for one resembling the Prophet, not resembling Ali, with Ali beside him smiling."
"39","Abbad b. Musa al-Khuttali narrated to us, Isma'il b. Ja'far narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Jabir, from Amir, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abza, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Ma'iz b. Malik came and confessed adultery, so he turned him away; then he returned a second time and he turned him away; then he returned a third time and he turned him away; I said: If you return a fourth time he will stone you; so he returned a fourth time; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his detention, then he sent and asked about him; they said: We know only good; so he ordered his stoning."
"40","Musa b. Hayyan narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Kufi al-Zubayri narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amir, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abza, from Abu Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned Ma'iz b. Malik away four times."
"41","Ubayd Allah b. Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us, Abd Allah b. al-Mubarak narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from al-Miswar b. Makhrama and Marwan b. al-Hakam, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out at the time of al-Hudaybiyya with some ten-odd hundred of his Companions, until when they were at Dhu al-Hulayfa the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) garlanded the sacrificial animals, marked them, and entered ihram for Umra; then Urwa b. Mas'ud al-Thaqafi came and said: I see faces likely to flee and leave you; Abu Bakr said: Suck the clitoris of al-Lat! Would we flee and leave him?"
"42","Zuhayr b. Harb narrated to us, Ya'qub b. Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, Urwa b. al-Zubayr informed me that A'isha, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that Fatima daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Abu Bakr after the passing of the Messenger of Allah to apportion to her her inheritance from what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left, of what Allah had restored to him; Abu Bakr said to her: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited; whatever we leave is charity."
"43","Muhammad b. Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami and Musa b. Muhammad b. Hayyan narrated to us, they said: Ibn Abi al-Wazir narrated to us, Zanfal al-Arafi — residing at Arafa — narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Abi Mulayka narrated to us, from A'isha, from Abu Bakr — and in Musa b. Hayyan's hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he intended a matter, would say: O Allah, choose for me and select for me."
"44","Abu Musa al-Harawi Ishaq b. Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from A'isha, she said: They differed about the burial of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he passed away; Abu Bakr said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A prophet is taken only in the most beloved place to him; he said: Bury him where he was taken."
"45","Musa b. Hayyan narrated to us, Ubayd Allah b. Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi narrated to us, Musa b. Mutayr narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from A'isha, she said: Abu Bakr narrated to me, he said: A man of the polytheists came until he faced the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his private part urinating; I said: O Messenger of Allah, does the man not see us? He said: Had he seen us he would not have faced us with his private part — meaning while they were in the cave."
"46","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad b. al-Hasan b. Abi al-Hasan al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us, from Abd al-Hakim b. Abd Allah b. Abi Farwa, from Ya'qub b. Utba, from Urwa b. al-Zubayr, from A'isha, that when Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr passed away he was wept over; Abu Bakr went out to the men and said: I apologize to you for these women; they are fresh from the Jahiliyya; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The dead is scorched with boiling water by the weeping of the living."
"47","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Marhum b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Yazid b. Babanus, from A'isha, that Abu Bakr entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after his passing, placed his mouth between his eyes, placed his hands on his temples, and said: O my Prophet! O my close friend! O my chosen one!"
"48","Kamil b. Talha narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Urwa, from A'isha, or Asma, that Abu Bakr stood in the place of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the coming year after the year in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, and said: I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the summer of last year, in a place like this station of mine — then his eyes overflowed — then he said: I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the summer of last year, in a place like my station — then his eyes overflowed — then he said: I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the summer of last year, in a place like this station of mine — then his eyes overflowed — then he said: I heard your Prophet, peace be upon him, in a place like this station of mine, saying: Ask Allah for pardon, well-being, and full protection in this world and the Hereafter."
"49","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Urwa, from A'isha, that Abu Bakr entered upon her while two slave girls were beating two tambourines; Abu Bakr scolded them, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Leave them, for every people has a festival."
"50","Abu Bakr b. Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muhammad b. Umar al-Aslami narrated to us, al-Dahhak b. Uthman narrated to us, from Habib, the freedman of Urwa, he said: I heard Asma daughter of Abu Bakr saying: I saw my father praying in a single garment; I said: O father! You pray in a single garment while your clothes are laid out? He said: O my daughter, the last prayer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed behind me was in a single garment."
"51","Abu Musa Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Harawi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Walid b. Kathir, from Ibn Tadrus, the freedman of Hakim b. Hizam, from Asma daughter of Abu Bakr, that they said to her: What is the worst you saw the polytheists do to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: The polytheists sat in the mosque discussing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and what he said about their gods; while they were so, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and they rose against him all together; a cry went to Abu Bakr: Reach your companion; he came out from us with four braids of hair, saying: Woe to you! Would you kill a man for saying: My Lord is Allah, when he has come to you with clear proofs from your Lord; they turned from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and set upon Abu Bakr; she said: Abu Bakr returned to us, and he would not touch anything of his braids except that it came away with it, while he was saying: Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor."
"52","Abu Musa narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Walid, from Ibn Tadrus, from Asma, she said: When: Perish the hands of Abu Lahab was revealed, the one-eyed Umm Jamil came, wailing, with a stone in her hand, saying: We refuse the blameworthy — or: we came to him, Abu Musa doubted — his religion we hate, his command we disobey; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with Abu Bakr beside him — or he said: with him; he said: Abu Bakr said: She has come and I fear she will see you; he said: She will not see me; and he recited Qur'an seeking protection with it: And when you recite the Qur'an, We place between you and those who do not believe in the Hereafter a hidden barrier; he said: She came until she stood over Abu Bakr, not seeing the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O Abu Bakr, it reached me that your companion lampooned me; Abu Bakr said: No, by the Lord of this House, he did not lampoon you; she left saying: Quraysh knows I am the daughter of its chief."
"53","Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, from Malik b. Anas, from Abd al-Rahman b. al-Qasim, from his father, from Asma daughter of Umays, that she gave birth at Dhu al-Hulayfa; Abu Bakr asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Order her to bathe and enter ihram."
"54","Ubayd Allah b. Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, al-Kalbi narrated to us, from Salama b. al-Sa'ib, from Abu Rafi', he said: I went out with two anklets to sell them, while our family needed maintenance; I saw Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, and he said: Where are you going? He said: I said: Our family needed maintenance, so I wanted to sell these two anklets; he said: And I went out with small dirhams wanting silver better than it; he said: He placed the two anklets in one scale and the dirhams in the other, and the two anklets outweighed the dirhams somewhat; he called for shears; he said: I said: Glory be to Allah, it is yours, it is yours; he said: If you leave it, Allah will not leave it; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Gold for gold, like for like, and silver for silver, like for like; the one who gives excess and the one who takes excess are in the Fire."
"55","Abu Musa Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Harawi narrated to us, al-Nadr b. Shumayl narrated to us, Abu Na'ama narrated to us, al-Bara b. Nawfal narrated to us, from Walan al-Adawi, from Hudhayfa, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose one morning, prayed the dawn prayer, then sat until forenoon came, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed; then he sat in his place until he prayed the first, Asr, Maghrib — all without speaking — until he prayed the last Isha; then he stood to his family; the people said to Abu Bakr: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what is with him; today he did something he never did; he said: Yes; there was displayed to me what will be of the affair of this world and the Hereafter; the first and the last were gathered on one plain; the people were horrified by that and went to Adam, sweat almost bridling them, and said: O Adam, you are the father of mankind and Allah chose you; intercede for us with your Lord; he said: I met the like of what you met; go to your father after your father, to Nuh; Allah chose Nuh and the family of Ibrahim and the family of Imran above the worlds; he said: So they go to Nuh and say: Intercede for us with your Lord; Allah chose you and answered you in your supplication, so no dweller of the disbelievers remained on earth; he says: That is not with me; go to Musa, for Allah spoke to him directly; Musa says: That is not with me, but go to Isa, for he would heal the blind and the leper and revive the dead; Isa says: That is not with me, but go to the chief of Adam's children, for he is the first over whom the earth will split on the Day of Resurrection; go to Muhammad to intercede for you; so they come to me and I go with them. He said: So he sets out, and Jibril is called; he said: Jibril comes to his Lord, and Allah says: Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise; he said: Jibril sets out with him, and he falls prostrate for the duration of a Jumu'a; then Allah says: O Muhammad, raise your head, speak and you will be heard, intercede and your intercession will be granted; he said: He raises his head, and when he looks at his Lord he falls prostrate for another Jumu'a duration; Allah says: O Muhammad, raise your head, speak and you will be heard, intercede and your intercession will be granted; he said: And he falls prostrate; he said: Jibril takes him by his upper arms; he said: Allah opens upon him supplication He never opened upon any human ever; he said: He says: O Lord, You made me chief of Adam's children, without pride, and the first over whom the earth splits on the Day of Resurrection, without pride, until there comes to my Hawd more than between Sana'a and Ayla; he said: Then it is said: Call the truthful, and they intercede; he said: Then it is said: Call the prophets; he said: A prophet comes, peace be upon him, with a group, a prophet with five and six, a prophet with none; he said: Then it is said: Call the martyrs; he said: They intercede for whomever they wish; he said: When the martyrs finish, he said: The Blessed and Exalted says: I am the Most Merciful of the merciful; admit to My Paradise whoever did not associate anything with Me; he said: They enter Paradise; then Allah says: Look at the Fire, is there anyone who ever did any good? He said: They find in the Fire a man, and it is said to him: Did you ever do any good? He says: No, except that I was lenient in selling; Allah says: Be lenient to My servant for his leniency to My servants; then he is brought out of the Fire; he said: And another man, and Allah says: Did you ever do any good? He says: No, except that I ordered my children when I die: burn me, then grind me, until when I become like kohl, take me to the sea and scatter me in the wind; he said: Allah says: Why did you do that? He says: From fear of You; he says: Look at the dominion of the greatest king, for you have its like and ten likes of it; he says: Do You mock me while You are the King? And that is what I laughed at in the forenoon."
"56","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibrahim Abu Ishaq al-Bunani narrated to us, al-Nadr b. Shumayl narrated to us, Abu Na'ama narrated to us, Abu Hunayda al-Bara b. Nawfal narrated to us, from Walan al-Adawi, from Hudhayfa b. al-Yaman, from Abu Bakr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose one morning, then he mentioned a hadith like this hadith or close to it."
"57","Ishaq b. Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham b. Yusuf narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, about His saying: Or have they made for Allah partners who created as He created; Layth b. Abi Sulaym informed me, from Abu Muhammad, from Hudhayfa, from Abu Bakr — whether Hudhayfa attended that from the Prophet, peace be upon him, or Abu Bakr informed him — that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Association in you is more hidden than the crawling of ants; he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, is association anything but what is worshipped besides Allah — or: invoked with Allah, Abd al-Malik doubted; he said: May your mother be bereaved of you, O Siddiq! Association in you is more hidden than the crawling of ants; shall I not inform you of a statement that removes its small and great — or: its lesser and greater? He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah; he said: You say three times each day: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from associating with You while I know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what I do not know; and association is to say: Allah and so-and-so gave me; and the equal is for a person to say: Were it not for so-and-so, so-and-so would have killed me."
"58","Amr b. al-Husayn narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz b. Muslim narrated to us, from Layth b. Abi Sulaym, from Abu Muhammad, from Ma'qil b. Yasar. Abu Bakr narrated to me from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: [The report breaks off here; its completion is in the next reports.]"
"59","And Musa b. Muhammad b. Hayyan narrated to us, Rawh b. Aslam and Fahd narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Aziz b. Muslim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Abu Muhammad, from Ma'qil b. Yasar, he said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with Abu Bakr — or he said: Abu Bakr narrated to me from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — that he said: Association is more hidden among you than the crawling of ants; then he said: Shall I not guide you to what removes its small and great from you? Say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from associating with You while I know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what I do not know."
"60","Musa b. Muhammad b. Hayyan narrated to us, Rawh b. Aslam and Fahd narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Aziz b. Muslim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Abu Muhammad, from Ma'qil b. Yasar, he said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with Abu Bakr — or he said: Abu Bakr narrated to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — that he said: Association is more hidden among you than the crawling of ants; Abu Bakr said: Is association anything but invoking another god with Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Association is more hidden among you than the crawling of ants; then he said: Shall I not guide you to what removes its small and great from you? Say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from associating with You while I know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what I do not know."
"61","Surayj narrated to us, Marwan b. Mu'awiya narrated to us, Ja'far b. al-Zubayr narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umama, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the cave, and he said: O Allah, stabbing and plague; I said: O Messenger of Allah, I know you asked for the deaths of your nation; this stabbing we know, but what is the plague? He said: An inflammation like boils; if your life is prolonged you will see it."
"62","Ishaq b. Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Ibrahim b. Sa'd narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Ubayd b. al-Sabbaq, from Zayd b. Thabit, he said: Abu Bakr sent to me after the battle of al-Yamama, so I came and Umar was with him; he mentioned something like al-Umari's hadith, adding after Zayd b. Thabit's saying: So I joined it; he said: Ibn Shihab said: They differed that day over al-Tabut; Zayd said: al-Tabuh, while the Qurashi group said: al-Tabut; they raised their dispute to Uthman, who said: Write it al-Tabut, in the tongue of Quraysh; Ibn Shihab said: Ibn Mas'ud had disliked that Zayd was put in charge of copying the codices; Ibn Shihab said: Ubayd Allah b. Abd Allah narrated to me that Abd Allah said: O assembly of Muslims, am I removed from Allah's Book while a man is put in charge of it — by Allah, I submitted while he was in the loins of a disbelieving man — meaning Zayd b. Thabit; he said: Therefore Abd Allah said: O people of Iraq — or: O people of Kufa — conceal the codices you have and hide them, for Allah says: And whoever conceals will bring what he concealed on the Day of Resurrection; Ibn Shihab said: It reached me that men among the best of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked this statement of his."
"63","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, Ibrahim b. Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd b. al-Sabbaq, that Zayd narrated to him, he said: Abu Bakr sent after the battle of al-Yamama, and Umar b. al-Khattab was with him; he said: Umar came to me and said: Killing has fallen heavily upon the reciters of the Qur'an on the day of al-Yamama, and I fear killing will fall heavily upon the reciters in all lands, so much Qur'an will go; I think you should order its collection; Abu Bakr said: I said to Umar: How do I do something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do? Umar said: By Allah, it is good; Umar b. al-Khattab kept urging me until Allah opened my chest to what He opened Umar's chest to, and I saw in it what he saw; Zayd said: Abu Bakr said: You are a young, intelligent man, we do not accuse you; you used to write revelation for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so trace the Qur'an and collect it; he said: By Allah, had they charged me with moving a mountain of mountains it would not have been heavier upon me than that; he said: I said: How do you do something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do? Abu Bakr said: By Allah, it is good; he kept urging me, Abu Bakr and Umar, until Allah opened my chest to what He opened the chests of Abu Bakr and Umar to; so I traced the Qur'an collecting it from scraps, palm stalks, stones, thin skins, and men's chests, until I found at the end of Surat al-Tawba (Bara'a) with Khuzayma b. Thabit: There has come to you a Messenger from yourselves, to the end of the verse."
"64","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ya'qub b. Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd b. al-Sabbaq, that Zayd b. Thabit narrated to him: That Abu Bakr said: You are a young, intelligent man, we do not accuse you; you used to write revelation for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so trace the Qur'an and collect it."
"65","Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Affan b. Muslim narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that Abu Bakr narrated to him, he said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were in the cave: If one of them looked beneath his feet he would see us beneath his feet; he said: So he said: O Abu Bakr, what do you think of two, Allah being their third?"
"66","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Habban b. Hilal narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Thabit, Anas narrated to us, that Abu Bakr narrated to him, he said: I looked at the feet of the polytheists above our heads while we were in the cave, and said: O Messenger of Allah, if one of them looked at his feet he would see us beneath his feet; he said: O Abu Bakr, what do you think of two, Allah being their third?"
"67","Muhammad b. Isma'il b. Abi Samina al-Basri and Muhammad b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, they said: Amr b. Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, Imran narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, he said: Umar said to Abu Bakr regarding apostasy: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not say: I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they say it they protect from me their blood and property except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah? Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — and in Ibn Abi Samina's hadith: Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah, establish prayer, and give zakah; by Allah, if they withheld from me a hobble I would fight them for it until my soul joins Allah; Umar said: When I saw Abu Bakr resolved upon that I knew it was the truth."
"68","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Amr b. Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, Sulayman b. al-Mughira narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: Abu Bakr said after the passing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Umar: Let us go to Umm Ayman to visit her as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit her; when we reached her she wept; we said to her: What makes you weep? What is with Allah is better for His Messenger; she said: I do not weep from not knowing that what is with Allah is better for His Messenger, but I weep that revelation has ceased from heaven; he said: So she moved them to weeping, and they wept with her."
"69","Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Za'ida b. Abi al-Ruqad narrated to us, Ziyad al-Numayri narrated to me, from Anas, that Abu Bakr entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was gloomy; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why do I see you gloomy? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I was with a cousin of mine last night, so-and-so, wrestling with his soul; he said: Did you not prompt him with: There is no god but Allah? He said: I did, O Messenger of Allah; he said: Did he say it? He said: Yes; he said: Paradise became due for him; Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, how is it for the living? He said: It demolishes their sins; it demolishes their sins."
"70","Ubayd Allah b. Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Uthman b. Umar narrated to us, Yunus b. Yazid narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Ibn al-Sabbaq informed me, Zayd b. Thabit informed me, that Abu Bakr sent to him after the battle of Yamama; he said: I came to him and Umar was with him; Abu Bakr said: Umar came to me and said: Killing has fallen heavily upon the reciters of the Qur'an at Yamama — or: the people, Abu Ya'la doubted — and I fear killing will fall heavily in all lands, so much of the Qur'an will go unpreserved; I think you should order the Qur'an collected; I said to Umar: How do I do something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do? Umar said: By Allah, it is good; he kept urging me about that until Allah opened my chest, and I saw in it what Umar saw; Zayd said — with Umar sitting with him silent — Abu Bakr said: You are a young, intelligent man, we do not accuse you; you used to write revelation for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so follow the Qur'an and collect it; Zayd said: By Allah, had they charged me with moving a mountain of mountains it would not have been heavier upon me than what he ordered me of collecting the Qur'an; I said: How do you do something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do? He said: By Allah, it is good; he kept urging me until Allah opened my chest with what He opened the chests of Abu Bakr and Umar with; so I collected the Qur'an tracing it from scraps, shoulder blades, men's chests, until I found the end of Surat al-Tawba with Khuzayma al-Ansari, not finding it with anyone else: There has come to you a Messenger from yourselves, to the end of the verse; the codices in which we collected the Qur'an remained with Abu Bakr his life until Allah took him, then with Umar until Allah took him, then with Hafsa."
"71","Al-Abbas b. al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Umar b. Ali narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Ziyad b. An'um narrated to us, he said: I heard Malik b. Qays narrating, he said: Uqba b. Amir came to Mu'awiya while he was at Iliya, and soon went out; he was sought but not found — or he said: We sought him but did not find him — so we followed him, and there he was praying in an open land; he said: So he said: What brought you? They said: We came to renew our bond with you, or fulfill your right; he said: Then your prize is with me: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and each man of us tended the camels one day; it was my day to graze; he said: I brought back the camels at evening and reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his Companions around him, narrating; he said: I neglected the camels and turned toward him, reaching him while he was saying: Whoever performs ablution and perfects it, then prays two rak'ahs intending by them Allah's face, Allah forgives him what preceded them; I said: Allah is Greatest; he said: A man struck my shoulder; I turned, and there was Abu Bakr; he said: O Ibn Amir, what was before it is better; I said: What was before it? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah, his heart confirming his tongue, will enter through whichever gate of Paradise he wishes."
"72","Amr b. Malik narrated to us, Jariya b. Harim al-Fuqaymi narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah b. Darim narrated to me, Abd Allah b. Busr al-Hubrani narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Kabsha al-Anmari — who had companionship — narrating from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, or rejects anything I commanded, let him take a house in Hell."
"73","Ahmad b. Umar al-Waki'i narrated to us, Husayn b. Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'ida, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: Abu Bakr stood upon the pulpit and said: You know what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with last year; then he wept, then he repeated it, then he wept, then he repeated it, then he wept; he said: People were not given in this world anything better than pardon and well-being, so ask Allah for them."
"74","Ishaq b. Isma'il al-Talqani narrated to us, Husayn b. Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'ida, from Asim b. Abi al-Najud, from Abu Salih, he said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq stood upon the pulpit, preached, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us last year upon this pulpit, on a day like this, in a month like this; he said: Then he wept and said: Ask Allah for pardon and well-being."
"75","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd b. Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, from Abu Hurayra, that Abu Bakr was sent in the Hajj which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put him in charge of before the Farewell Hajj, on the Day of Sacrifice, among a group, announcing among people that no polytheist shall perform Hajj after this year, and no naked person shall circumambulate the House."
"76","Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Ya'la b. Ata, from Amr b. Asim, from Abu Hurayra, that Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me words to say when I wake and when I sleep; he said: Say: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Lord of everything and its Sovereign, there is no god but You; I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul and the evil of Satan and his association; say it when you wake, when you sleep, and when you lie on your bed."
"77","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, Yahya b. Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: Abu Bakr narrated to me, he said: I missed Isha one night and came to my family and said: Do you have supper? They said: No, by Allah, we have no supper; I lay on my bed but sleep did not come from hunger; I said: If I went out to the mosque, prayed, and distracted myself until morning; I went out to the mosque, prayed what Allah willed, then leaned against a corner of the mosque; then Umar b. al-Khattab appeared to me and said: Who is this? I said: Abu Bakr; he said: What brought you out at this hour? I told him the story; he said: By Allah, nothing brought me out but what brought you out; he sat beside me; while we were so, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and did not recognize us; he said: Who is this? Umar hastened to me and said: This is Abu Bakr, and Umar; he said: What brought you both out at this hour? Umar said: I went out, entered the mosque, saw the shape of Abu Bakr, and said: Who is this? He said: Abu Bakr; I said: What brought you out at this hour? He mentioned what happened; I said: And I, by Allah, nothing brought me out but what brought him out; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I, by Allah, nothing brought me out but what brought you both out; come with us to al-Waqifi Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayyihan; perhaps we find with him something to feed us. So we went walking until we reached the garden wall in the moonlight; we knocked; the woman said: Who is this? Umar said: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar; she opened for us and we entered; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where is your husband? She said: He went to fetch us sweet water from the well of Banu Haritha; he will come to you now; he said: He came carrying a waterskin until he brought it to a palm and hung it on a stalk of its stalks, then turned to us and said: Welcome and greetings; no one ever visited people like who visited me; then he cut a cluster for us and brought it, and we picked from it in the moonlight and ate; then he took the knife and roamed among the sheep; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Beware the milking ewe — or: beware those with milk — so he took a sheep, slaughtered and skinned it, told his wife, and she cooked and baked; he cut meat into the pot and lit beneath it until the meat and bread were done; he crumbled bread, ladled broth and meat over it, brought it and placed it before us; we ate until full; then he went to the waterskin, which the wind had cooled, so it was cold; he poured into a vessel and handed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who drank, then handed Abu Bakr, who drank, then handed Umar, who drank; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Praise be to Allah; we went out brought out only by hunger, then returned having attained this; you will be asked about this on the Day of Resurrection; this is of bliss; then he said to al-Waqifi: Have you no servant to draw water for you? He said: No, O Messenger of Allah; he said: When captives come to us, come to us so we may order a servant for you; soon captives came to him, and al-Waqifi came to him; he said: What brought you? He said: O Messenger of Allah, your promise you promised me; he said: These are captives, so stand and choose among them; he said: Be you the one to choose for me; he said: Take this boy and treat him well; he said: He took him to his wife; she said: What is this? He told her the story; she said: What did you say to him? He said: I said to him: Be you the one to choose for me; she said: You did well; he told you: Treat him well; she said: Treat him well; he said: What is treating him well? She said: To free him; he said: Then he is free for Allah's face."
"78","Umayya b. Bistam narrated to us, Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us, Yunus — meaning Ibn Ubayd — narrated to us, from Humayd b. Hilal, from Abd Allah b. Mutarrif, from Abu Barza, he said: While Abu Bakr was in his work he became angry at a Muslim man, his anger intensifying greatly; when I saw that I said: O successor of the Messenger of Allah, shall I strike his neck? When I mentioned killing he turned from that whole discussion to other talk; when we dispersed Abu Bakr sent for me after that and said: O Abu Barza, what did you say? He said: And I had forgotten what I said; he said: I said: What did I say? Remind me; he said: Do you not remember what you said? I said: No, by Allah; he said: Consider when you saw me angry at the man and you said: Shall I strike his neck, O successor of the Messenger of Allah; do you remember that? Would you have done it? He said: Yes, by Allah, and now if you order me I will do it; he said: Woe to you — or: woe unto you — by Allah, it belongs to none after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"79","Hashim b. al-Harith narrated to us, Ubayd Allah b. Amr narrated to us, from Zayd b. Abi Unaysa, from Amr b. Murra, from Abu Nasr, from Abu Barza al-Aslami, he said: Abu Bakr became angry at a man with anger more severe than ever seen that day; Abu Barza said to him: O successor of the Messenger of Allah, order me to strike his neck; he said: It was as though a fire was extinguished; he said: Abu Barza left, then he sent for him and said: May your mother be bereaved of you, what did you say? He said: I said: By Allah, if you ordered me to kill him I would kill him; he said: May your mother be bereaved of you, O Abu Barza, it belonged to none after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"80","Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Mu'adh b. Mu'adh narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Tawba al-Anbari, from Abd Allah b. Qudama, from Abu Barza al-Aslami, he said: A man spoke harshly to Abu Bakr; he said: I nearly killed him; he said: Abu Bakr scolded me and said: It belongs to none but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"81","Zuhayr b. Harb narrated to us, Uthman b. Umar narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, Tawba al-Anbari informed me, he said: I heard Abu al-Sawwar Abd Allah narrating from Abu Barza, that a man reviled Abu Bakr; he said: I said: Shall I not strike his neck, O successor of the Messenger of Allah? He said: No; it belongs to none after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"82","Yahya b. Ma'in narrated to us, Abu Ubayda al-Haddad narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahid b. Zayd, from Farqad al-Sabakhi, from Murra al-Tayyib, from Zayd b. Arqam, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No body nourished on unlawful shall enter Paradise."
"83","Musa b. Muhammad b. Hayyan narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid b. Zayd narrated to us, from Aslam, from Murra, from Zayd b. Arqam, he said: I heard Abu Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No body nourished on unlawful shall enter Paradise."
"84","Muhammad b. Isma'il b. Ali al-Wasawisi narrated to us, Zayd b. al-Hubab al-Ukli narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman b. Sulayman b. al-Ghasil, from Shurahbil b. Sa'd, from Jabir b. Abd Allah, from Abu Bakr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the wooden pulpit saying: Fear the Fire even with half a date, for it straightens crookedness, repels an evil death, and suffices the hungry as it suffices the full."
"85","Ishaq b. Isma'il al-Talqani narrated to us, Yahya b. Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Zuhayr b. Muhammad narrated to us, from Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Aqil, from Mu'adh b. Rifa'a b. Rafi' al-Ansari, from his father Rifa'a, he said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq saying upon the pulpit: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and Abu Bakr wept when he mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he was relieved — then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and Abu Bakr wept when he mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he was relieved — then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this heat last year saying: Ask Allah for pardon, well-being, and certainty in the Hereafter and the first."
"86","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abu Amir Abd al-Malik b. Amr al-Aqadi narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Aqil, from Mu'adh b. Rifa'a b. Rafi' al-Ansari, from his father, he said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq upon the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying — and Abu Bakr wept when he mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he was relieved — then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in heat like this last year: Ask Allah for pardon, well-being, and certainty in the Hereafter and the first."
"87","Abu Bakr b. Abi Shayba narrated to us, Zayd b. al-Hubab narrated to us, from Musa b. Ubayda, Hud b. Ata narrated to me, from Anas b. Malik, he said: Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade striking those who pray."
"88","Amr b. al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Musa b. Ubayda, from Hud b. Ata, from Anas, from Abu Bakr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade striking those who pray."
"89","Muhammad b. al-Faraj narrated to us, Muhammad b. al-Zibriqan narrated to us, Musa b. Ubayda narrated to us, Hud b. Ata informed me, from Anas b. Malik, he said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) there was a man whose worship and striving impressed us; we mentioned him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by name but he did not know him, and described him by description but he did not know him; while we were mentioning him the man appeared; we said: Here he is; he said: You tell me of a man with a touch of Satan on his face; he came until he stood over them without greeting; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I adjure you by Allah, did you say when you stood over the assembly: There is none in the people better or more excellent than me? He said: O Allah, yes; then he entered to pray; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will kill the man? Abu Bakr said: I will; he entered upon him and found him standing praying; he said: Glory be to Allah, shall I kill a praying man, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing those who pray? So he came out; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did you do? He said: I disliked killing him while he prayed, and you forbade killing those who pray; Umar said: I will; he entered and found him placing his face down; Umar said: Abu Bakr is better than me; so he came out; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What then? He said: I found him placing his face down and disliked killing him; he said: Who will kill the man? Ali said: I will; he said: You, if you find him; he said: Ali entered and found him gone; he returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What then? He said: I found him gone; he said: Had he been killed, no two men in my nation would have differed; he was their first and last; Musa said: I heard Muhammad b. Ka'b saying: He is the one Ali killed, Dhu al-Thudayya."
"90","Abd al-Aziz b. Abi Salama b. Ubayd Allah b. Abd Allah b. Umar b. al-Khattab narrated to us, Ibrahim b. Sa'd narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd b. al-Sabbaq, from Zayd b. Thabit, he narrated to him, he said: Abu Bakr sent to me after the battle of Yamama, and Umar b. al-Khattab was with him; Abu Bakr said: Umar came to me and said: Killing fell heavily on the day of Yamama upon the reciters of the Qur'an, and I fear killing will fall heavily upon the reciters of the Qur'an in the lands, so much of the Qur'an will go; I think you should order its collection; he said: I said: How do I do something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do? He said: Umar said: By Allah, it is good; he kept urging me about that until Allah opened my chest to that, and I saw in that what Umar saw; Zayd b. Thabit said: Abu Bakr said: You are a young, intelligent youth, we do not accuse you; you used to write revelation for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so trace the Qur'an and collect it; Zayd said: By Allah, had he charged me with moving a mountain of mountains it would not have been heavier upon me than what he ordered me of collecting the Qur'an; he said: I said: How do you do something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do? He said: By Allah, it is good; he kept urging me until Allah opened my chest to what He opened the chests of Abu Bakr and Umar to, and I saw in that what they saw; so I traced the Qur'an collecting it from scraps, flat stones, palm stalks, men's chests, until I missed the end of Surat al-Tawba and found it with Khuzayma b. Thabit al-Ansari: There has come to you a Messenger from yourselves, mighty upon him is what you suffer, eager for you, to the believers kind, merciful, to the end of Bara'a; the sheets remained with Abu Bakr his life until Allah took him, then with Umar until Allah took him, then with Hafsa."
"91","Abd al-Aziz b. Abi Salama al-Umari narrated to us, Ibrahim b. Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas b. Malik: That Hudhayfa b. al-Yaman came to Uthman b. Affan while campaigning with the people of Sham in the conquest of Armenia and Azerbaijan alongside the people of Iraq, and their differences in recitation alarmed Hudhayfa; Hudhayfa said to Uthman: O Commander of the Believers, reach this nation before they differ over the Book as the Jews and Christians differed; Uthman sent to Hafsa: Send us the sheets to copy them into codices then return them to you; Hafsa sent them to Uthman; Uthman ordered Zayd b. Thabit, Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr, Sa'id b. al-As, and Abd al-Rahman b. al-Harith b. Hisham to copy them into codices, and said to the three Qurashi men: When you and Zayd b. Thabit differ over anything of the Qur'an, write it in the tongue of Quraysh, for it was revealed in their tongue; they did so until, when the sheets were copied, Uthman returned the sheets to Hafsa, sent to every region a codex of what they copied, and ordered whatever else containing Qur'an in any sheet or codex to be erased or burned. Ibrahim said: al-Zuhri said: Kharija b. Zayd b. Thabit informed me that he heard Zayd b. Thabit saying: I missed a verse of Surat al-Ahzab when copying the codices, though I used to hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting it; I sought it and found it with Khuzayma b. Thabit al-Ansari: Among the believers are men true to what they pledged Allah, so I joined it in its sura in the codex."
"92","Muhammad b. Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Sadaqa b. Musa narrated to us, Farqad narrated to us, from Murra, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No deceitful one shall enter Paradise, nor one evil in mastery; the first to knock at Paradise's gate are the male and female slave when they perfect worship of their Lord and are sincere to their master."
"93","Zuhayr b. Harb narrated to us, Ishaq b. Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, from Mughira b. Muslim Abu Salama, from Farqad al-Sabakhi, from Murra al-Tayyib, from Abu Bakr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one evil in mastery shall enter Paradise; he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not tell us that this nation has the most slaves and orphans of nations? He said: Honor them as you honor your children, feed them of what you eat, clothe them of what you wear; he said: What benefit is the world to us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A horse you tie in Allah's path, and a slave who suffices you; when he prays he is your brother, when he prays he is your brother."
"94","Amr b. Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, Hammam b. Yahya narrated to us, from Farqad al-Sabakhi, from Murra al-Tayyib, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No deceitful one shall enter Paradise, nor miser, nor one who reminds of favors, nor one evil in mastery; the first to enter Paradise is the slave when he obeys Allah and obeys his master."
"95","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Mu'awiya b. Hisham narrated to us, from Shayban, from Amir, from Murra, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No one evil in his mastery shall enter Paradise; cursed is whoever harms a Muslim or deceives him."
"96","Ishaq b. Isma'il narrated to us, Jarir and Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, he said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in a place like my station, then wept and said: Ask Allah for well-being; no one was given anything better than well-being, except certainty. Abu Mu'awiya said: Except certainty."
"97","Muhammad b. Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Yahya and Uthman b. Ali narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Abu Bakr b. Abi Zuhayr, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how is soundness after this verse? Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it — are we recompensed for all that comes from us? He said: May Allah have mercy on you, O Abu Bakr, do you not grieve? Do you not toil? Does hardship not befall you? I said: Yes; he said: That is what you are recompensed with."
"98","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya b. Sa'id and Waki' narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq — and Yahya said: from Abu Bakr b. Abi Zuhayr — that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how is soundness after this verse: Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it; he said: May Allah have mercy on you, O Abu Bakr, do you not toil? Does hardship not befall you? That is what you are recompensed with."
"99","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, he said: Abu Bakr b. Abi Zuhayr narrated to me, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, how is soundness after this verse: Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it — every evil we do we are recompensed for it? He said: May Allah have mercy on you, O Abu Bakr, do you not fall ill? Do you not toil? Does hardship not befall you? That is what you are recompensed with."
"100","Muhammad b. Abi Bakr narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, he said: A man of Thaqif called Abu Bakr b. Abi Zuhayr narrated to me, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How is soundness after this verse: Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it — every evil we do we are recompensed for it? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: May Allah forgive you — or: May Allah have mercy on you — do you not fall ill? Do you not grieve? Does hardship not befall you?"
"101","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir b. Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, he said: I was told that Abu Bakr met Talha and said: Why do I see you gloomy? He said: A word I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), claiming it is decisive, but I did not ask him about it; Abu Bakr said: I know what it is; he said: What is it? He said: There is no god but Allah."
"102","Zuhayr narrated to us, Mu'alla b. Mansur narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. al-Asbahani narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: The Prophet camped at a place, and a woman sent him a sheep with her son; he milked, then said: Take it to your mother; she drank until quenched; then he brought another sheep, milked, then gave Abu Bakr to drink; then he brought another sheep, milked, then drank."
"103","Ishaq b. Isma'il narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd b. Yuthay', from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him with Bara'a to the people of Mecca: No polytheist shall perform Hajj after this year, no naked person shall circumambulate the House, none shall enter Paradise but a Muslim soul; whoever had a term with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his term is to its end; Allah is free of the polytheists, and His Messenger; he said: He traveled with it three days, then he said to Ali: Join him, return Abu Bakr to me, and convey it; he said: He did so; he said: When Abu Bakr came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he wept and said: O Messenger of Allah, has something happened concerning me? He said: Then he said: Nothing happened concerning you but good, except that I was commanded that none convey but I or a man of me."
"104","Suwayd b. Sa'id narrated to us, Suwayd b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Thabit b. Ajlan, from Sulaym b. Amir, he said: I heard Abu Bakr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go out and call among people: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah, Paradise becomes due for him; he said: So I went out and Umar b. al-Khattab met me and said: What is with you, O Abu Bakr? I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Go out and call among people: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah, Paradise becomes due for him; Umar said: Return to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for I fear they will rely upon it; so I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What sent you back? I told him Umar's saying, and he said: He spoke the truth."
"105","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yunus b. Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir b. Hazim narrated to us, al-Zubayr b. al-Khirrit narrated to us, from Abu Labid, he said: A man came out of captivity, from Tahiya, called Bayrah b. Asad, emigrating to Medina, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had died shortly before; he said: Umar b. al-Khattab saw Bayrah wandering Medina's streets and disapproved; he said: Who are you? He said: I am a man of Oman; he took his hand to Abu Bakr and said: O Abu Bakr, this is from the land whose people I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioning, of the people of Oman; Abu Bakr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I know a land washed on its side by the sea, with an Arab tribe; had my messenger come to them they would not shoot him with arrow or stone."
"106","Khalaf b. Hisham narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ikrima, he said: Abu Bakr said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What grayed you? He said: Hud, al-Waqi'a, Amma yatasa'alun, and Idha al-shamsu kuwwirat grayed me."
"107","Al-Abbas b. al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ikrima, he said: Abu Bakr said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What grayed you? And he mentioned something similar."
"108","Abd al-A'la b. Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, narrated to us — he said, and I asked about him, and he said: This is a mistake — then he narrated it to me, he said: Hammad b. Salama narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Atiq, from his father, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The toothstick purifies the mouth and pleases the Lord."
"109","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yunus b. Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad b. Salama narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Atiq, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The toothstick purifies the mouth and pleases the Lord."
"110","Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. Ar'ara al-Sami narrated to us at Basra, Ibrahim b. Abd Allah Abu Ishaq al-Razi narrated to us, Isma'il b. Nuh narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise do not trade; had they traded they would trade only in cloth."
"111","Musa b. Muhammad b. Hayyan narrated to us, Abu Dawud, the author of al-Tayalisa, narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Bukayr b. al-Akhnas, from a man, from Abu Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my nation shall enter Paradise without reckoning, their faces like the moon on the night of fullness, their hearts upon one man's heart; I asked my Lord for more, and He gave me with each man seventy thousand; Abu Bakr said: So we considered that it encompassed the people of villages and would reach the extra people of the desert."
"112","Ubayd Allah b. Mu'adh al-Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara b. Azib, he said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: When we left with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Mecca to Medina, we passed a shepherd while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thirsted; I milked for him a draught of milk, brought it to him, and he drank until I was satisfied."
"113","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani saying: I heard al-Bara b. Azib saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from Mecca to Medina, Suraqa b. Malik b. Ju'shum followed him; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated against him, and his horse sank; he said: Supplicate Allah and I will not harm you; he said: So he supplicated Allah for him; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thirsted, and they passed a sheep shepherd; Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: I took a cup and milked for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a draught of milk, brought it to him, and he drank until I was satisfied."
"114","Muhammad b. Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, he said: I heard al-Bara b. Azib saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from Mecca to Medina, Suraqa b. Malik b. Ju'shum followed him; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated against him, and his horse sank; he said: Supplicate Allah for me and I will not harm you; so he supplicated for him; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thirsted and they passed a shepherd; Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: I took a cup and milked in it a draught of milk, brought it to him, and he drank, then drank until I was satisfied."
"115","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Uthman b. Umar narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara b. Azib, he said: Abu Bakr bought a saddle from my father for thirteen dirhams, and said: Order al-Bara to carry it to my saddle; he said: No, until you tell me how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Mecca for Medina; he said: We departed and were held up our day and night until noon stood — or he said: the midday heat stood — I cast my sight and saw a rock with some shade remaining; I sprinkled it and spread for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a fur therein; I said: Sleep, O Messenger of Allah; then I went scanning around: Do I see any seeker? I saw a sheep shepherd wanting of the rock what I wanted; I said: Who are you, boy? He said: Of a Qurashi man; I recognized him; I said: Is there milk in your sheep? He said: Yes; I said: Will you milk for us? He said: Yes; I ordered him and he hobbled a sheep, I ordered him and he shook its udder, then I ordered him and he shook his hands of dust, and milked for me a draught of milk; with me was a waterskin with a cloth on its mouth; I poured water over the milk, then brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), finding him awake; I said: Drink, O Messenger of Allah; we departed, and no seeker caught us but Suraqa b. Malik b. Ju'shum upon his horse; I said: This seeker has caught us, O Messenger of Allah; he said: Grieve not, Allah is with us; when he drew near the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated against him, and his horse sank in the earth to its belly; he leapt off and said: O Muhammad, I knew this is your doing; supplicate Allah to free me from what I am in, and upon me I will blind the seekers from you; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for him, so he was freed; and this is my quiver, take an arrow from it, for you will pass by my camels and servants at such-and-such place, so take of them your need; he said: I have no need of your camels; we arrived at Medina by night, and they disputed which of them he would stay with; he said: I will stay with Banu al-Najjar, the maternal uncles of Abd al-Muttalib, honoring them with that; men and women climbed atop the houses, and boys and servants scattered in the roads calling: O Muhammad! O Messenger of Allah! O Muhammad! O Messenger of Allah!"
"116","Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. Ar'ara al-Sami narrated to us, Muhammad b. Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from al-Dahhak b. Uthman, from Muhammad b. al-Munkadir, from Abd al-Rahman b. Yarbu', from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which deed is best? He said: Raising the voice in talbiya and shedding blood of sacrifice."
"117","Shuja' b. Makhlad narrated to us, Sa'id b. Sallam al-Attar narrated to us, from Abu Bakr b. Abi Sabra al-Amiri, from Ata b. Yasar, from Abd al-Rahman b. Yarbu', from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between my house and my pulpit is a garden of Paradise's gardens, and my pulpit is upon a rivulet of Paradise's rivulets."
"118","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Uthman b. Umar narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Uthman b. Ishaq, from Qabisa b. Dhu'ayb, he said: The grandmother came to Abu Bakr asking about her inheritance; he said: You have nothing in Allah's Book, and nothing in the Sunna of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); return until I ask the people."
"119","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Sufyan b. Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Qabisa b. Dhu'ayb, that the grandmother came to Abu Bakr after the passing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I was told I have a right; Abu Bakr said: I find no right for you in the Book, nor did I hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decree anything for you; he said: Al-Mughira b. Shu'ba testified, then he said: Who testifies with you? Muhammad b. Maslama said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the sixth; al-Zuhri said: She is the mother of the mother's father or the father; when Umar's time came, the opposing one came; Umar said: Whichever of you is alone with it, it is hers; if you both come together it is between you."
"120","Zuhayr b. Harb narrated to us, Wahb b. Jarir narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Yazid b. Khumayr, from Sulaym b. Amir, from Awsat al-Bajali, he said: Abu Bakr preached to us and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preached to us last year, then Abu Bakr wept and said: Ask Allah for well-being; people were not given in this world after certainty anything better than full protection; indeed hold to truthfulness, for it is with righteousness, and they are in Paradise; beware lying, for it is with wickedness, and they are in the Fire; do not sever, do not hate, do not envy; be servants of Allah, brothers, as Allah commanded you."
"121","Ishaq b. Isma'il narrated to us, Yahya b. Abi Bukayr narrated to me, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: Yazid b. Khumayr informed me, he said: I heard Sulaym b. Amir narrating from Awsat b. Isma'il b. Awsat al-Bajali, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold to truthfulness, for it is with righteousness, and they are in Paradise; beware lying, for it is with wickedness, and they are in the Fire; do not sever, do not turn away, be servants of Allah, brothers, as Allah commanded you."
"122","Ishaq b. Isma'il narrated to us, Rawh b. Ubada narrated to us, from Shu'ba, Yazid b. Khumayr informed me, he said: I heard Sulaym b. Amir, from a man of Hims who had met the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I heard Abu Bakr preaching to us when he succeeded, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in this station of mine last year, then wept, then said: Ask Allah for pardon and full protection."
"123","Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya b. Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: Yazid b. Khumayr informed me, he said: I heard Sulaym b. Amir — a man of Himyar — narrating from Awsat b. Isma'il b. Awsat al-Bajali, from Abu Bakr, that he said when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us last year in this station of mine, then said: Ask Allah for full protection; no one was given after certainty anything better than full protection."
"124","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: I heard Ayyub, Abd al-Rahman al-Sarraj, and Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrating it, from Nafi', that he read Umar b. al-Khattab's letter: That there is nothing for fewer than five camels, and when they reach five, a sheep to nine; when ten, two sheep to fourteen; when fifteen, three to nineteen; when twenty, four to twenty-four; when twenty-five, a bint makhad to thirty-five; when exceeding, a bint labun to forty-five; when exceeding, a hiqqa to sixty; when exceeding, two bint labun to ninety; when exceeding, two hiqqas to one hundred twenty; when exceeding, in every fifty a hiqqa, in every forty a bint labun; there is nothing in sheep for fewer than forty; when forty, a sheep to one hundred twenty; when exceeding, two sheep to two hundred; when exceeding two hundred, three sheep to three hundred; when exceeding three hundred, in every hundred a sheep."
"125","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, he said: We saw with Thumama b. Abd Allah b. Anas a letter Abu Bakr al-Siddiq wrote for Anas b. Malik when he sent him over the charity of Bahrayn, bearing the seal of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), containing similar to this saying."
"126","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yunus b. Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad b. Salama narrated to us, he said: I took this letter from Thumama b. Abd Allah b. Anas, from Anas b. Malik, that Abu Bakr wrote to him that these are the obligations of charity which Allah commanded His Messenger with: Whoever is asked for them among Muslims in their proper manner, let him give them; whoever is asked above it, let him not give: In fewer than twenty-five camels, in every five camels: a sheep; when twenty-five, a bint makhad to thirty-five; if no bint makhad, a male ibn labun; when thirty-six, a bint labun to forty-five; when forty-six, a hiqqa fit for breeding to sixty; when sixty-one, a jadha'a to seventy-five; when seventy-six, two bint labun to ninety; when ninety-one, two hiqqas fit for breeding to one hundred twenty; when exceeding one hundred twenty, in every forty a bint labun, in every fifty a hiqqa; when camels' ages differ in charity obligations: Whoever owes a jadha'a but has only a hiqqa, it is accepted with two sheep if easy, or twenty dirhams; whoever owes a hiqqa but has only a jadha'a, it is accepted and the collector gives him twenty dirhams or two sheep; whoever owes a hiqqa but has only a bint labun, it is accepted with two sheep if easy, or twenty dirhams; whoever owes a bint labun but has only a hiqqa, it is accepted and the collector gives him twenty dirhams or two sheep; whoever owes a bint labun but has no bint labun, having a bint makhad, it is accepted from him with two sheep if easy, or twenty dirhams; whoever owes a bint makhad but has only a male ibn labun, it is accepted from him with nothing along; whoever has only four camels has nothing unless its owner wishes; in sheep charity, in its grazing flock: when forty, a sheep to one hundred twenty; when exceeding, two sheep to two hundred; when exceeding, three sheep to three hundred; when exceeding by one, in every hundred a sheep; no old, defective, or he-goat is taken in charity except what the collector wishes; no separate is combined nor combined separated fearing charity; what belongs to two partners is settled between them equally; when a man's grazing flock lacks one sheep of forty, there is nothing unless its owner wishes; in silver a quarter tenth; when property is only one hundred ninety dirhams, there is nothing unless its owner wishes; Abu Khaythama said: al-Riqqa means dirhams."
"127","Ubayd Allah b. Mu'adh al-Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O people, you recite this verse and place it other than where Allah placed it: O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; whoever strays harms you not if you are guided; when people see evil and do not change it, Allah is about to envelop them with punishment."
"128","Ubayd Allah b. Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, with similar, not mentioning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"129","Abu Talib Abd al-Jabbar b. Asim narrated to us, Ubayd Allah b. Amr narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, from Abu Bakr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When people see evil and do not change it, Allah is about to envelop them with punishment."
"130","Muhammad b. Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Umar b. Ali narrated to us, Isma'il b. Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays b. Hazim, he said: I heard Abu Bakr saying: O people, you recite this verse and place it other than its places: O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; whoever strays harms you not if you are guided; we heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When people see evil and do not change it, Allah is about to envelop them with His punishment."
"131","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid, from Qays b. Abi Hazim, he said: Abu Bakr recited this verse: O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; whoever strays harms you not if you are guided, then said: People place this verse other than its place; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When people see the wrongdoer and do not seize his hand, and evil and do not change it, Allah envelops them with His punishment."
"132","Yahya b. Ayyub narrated to us, Isma'il b. Ja'far narrated to us, Amr — meaning Ibn Abi Amr — informed me, from Abu al-Huwayrith, from Muhammad b. Jubayr: That Umar b. al-Khattab passed by Uthman sitting in the mosque, greeted him, but he did not return it; he entered upon Abu Bakr complaining of that to him, saying: I passed by Uthman, greeted him, but he did not return to me; he said: Where is he? He said: He is sitting in the mosque; he said: So we went to him, and Abu Bakr said to him: What prevented you from returning your brother's greeting when he greeted you? He said: By Allah, I did not perceive he greeted; he passed me while I was talking to myself, not perceiving he greeted; Abu Bakr said: What were you telling yourself? He said: Satan secluded me, casting into my soul things I would not wish I uttered though I owned the earth; I said to myself when Satan cast that into my soul: Would that I had asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what saves us from this discourse Satan casts into our souls? Abu Bakr said: I, by Allah, complained of that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him: What saves us from this discourse Satan casts of it into our souls? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What saves you from that is to say what I commanded my uncle with at death and he did not do."
"133","Ishaq b. Isma'il narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Ja'far b. Burqan, from Thabit b. al-Hajjaj, he said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq stood after the passing of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: You know what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with among you last year; he said: Ask Allah for well-being, for no servant was given anything better than full protection except certainty; and I ask Allah for certainty and well-being."
"134","Abu Khaythama and Ishaq b. Isma'il narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr b. Dinar, from Yahya b. Ja'da, he said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said upon the pulpit, weeping: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the summer of last year, the covenant near, saying: Ask Allah for certainty and well-being."
"135","Muhriz b. Awn narrated to us, Uthman b. Matar narrated to us, Abd al-Ghafur narrated to us, from Abu Nusayra, from Abu Raja, from Abu Bakr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Hold to: There is no god but Allah, and seeking forgiveness; increase in them, for Iblis said: I destroyed people with sins, but they destroyed me with: There is no god but Allah, and seeking forgiveness; when I saw that I destroyed them with desires while they deem themselves guided."
"136","Yahya b. Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Uthman b. Waqid, from Abu Nusayra, he said: I met a freedman of Abu Bakr and said to him: Did you hear Abu Bakr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None persists who seeks forgiveness, even if he returns seventy times in a day?"
"137","Ishaq b. Abi Isra'il and others narrated to us, Abu Yahya Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, from Uthman b. Waqid, from Abu Nusayra, from a freedman of Abu Bakr, from Abu Bakr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar."
"138","Abd al-Ghaffar b. Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr narrated to us, Afif b. Salim narrated to us, from Uthman b. Waqid, he said: Abu Nusayra narrated to me, from a freedman of Abu Bakr, from Abu Bakr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever seeks forgiveness does not persist, even if he returns seventy times in a day. End of Abu Bakr's Musnad; next follows Umar's Musnad, may Allah be pleased with him."
"139","With the same chain, Abu Ya'la Ahmad b. Ali b. al-Muthanna al-Mawsili narrated to us, Shayban b. Farrukh narrated to us, Sulayman b. al-Mughira narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: We were with Umar b. al-Khattab at Medina, and we sighted the crescent; I was a man of sharp sight, so I saw it with none claiming to see it but me; he said: I kept saying to Umar: Do you not see it? But he would not see it; he said: Umar was saying: I shall see it lying on my bed; then he began narrating to us of Badr's people; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to show us the death places of Badr's people the day before; he said, saying: This is so-and-so's death place tomorrow, Allah willing; he said: Umar said: By the One Who sent him with truth, they did not miss the limits the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marked; he said: So they were put in a well, some upon others; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went until he stood over them and said: O so-and-so son of so-and-so, and O so-and-so son of so-and-so, did you find what Allah and His Messenger promised you true? I have found what Allah promised me true; Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, do you address bodies with no souls in them? He said: You are not more hearing of what I say than they, except that they cannot answer me anything."
"140","Shayban narrated to us, Jarir b. Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik b. Umayr narrating from Jabir b. Samura al-Suwa'i, and he said: Umar b. al-Khattab preached to us at al-Jabiya and said: O people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us in my station among you today; he said: Treat my Companions well, then those following them; then lying will spread until a man testifies to testimony unasked, and swears an oath unasked; whoever wants Paradise's midst, let him hold to the community, for Satan is with the one, and is farther from the two; let none of you be alone with a woman, for Satan is their third; whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his evil deed is a believer."
"141","Ali b. Hamza al-Basri narrated to us, Jarir b. Hazim narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik b. Umayr, from Jabir b. Samura, he said: Umar b. al-Khattab preached to us at al-Jabiya and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in my station among you today and said: Treat my Companions well, then those following them; and he mentioned similar to Shayban's hadith."
"142","Abu Khaythama Zuhayr b. Harb narrated to us, Jarir b. Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik b. Umayr, from Jabir b. Samura, he said: Umar b. al-Khattab preached to people at al-Jabiya and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in a place like this station of mine and said: Treat my Companions well, then those following them, then those following them; then lying will spread until a man swears an oath before being asked to swear, and testifies to testimony before being asked to testify to it; whoever of you wishes to attain Paradise's midst, let him hold to the community, for Satan is with the one, and is farther from the two; let no man be alone with a woman, for their third is Satan; whoever of you is grieved by his evil deed and pleased by his good deed is a believer."
"143","Shayban narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Ghaylan b. Jarir narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Ma'bad al-Zimmani narrated to me, from Umar b. al-Khattab, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he passed a man; it was said: He has not broken fast for such-and-such; he said: He neither fasted nor broke fast — or: He neither fasted nor broke fast, Ghaylan doubted; when Umar saw the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) anger he said: O Messenger of Allah, fasting two days and breaking one? He said: Can anyone bear that? He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, fasting a day and breaking a day? He said: That is the fast of my brother Dawud; he said: O Messenger of Allah, fasting a day and breaking two days? He said: Who can bear that? He said: O Messenger of Allah, fasting Monday? He said: That is a day I was born in, and a day prophethood was sent down upon me; he said: O Messenger of Allah, fasting Arafat and Ashura? One of them said: It expiates; the other said: What is before it, or: what is after it, Abu Hilal doubted."
"144","Shayban narrated to us, Dawud b. Abi al-Furat narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Burayda narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad al-Dili, he said: I came to Medina while sickness had fallen; they were dying swiftly; I sat with Umar b. al-Khattab, and a funeral passed him praised with good for its man; Umar said: It became due; then another passed praised with evil for its man; Umar said: It became due; Abu al-Aswad said: I said: What became due, O Commander of the Believers? He said: I said as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any Muslim whom four testify well for, Allah admits him to Paradise; he said: We said: And three? He said: And three; we said: And two? He said: And two; then we did not ask him about one."
"145","Hudba b. Khalid narrated to us, Hammad b. Salama narrated to us, from Ali b. Zayd, from Yusuf b. Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard Umar b. al-Khattab saying: O people, be not deceived away from stoning; be not deceived away from stoning; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned, Abu Bakr stoned, and I stoned; there will be a people denying stoning, intercession, the Dajjal, and people exiting the Fire after it scorched them — or: they were scorched."
"146","Muhammad b. al-Sabbah and Zahmawayh narrated to us, both said: Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Qatada, he said: Abu al-Aliyah informed us, from Ibn Abbas: More than one informed me from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among them Umar b. al-Khattab, and Umar was the dearest of them to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after Fajr until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets."
"147","Mus'ab b. Abd Allah b. Mus'ab al-Zubayri narrated to us, Malik b. Anas narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from his father, that Umar b. al-Khattab was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, and he asked him about something and he did not answer him, then he asked him and he did not answer him, then he asked him and he did not answer him, so Umar said: I said: May your mother lose you, Umar; you asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three times, each time he does not answer you, so I moved my camel and went ahead of the people, and I had hardly waited when I heard a caller calling out, so I came and said: I feared that Quran had been revealed about me, so I greeted him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tonight a surah was revealed to me that is dearer to me than anything the sun has risen upon, then he recited: Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory, that Allah may forgive you what preceded of your sin and what will follow."
"148","Abu Khaythama, Ishaq b. Ismail al-Talqani, and al-Qawariri narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Malik b. Aws b. al-Hadathan; he heard Umar b. al-Khattab saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for silver is usury except hand to hand, and barley for barley is usury except hand to hand, and in the hadith of Ishaq: and dates for dates is usury except hand to hand, and in it, from Malik b. Aws: I heard Umar reporting that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ..."
"149","Ishaq b. Ismail narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri; he heard Abu Ubayd, the freedman of the Zuhriyun, saying: I witnessed the Eid with Umar b. al-Khattab, and he began with the prayer before the sermon, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting these two days; as for the day of Fitr, it is your breaking from your fast, and as for the day of Adha, then eat from the meat of your sacrifices; he did not mention in it more than this."
"150","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the sun declined, Umar ascended the minbar, and the muezzins called the adhan, and he delivered the sermon, praised Allah and extolled Him, and said in his sermon: Stoning is due for the married adulterer when there is clear proof, or pregnancy, or confession, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned, and we stoned with him and after him."
"151","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Ubayd, he said: I witnessed the Eid with Umar, and he began with the prayer before the sermon, then said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting these two days: as for the day of Adha, you eat from your sacrifices, and as for the day of Fitr, it is your breaking from your fast, he said: And I witnessed it with Uthman, and he began with the prayer before the sermon, and that coincided with Friday, so he said: This is a day on which two Eids gather; whoever is here from the people of al-Awali, we have permitted him, so if he wishes to return, let him return, and whoever loves to remain, let him remain. Then I witnessed it with Ali, and he began with the prayer before the sermon, and said: None of you should eat from his sacrifice beyond three days."
"152","Abu Khaythama Zuhayr b. Harb and Ubayd Allah b. Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah b. Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not extol me as the Christians extolled Isa son of Maryam; rather say: the slave of Allah and His Messenger."
"153","Abd al-A'la b. Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Bishr b. Mansur narrated to us, Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah."
"154","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya b. Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The dead is punished by the weeping of his family over him."
"155","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Abd Allah b. Umar, that Umar b. al-Khattab reported that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dead is punished in his grave as long as he is wailed over."
"156","Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id b. Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The dead is punished in his grave as long as he is wailed over, or: as long as he is wept over."
"157","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya b. Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Nafi' narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The dead is punished by the weeping of his family over him."
"158","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya b. Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Qatada narrated to me, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Men narrated to me, and the most pleasing of them to me was Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after the morning prayer until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets."
"159","Mus'ab b. Abd Allah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz b. Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Abi Humayd, from Zayd b. Aslam, from his father, from Umar b. al-Khattab, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Inform me of the best of the people of faith in faith, they said: O Messenger of Allah, the angels, he said: They are so, and it is right for them, and what prevents them when Allah has given them the station He has given them? Rather others, they said: O Messenger of Allah, the prophets whom Allah has honored with His message and prophethood, he said: They are so, and it is right for them, and what prevents them when Allah has given them the station He has given them? Rather others, they said: O Messenger of Allah, the martyrs who were martyred alongside the enemies, he said: They are so, and it is right for them, and what prevents them when Allah has honored them with martyrdom alongside the prophets? Rather others, they said: Then who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Peoples in the loins of men who will come after me, believing in me though they have not seen me, and affirming me though they have not seen me, finding the suspended leaves and acting upon what is in them, so these are the best of the people of faith in faith."
"160","Mus'ab b. Abd Allah narrated to us, Ibn al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Abi Humayd, from Zayd b. Aslam, from his father, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best of your leaders and the worst of them? Those whom you love and who love you, and who supplicate for you and you supplicate for them, and the worst of your leaders are those whom you hate and who hate you, and whom you curse and who curse you."
"161","Mus'ab narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz b. Muhammad narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah b. Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar assigned to Usama more than he assigned to me, so I said: My migration and Usama's migration are one, so he said: His father was dearer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than your father, and he was dearer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than you, and your parents migrated with you."
"162","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us, from Ubayd b. Hunayn, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar b. al-Khattab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) vowed to keep away from his wives for a month, then when twenty-nine days had passed, he came down to them."
"163","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Uthman b. Umar narrated to us, Ikrimah b. Ammar narrated to us, from Simak Abu Zummayl al-Hanafi, he said: Abd Allah b. Abbas narrated to me, he said: Umar b. al-Khattab narrated to me, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) secluded himself from his wives, he said: I entered the mosque and the people were striking the pebbles, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has divorced his wives, and that was before veiling was enjoined, Umar said: So I said: I will surely find out that day, he said: So I entered upon A'ishah and said: O daughter of Abu Bakr, has your affair reached that you harm the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: What have I to do with you, O son of al-Khattab? Mind your own household, he said: So I entered upon Hafsah daughter of Umar and said: O Hafsah, has your affair reached that you harm the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? By Allah, I knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) does not love you, and were it not for me, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have divorced you, he said: So she wept most intensely, and I said to her: Where is the Messenger of Allah? She said: He is in his storeroom in the loft, so I entered, and there I was with Rabah, the servant of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sitting on the threshold of the loft, dangling his feet upon a hollowed piece of wood, which is a trunk upon which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) climbed up and down, so I called him and said: O Rabah, ask permission for me with you for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Rabah looked at the room, then looked at me and said nothing, so I said: O Rabah, ask permission for me with you for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Rabah looked at the room, then looked at me and said nothing, so I said: O Rabah, ask permission for me with you for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he looked at the room, then looked at me and said nothing, then I raised my voice and said: O Rabah, ask permission for me with you for the Messenger of Allah, for I think the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thinks I came because of Hafsah; by Allah, if the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) orders me to strike her neck, I will strike her neck, and I raised my voice, so he gestured to me to give him permission, so I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining upon a mat, so I sat, and there was upon him his waist-wrap and nothing else upon him, and the mat had left marks on his side, so I looked with my sight in the storeroom of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and there I was with a handful of barley, about a sa', and the like of qaraẓ leaves in a corner of the room, and a skin hung up, he said: So my eyes hastened to tears, he said: What makes you weep, O son of al-Khattab? So I said: O Prophet of Allah, what is with me that I should not weep when this mat has left marks on your side, and this your storeroom in which I see nothing but what I see? While Caesar and Chosroes are amidst fruits and rivers, and you are the Messenger of Allah and His chosen one, and this is your storeroom? He said: O son of al-Khattab, are you not pleased that the Hereafter be ours and this world be theirs? I said: Yes, he said: And I entered upon him when I entered, and I saw anger in his face, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, what distresses you of the affair of women? If you have divorced them, then Allah is with you, and His angels, and Jibril and Mikail, and I and Abu Bakr and the believers are with you, and seldom did I speak — and I praise Allah — a word except I hoped Allah would affirm the word I say, he said: And this verse was revealed, the verse of giving choice: Perhaps his Lord, if he divorces you, will replace for him wives better than you, and: If you two support one another against him, then Allah is his Protector, and Jibril, and the righteous believers, and the angels after that are supporters, and A'ishah daughter of Abu Bakr and Hafsah used to league together against the rest of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I said: O Messenger of Allah, have you divorced them? He said: No, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, I entered the mosque and the Muslims were striking the pebbles, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has divorced his wives, so go down and inform them that you have not divorced them, he said: Yes, if you wish, so I kept speaking to him until the anger cleared from his face and until he grinned and laughed, and he was of the most beautiful of people in front teeth, then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came down, and I came down clinging to the trunk, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came down as though walking upon the ground without touching it with his hand, so I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you were in the room twenty-nine days? He said: A month may be twenty-nine days, so I stood at the door of the mosque and called out at the top of my voice: He has not divorced his wives, he said: And this verse was revealed: And when there comes to them a matter of security or fear, they spread it, but if they had referred it to the Messenger and to those in authority among them, those who derive it among them would have known it, so I was the one who derived that matter, and Allah revealed the verse of giving choice."
"164","Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Asim, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights of Ramadan."
"165","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hisham b. Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from his father, from Umar, that he found a horse which he had given as a mount in the path of Allah, and he wanted to buy it, so he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he forbade him from it."
"166","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hisham b. Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from his father, from Umar b. al-Khattab, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not tell me: It is better for you not to ask anyone among people for anything? He said: That is only asking; and whatever Allah gives you without asking, it is but provision Allah has provided you."
"167","Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Asim b. Kulayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, he said: You know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek it in the last ten, on the odd nights."
"168","Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Asim b. Kulayb, from his father, he said: I met Umar while he was at the fair, so I called him from behind the tent: Lo, I am so-and-so son of so-and-so al-Jarmi, and a nephew of ours has a captive brother among so-and-so tribe, and we offered him the ordinance of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but he refused, he said: So Umar lifted the side of the tent and said: Do you know your companion? I said: Yes, there he is, he said: Take you both with him until he carries out for you the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: And we used to say that the judgment was four camels."
"169","Abu Kurayb Muhammad b. al-Ala' narrated to us, Zayd b. al-Hubab narrated to us, Khalid b. Abi Bakr b. Ubayd Allah al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Salim narrated to me, from his father, that Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas asked Umar about wiping, so Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanding wiping over the back of the two leather socks when one wears them while they are pure."
"170","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Zayd narrated to us, from Khalid b. Abi Bakr, Salim narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanding us to wipe over the leather socks, for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"171","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yunus b. Bukayr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar entered upon Hafsah while she was weeping, and said to her: What makes you weep? Perhaps the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced you? He had divorced you once, then taken you back for my sake; by Allah, if he divorces you another time, I shall never speak to you again."
"172","Abd Allah b. Umar b. Aban narrated to us, Yahya b. Zakariya b. Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Salih b. Abi Salih, from Salamah b. Kuhayl, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had divorced Hafsah, then taken her back."
"173","Abd al-Rahman b. Salih narrated to us, and others, with his chain, the like of it."
"174","Muhammad b. Bakkar narrated to us, Bashir b. Maymun narrated to us, from Abd Allah b. Yusuf, from Abd Allah b. Umar b. al-Khattab, from Umar b. al-Khattab, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioning the people of a graveyard one day, he said: So he prayed over it and prayed abundantly over it, he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about it, and he said: The people of the graveyard of the martyrs of Asqalan; they will be escorted to Paradise as a bride is escorted to her husband."
"175","Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Numayr narrated to us, my father Abd Allah b. Numayr narrated to us, Hisham b. Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from his father, from Umar, that a man nicknamed Himar used to gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a skin of clarified butter and a skin of honey, then when its owner came demanding payment, he would bring him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say: O Messenger of Allah, give this one the price of his goods, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would do no more than smile and order that he be given, then he was brought one day to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having drunk wine, so a man said: O Allah, curse him; how often he is brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse him, for he loves Allah and His Messenger."
"176","Abd Allah b. Amir b. Barrad narrated to us, Muhammad b. Bishr narrated to us, Hisham b. Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, and he mentioned the like of it."
"177","Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah b. Abd Allah b. Abi Thawrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I said to Umar b. al-Khattab: O Commander of the Faithful, who are the two women who backed one another against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: A'ishah and Hafsah."
"178","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id b. Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The dead is punished in his grave as long as he is wailed over, or: as long as he is wept over."
"179","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Yazid narrated to us, Haywah b. Shurayh narrated to us, Abu Aqil narrated to us, from a cousin of his, from Uqbah b. Amir, that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, before you came: Whoever performs ablution and perfects the ablution and raises his gaze to the sky, and says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, without partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His slave and His Messenger, eight gates of Paradise are opened for him, entering through whichever he wishes."
"180","Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, he said: Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to me, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Rahman b. Abd Allah b. Abi Ammar narrated to me, from Abd Allah b. Babayh, from Ya'la b. Umayyah, he said: I said to Umar: Why do people shorten the prayer today? Whereas He only said: If you fear that those who disbelieve may afflict you, and that day has gone, he said: I wondered at what you wondered at, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: It is a charity Allah has given in charity to you, so accept His charity."
"181","Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Sulayman b. Atiq narrated to me, from Abd Allah b. Babayh, from Ya'la b. Umayyah, he said: I circumambulated with Umar b. al-Khattab, then when he was at the third corner facing the Stone, or the chambers facing the door, I took his hand to touch, so he said: Did you not circumambulate with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes, he said: Did you see him touching it? I said: No, he said: Then pass on from you, for you have in the Messenger of Allah a good example."
"182","Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Ghundar Muhammad b. Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak b. Harb, he said: I heard al-Nu'man b. Bashir delivering a sermon, he said: Umar b. al-Khattab mentioned what people had attained of this world, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spending the day writhing, not finding poor-quality dates to fill his belly with."
"183","Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us, Hisham b. Abi Abd Allah narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Salim b. Abi al-Ja'd, from Ma'dan b. Abi Talhah, that Umar b. al-Khattab delivered a sermon on a Friday, and mentioned the Prophet of Allah, and mentioned Abu Bakr, and said: I saw as though a rooster pecked me once or twice, and I see it only as the nearness of my term, and some people bid me to appoint a successor, and Allah would not waste His religion, nor His caliphate, nor that with which He sent His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I know that some people will impugn this affair; I struck them with this hand of mine for Islam, and if they do, then those are the enemies of Allah, the disbelievers, the misguided, so if my affair is hastened, then the caliphate is consultation among these men with whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while pleased with them, and I leave nothing after me more weighty to me than al-Kalalah, and I did not revisit the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about anything as I revisited him about al-Kalalah, and he was not harsh with me about anything as he was harsh with me about it, until he poked my chest with his finger, and said to me: O Umar, does not the summer verse at the end of Surat al-Nisa' suffice you? And if I live, I shall judge in it with a judgment by which both he who recites the Quran and he who does not recite the Quran will judge. Then he said: O Allah, I call You to witness over the governors of the provinces, for I sent them only to teach them their religion and the Sunnah of their Prophet, and to be just to them, and to divide their fay' among them, and to refer to me what is obscure of their affair to them. Then, O people, you eat from two trees which I see only as foul: this onion and garlic; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he found their smell from a man in the mosque, order him taken out to al-Baqi', so whoever eats them, let him kill them by cooking."
"184","Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Mu'adh b. Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Hajjaj b. Artah, from Musa b. Talhah, from Yazid b. al-Hawtakiyyah, that Umar b. al-Khattab said: Who witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the Bedouin brought him a rabbit? So a man among the people said: I; the Bedouin brought it, having cleaned it and prepared it, gifting it to the Messenger of Allah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat, so a man among the people said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw it bleeding, so the people ate and the Bedouin did not eat, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Will you not eat? He said: I am fasting. He said: Then why not the eggs?"
"185","Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yahya b. Hani', from Nu'aym b. Dajajah, he said: I heard Umar saying: There is no migration after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"186","Ubayd Allah b. Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, Asim b. Muhammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, he said: I know only that he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, blessed and exalted, said: Whoever humbles himself to Me like this — and Yazid inclined his palm toward the ground — I raise him like this, and Yazid gestured with the inside of his palm toward the sky."
"187","Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, from Hisham b. Sa'd, from Zayd b. Aslam, from his father, he said: I heard Umar b. al-Khattab saying: Why the trotting and baring of the shoulders, when Allah has made Islam firm and removed polytheism? He said: Then he said: And what is that? Shall we abandon something we used to do in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"
"188","Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibrahim b. Abd al-A'la, from Suwayd b. Ghafalah, he said: I saw Umar b. al-Khattab kissing the Stone, saying: I do kiss you, and I know you are a stone that neither harms nor benefits, but I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) devoted to you."
"189","Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, from Abd Allah b. Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: That Umar used to perfume the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with incense every Friday."
"190","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Bishr b. al-Mufaddal and Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah b. Umar, from Nafi', that Ibn Umar narrated to him that he divorced his wife with one divorce while she was menstruating, so Umar sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Order Abd Allah b. Umar to take her back, then let him keep her until she becomes pure from this menstruation of hers, then when she menstruates another menstruation and becomes pure, if he wishes let him divorce her before he touches her, and if he wishes let him keep her, for that is the waiting period Allah ordered that women be divorced for."
"191","Abu Sa'id al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid b. Zuray' and Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us, both said: Awf narrated to us, he said: Alqamah b. Abd Allah al-Muzani narrated to me — Yazid said in his hadith: in the mosque of Basra — he said: A man narrated to me whom he named, and Awf forgot his name, and Yahya said: A man narrated to me, he said: I was in Medina in a gathering in which was Umar b. al-Khattab, so he said to one of his companions: How did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) describe Islam? So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Islam began as a young camel, then as a two-toothed, then as a four-toothed, then as a six-toothed, then as a full-mouthed old camel, so Umar said: After full maturity there is nothing but decline."
"192","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Khaythamah, from Qays b. Marwan, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to recite the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it upon the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd."
"193","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad b. Khazim narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said, and al-A'mash, from Khaythamah, from Qays b. Marwan, he said: A man came to Umar while he was at Arafah and said: O Commander of the Faithful, I came from Kufa and left a man dictating the codices from memory, he said: So Umar became angry and swelled until he almost filled what is between the two arms of the saddle, and said: Woe to you, who is he? He said: So he said: Abd Allah b. Mas'ud, so Umar kept calming and concealing the anger from him until he returned to the state he was upon, and said: Woe to you! By Allah, I know no one among people remaining more deserving of that than him, and I shall tell you about that: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would continually spend the night in conversation at Abu Bakr's, likewise on a night, concerning some affair of the Muslims, and he spent one night in conversation at his place while I was with him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out walking and we walked with him, and there was a man standing praying in the mosque, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood listening to his recitation, then when we were about to recognize the man, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to recite the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it upon the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd, he said: Then the man sat supplicating, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began saying: Ask, you will be given, so Umar said: So I said: By Allah, I shall go to him in the morning and give him glad tidings, he said: So I went to him in the morning to give him glad tidings, and found Abu Bakr had preceded me to him and given him glad tidings, and by Allah, I never raced him to any good but he preceded me to it."
"194","Al-Qawariri Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Muhammad b. Khazim narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: A man came to Umar while he was standing at Arafah, and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Abu Khaythama, and the two did not mention in it Khaythamah, nor Qays b. Marwan."
"195","Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Asma' narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, Sa'id al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Firas, he said: I witnessed Umar b. al-Khattab while he was addressing the people, he said: So he said: O people, a time has come upon me when I saw that whoever recited the Quran sought Allah and what is with Him, then it seems to me that some people recited it seeking thereby people and seeking thereby this world; lo, seek Allah by your deeds; lo, we used to know you when revelation came down, and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us, and when Allah informed us of your news, but revelation has ceased, and the Prophet of Allah has gone, so we know you only by what we say to you; lo, whoever we see good from, we think good of him and love him for it, and whoever we see evil in, we think evil of him and hate him for it; your secrets are between you and your Lord; lo, I send my workers only to teach you your religion, and to teach you your ways, and I do not send them to strike your backs, nor to take your wealth; lo, whoever is disturbed by anything of that, let him raise it to me, for by Him in whose hand is the soul of Umar, I shall surely retaliate you against him, he said: So Amr b. al-As stood and said: O Commander of the Faithful, what if you send a worker among your workers and he disciplines a man among his subjects and strikes him, will you retaliate him from him? He said: So he said: Yes, by Him in whose hand is the soul of Umar, I shall surely retaliate from him; shall I not retaliate when I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) retaliating from himself? Lo, do not strike the Muslims lest you humiliate them, nor withhold their rights lest you make them disbelieve, nor keep them in garrisons lest you tempt them, nor settle them in thickets lest you waste them."
"196","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yahya b. Sa'id; he heard it from Ubayd b. Hunayn, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I wanted to ask Umar for nearly a year about the two women who backed one another against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but I did not dare to ask him, and we were at Marr Zahran when he went to perform ablution, and said: Bring me a skin of water, so I brought it to him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, who are the two women? I had not finished my speech before he said: A'ishah and Hafsah."
"197","Abu Khaythama and al-Qawariri narrated to us, both said: Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us, from Asim b. Ubayd Allah b. Asim, from Abd Allah b. Amir b. Rabi'ah, from his father, from Umar b. al-Khattab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow between Hajj and Umrah, for following between them removes poverty and debts, as the bellows removes the dross of iron."
"198","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah b. Abi Yazid, from his father; he heard Umar b. al-Khattab saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child belongs to the bed."
"199","Abu Khaythama and Abu Sa'id narrated to us, both said: Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Samurah sold wine, so Umar said: May Allah fight Samurah; did he not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse the Jews; fats were forbidden to them, so they sold them and consumed their prices?"
"200","Ibrahim b. al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abd Allah b. al-Mukhtar, from Abd al-Malik b. Umayr, from Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr, from Umar b. al-Khattab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is displeased by his evil deed, and pleased by his good deed, he is the believer."
"201","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abd Allah b. al-Mukhtar, with its chain, the like of it, he said: He is a believer."
"202","Abu Ubaydah b. al-Fudayl b. Iyad narrated to us, Malik b. Su'ayr narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Umar b. al-Khattab, he said: And I see only that he raised it; he judged concerning the hyena struck by a pilgrim in ihram with a sheep, and concerning the rabbit with a young goat, and concerning the jerboa with a young weaned female, and concerning the gazelle with a ram."
"203","Ahmad b. Hatim al-Tawil narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz b. Muhammad narrated to us, from Salih b. Muhammad b. Za'idah, from Salim, from his father, from his grandfather Umar b. al-Khattab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever you find stealing war booty, beat him and burn his goods, he said: So I entered upon Maslamah b. Abd al-Malik, and he seized a man who had stolen, so he called Salim and he narrated the hadith to him, he said: So he burned his goods, and found in his goods a mushaf, so he valued the mushaf and gave its value in charity."
"204","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Husayn, from Amr b. Maymun, from Umar b. al-Khattab, he said: When he was struck, Abd Allah b. Umar said to him: Will you not appoint a successor, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: I find no one more deserving of this affair than these with whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while pleased with them, so he named Ali, Uthman, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas, and said: Let Abd Allah b. Umar witness them, and he has nothing of the affair; whomever they appoint as successor, he is the caliph after me, and if Sa'd gets it, otherwise let the caliph after me seek his help; for I did not remove him for weakness nor treachery."
"205","Husayn b. al-Aswad al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Hisham b. Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: I attended my father when he was struck, he said: So they praised him with good, and he said: A monk and a desirer, they said: Will you not appoint a successor? He said: Shall I bear your affair alive and dead? I wish my share from you were sufficiency, neither against me nor for me, then he said: If I appoint a successor, one better than me appointed, and if I leave you, one better than me left you, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abd Allah b. Umar said: So I knew that when he mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would not appoint a successor."
"206","Abd Allah b. Aban al-Kufi narrated to us, Abdah b. Sulayman narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah b. Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr b. Ubayd Allah, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should eat with his left hand, for Satan eats with his left hand."
"207","Ubayd Allah b. Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Malik b. Aws b. al-Hadathan narrated to us, he said: Talhah b. Ubayd Allah exchanged with me silver for gold, and said: Wait until our produce comes from al-Ghabah, so Umar b. al-Khattab heard him saying it, he said: So he said: No, by Allah, do not leave him until you pay him in full, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Gold for silver is usury except hand to hand, and wheat for wheat is usury except hand to hand, and barley for barley is usury except hand to hand, and dates for dates is usury except hand to hand."
"208","Dawud b. Rushayd narrated to us, Abbad b. al-Awwam narrated to us, Sufyan b. Husayn narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Malik b. Aws b. al-Hadathan, that Umar b. al-Khattab sold Talhah b. Ubayd Allah one hundred dinars for silver, so Umar said: The like of it is in his hand, I said: I have no wealth until the owner of my estate comes from al-Ghabah, so he said: No, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Gold for silver is usury except hand to hand."
"209","Ibrahim b. al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan b. Salm, that Umar b. al-Khattab employed Ibn Abd al-Harith over the people of Mecca, then Umar came and Nafi' b. Abd al-Harith met him, while Abd al-Rahman b. Abza was left as deputy over the people of Mecca, so Umar became angry until he stood in the stirrup, and said: Do you appoint over the household of Allah Abd al-Rahman b. Abza? He said: I found him the most reciting of them of the Book of Allah and the most understanding of them in the religion of Allah, so Umar humbled himself for it until he settled upon his mount, and said: If you said that? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah will raise by this religion some peoples and lower thereby others."
"210","Muhammad b. Ali b. al-Hasan b. Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: al-Husayn b. Waqid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib b. Abi Thabit, that Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla narrated to him, he said: I went out with Umar b. al-Khattab to Mecca, and the governor of Mecca, Nafi' b. Alqamah — named after an uncle of his called Nafi' — met us, and said: Whom did you appoint over Mecca? He said: I appointed over it Abd al-Rahman b. Abza, he said: You have turned to a man from the freedmen and appointed him over those in it of Quraysh and the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, I found him the most reciting of them of the Book of Allah, and Mecca is a land attended by many, so I loved that they hear the Book of Allah from a man of good recitation, he said: What a good view; Allah raises by the Quran some peoples and lowers by the Quran some peoples, and Abd al-Rahman b. Abza is among those Allah raised by the Quran."
"211","Hudbah b. Khalid Abu Khalid narrated to us, Mubarak b. Fadalah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Asfar narrated to me, from Sa'sa'ah b. Mu'awiyah, he said: Uways b. Amir was a man from Qaran, and he was from the people of Kufa, and he was among the Followers; a white leprous spot came upon him, so he supplicated to Allah to remove it from him, and He removed it, so he said: O Allah, leave for me in my body of it what I may remember Your favors to me by, so He left for him of it what he may remember His favors to him by, and he was a man who kept to the mosque among some of his companions, and he had a cousin who kept to the ruler, obsessed with him; if he saw him with rich people, he said: He only lives off them, and if he saw him with poor people, he said: He only deceives them, while Uways said nothing about his cousin but good, except that when he passed by him he hid from him fearing he would sin by insulting him, and Umar b. al-Khattab used to ask the delegations when they came to him from Kufa: Do you know Uways b. Amir al-Qarani? And they would say: No, then a delegation from the people of Kufa came, among them that cousin of his, so he said: Do you know Uways b. Amir al-Qarani? His cousin said: O Commander of the Faithful, he is my cousin, a base corrupt man who has not reached that you should know him, O Commander of the Faithful, so Umar said to him: Woe to you, you are ruined, woe to you, you are ruined; when you come to him, convey my greeting to him, and order him to come to me, so he came to Kufa and did not take off his travel clothes before he came to the mosque, he said: So he saw Uways and embraced him, and said: Ask forgiveness for me, O cousin, he said: May Allah forgive you, O cousin, he said: And may Allah forgive you, O Uways b. Amir, the Commander of the Faithful conveys his greeting to you, he said: And who mentioned me to the Commander of the Faithful? He said: He mentioned you, and ordered us to convey to you that you come to him, he said: Hearing and obedience to the Commander of the Faithful, so he came as a delegate to him until he entered upon Umar, so he said: Are you Uways b. Amir? He said: Yes, he said: Are you the one upon whom a white spot came, so you supplicated to Allah to remove it from you, and He removed it, then you said: O Allah, leave in my body of it what I may remember Your favor to me by, so He left in your body what you remember His favors to you by? He said: And how do you know, O Commander of the Faithful? By Allah, no human saw this, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us that there will be among the Followers a man from Qaran called Uways b. Amir; a white spot will come upon him, so he will supplicate to Allah to remove it from him, and He will remove it, then he will say: O Allah, leave in my body what I may remember Your favor to me by, he said: So He will leave for him of it what he remembers His favors to him by, so whoever among you reaches him and is able to have him ask forgiveness for him, let him have him ask forgiveness for him, so ask forgiveness for me, O Uways b. Amir, so he said to him: May Allah forgive you, O Commander of the Faithful, he said: And may Allah forgive you, O Uways b. Amir, he said: So when they heard Umar say: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man said: Ask forgiveness for me, O Uways, and another said: Ask forgiveness for me, O Uways, so when they crowded upon him, he slipped away and went, and was not seen until this hour."
"212","Ibrahim b. al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, he said: Umar b. al-Khattab wrote to Utbah b. Farqad: Peace be upon you, then: Wear coarse wool and waist-wraps, cast off trousers, wear sandals and cast off leather socks, shoot at targets and cut the stirrups, mount horses by leaping, and upon you is the Jurami and Ma'addi manner, and beware of excess and the dress of the non-Arabs, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade silk except what was like this, three fingers, or like this, four fingers."
"213","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman, from Umar, he said: Beware of wearing silk, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing silk except like this, and he raised his fingers, the index and the middle."
"214","Ibrahim b. al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali b. Zayd, from Abu Rafi', from Umar b. al-Khattab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Hajun, sad and grieving, and said: O Allah, show me today a sign after which I shall not care who among my people disbelieves me, so he called a tree from the direction of the Aqabah of the people of Medina, so he called it and it came splitting the earth until it reached him, and greeted him, then he ordered it and it went away, he said: So he said: I shall not care who among my people disbelieves me after it."
"215","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman b. Safwan, he said: I said to Umar b. al-Khattab: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do when he entered Mecca? He said: He prayed two rak'ahs."
"216","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Ata', from Ya'la b. Umayyah, he said: I saw Umar b. al-Khattab touch the Black Stone and kiss it, and say: I do kiss you, and I know you are a stone that neither harms nor benefits, but I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss you."
"217","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibrahim b. Abd al-A'la, from Suwayd b. Ghafalah, that Umar kissed it — meaning the Stone — and embraced it, and said: I saw Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) devoted to you."
"218","Muhammad b. Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Dawud, the author of al-Tayalisah, narrated to us, from Ja'far b. Muhammad al-Makhzumi, he said: I saw Muhammad b. Abbad b. Ja'far kiss the Stone and prostrate upon it, and say: I saw Umar b. al-Khattab kissing the Stone and prostrating upon it, and saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing it."
"219","Zakariya b. Yahya Zahmawayh al-Wasiti narrated to us, Umar b. Harun narrated to us, from Hanzalah b. Abi Sufyan, from Salim b. Abd Allah, from his father, he said: I saw Umar b. al-Khattab kiss the Stone and prostrate upon it, then return and kiss it and prostrate upon it, then say: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"220","Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Hizam b. Hisham b. Hubaysh b. al-Ashqar al-Khuza'i, he said: I heard my father mentioning that he saw Umar b. al-Khattab kissing the Stone, saying: I bear witness that you are a stone, but I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing you."
"221","Ishaq b. Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah b. Abd Allah b. Abi Thawr, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar b. al-Khattab, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was reclining upon a woven mat that had left marks on his side, so I raised my head in the house, and by Allah, I saw nothing in it to catch the eye except three hides."
"222","Ishaq narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Shu'bah b. al-Hajjaj, from Simak b. Harb, that he heard al-Nu'man b. Bashir delivering a sermon, he said: Umar b. al-Khattab mentioned what people had attained of this world, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spending the day writhing, not finding of the poor-quality dates what to fill his belly with."
"223","Abu Hammam al-Walid b. Shuja' narrated to us, Abd Allah b. al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Hisham b. Sa'd, from Zayd b. Aslam, from his father, from Umar b. al-Khattab, saying: By Allah, were it not that we would leave the end of time destitute with nothing for them, I would not leave a town Allah opened to the people of Islam but divide it as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided Khaybar."
"224","Abu Kurayb Muhammad b. al-Ala' narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham b. Sa'd, from Zayd b. Aslam, from his father, from Umar b. al-Khattab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of one who takes back his charity is like the example of the dog returning to its vomit."
"225","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Ishaq b. Uthman al-Kilabi narrated to us, Isma'il b. Abd al-Rahman b. Atiyah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: My grandmother Umm Atiyah narrated to me, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina, he gathered the women of the Ansar in a house, then sent Umar to us, so he stood and greeted, and we returned the greeting upon him, and said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah to you, we said: Welcome to the Messenger of Allah and to the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: So he said: Do you pledge me that you will not fornicate, nor steal, nor kill your children, nor bring a slander you fabricate between your hands and your feet, nor disobey in what is right? We said: Yes, she said: So we extended our hands from inside the house and he extended his hand from outside it, and he ordered us to bring out the menstruating women and the secluded maidens for the two Eids, and forbade us from following funerals, and there is no Friday upon us, he said: I said: What is the right in which you were forbidden? She said: Wailing."
"226","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Ishaq b. Sulayman narrated to us, Mu'awiyah b. Yahya narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, from Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying to a man: Come, I shall gamble with you, so he ordered him to give charity."
"227","Abu Hisham narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Umar b. Hamzah narrated to us, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah."
"228","Abu Hisham narrated to us, Zayd b. al-Hubab narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Budayl b. Warqa' narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim b. Abd Allah, from his father, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Evil omen is in three: in the mount, the dwelling, and the woman. Abu Hisham said: He is mistaken."
"229","Abu Hisham narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Asim b. Ubayd Allah b. Asim, from his father, from his grandfather Umar, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a battle, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, the enemy has come while they are satiated and the people are hungry, so the Ansar said: Shall we not slaughter our water-carrying camels and feed the people? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has surplus food, let him bring it, so they began bringing a mudd and a sa' and more and less, and all that was in the army was some twenty-odd sa's, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat beside it and invoked blessing, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take and do not snatch, so a man would take in his sack and in his bag, and they took in their vessels, until a man would tie the sleeve of his shirt and fill it, so they finished while the food was as it was, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah; no servant brings them truthfully but Allah shields him from the heat of the Fire."
"230","Abu Hisham narrated to us, al-Nadr, meaning Ibn Mansur, narrated to us, Abu al-Janub narrated to us, he said: I saw Ali fetching water for his ablution, so I hastened to fetch for him, so he said: Stop, O Abu al-Janub, for I saw Umar fetching water for his ablution, so I hastened to fetch for him, so he said: Stop, O Abu al-Hasan, for I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fetching water for his ablution, so I hastened to fetch for him, so he said: Stop, O Umar, for I dislike that anyone share with me in my purification."
"231","Uqbah b. Mukram narrated to us, Yunus b. Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id b. Ubayd, the freedman of Ibn Azhar, he said: I heard Umar b. al-Khattab saying: These two days, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade you fasting them: the day of your breaking from your fast, and a day in which you eat of the meat of your sacrifices."
"232","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that when Umar was stabbed, Hafsah wailed over him, so he said: O Hafsah, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The one wailed over is punished."
"233","Suwayd b. Sa'id narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Malik b. Aws b. al-Hadathan, that he informed him that he sought exchange for one hundred dinars, he said: So Talhah b. Ubayd Allah called me, and we agreed upon the exchange until he exchanged with me and took the gold turning it in his hand, he said: Until my treasurer comes from al-Ghabah, while Umar b. al-Khattab was listening, so Umar said: No, by Allah, do not leave him until you take from him, then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for gold is usury except hand to hand, and dates for dates is usury except hand to hand, and barley for barley is usury except hand to hand."
"234","Ahmad b. Isa narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Wahb narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, that al-Sa'ib b. Yazid and Ubayd Allah b. Abd Allah informed him, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abd al-Qari, he said: I heard Umar b. al-Khattab saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sleeps through his portion, or anything of it, then recites it between the Fajr prayer and the Zuhr prayer, it is written for him as though he recited it in the night."
"235","Ishaq b. Isma'il and Abu Ja'far, my maternal uncle, narrated to us, both said: Yahya b. Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Umar al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id b. Amr b. Sa'id narrated to me, that he heard his father on the day of al-Marj saying: I heard Umar b. al-Khattab saying: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah protects the religion by Christians from Rabi'ah on the bank of the Euphrates, I would not have left an Arab but I would have killed him or he submits."
"236","Ishaq b. Isma'il al-Talqani narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Husayn, from Salim b. Abi al-Ja'd, he said: Umar said, and he mentioned speech: Some people say: Why do you not appoint a successor? So I find none more deserving of this affair than these men with whom the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while pleased with them, so whichever of them they appoint, he is the caliph after me."
"237","Ishaq b. Isma'il narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri; he heard Abu Ubayd — meaning the freedman of Ibn Azhar — saying: I witnessed the Eid with Umar b. al-Khattab, and he began with the prayer before the sermon and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting these two days: as for the day of Fitr, it is your breaking from your fast, and as for Adha, eat from the meat of your sacrifices."
"238","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Abu Bakr b. Hafs informed me, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that Umar saw upon a man from al-Utarid a cloak of brocade, or silk, and said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you bought it? So he said: Only one with no share wears this, he said: So a striped Syrian cloak was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he sent it to me, he said: So I said: You sent it though I heard you say about it what you said? So he said: I sent it to you only to benefit from it."
"239","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Hisham b. Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Asim b. Umar, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the night comes and the day departs from here, the fasting one has broken his fast."
"240","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from Umar, he said: The travel prayer is two rak'ahs, and the Fitr prayer is two rak'ahs, and the Adha prayer is two rak'ahs, and the Friday prayer is two rak'ahs, complete, not shortened, upon the tongue of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"241","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Kahmas narrated to us, from Abd Allah b. Buraydah, from Yahya b. Ya'mar, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, that Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What is faith? He said: That you believe in Allah, and His angels, and His books, and His messengers, and in the Last Day, and in the decree, its good and its evil, so Jibril said: You spoke truly, so we wondered at him, asking him and affirming him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That was Jibril; he came to teach you your religion."
"242","Al-Harith b. Miskin al-Misri narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Wahb narrated to us, Hisham b. Sa'd informed us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from his father, from Umar b. al-Khattab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Musa said: O Lord, our father Adam removed us and himself from Paradise, so Allah showed him Adam, and said: Are you Adam? So Adam said to him: Yes, he said: Are you the one into whom Allah breathed of His spirit, and to whom He made His angels prostrate, and taught you all the names? He said: Yes, he said: What carried you to remove us and yourself from Paradise? So Adam said to him: Who are you? He said: I am Musa, he said: Are you Musa of the Children of Isra'il to whom Allah spoke from behind a veil, without placing between you and Him a messenger from His creation? He said: Yes, he said: Do you blame me for a matter whose decree from Allah preceded me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said thereupon: So Adam overcame Musa, so Adam overcame Musa."
"243","Muhammad b. al-Muthanna al-Zamin narrated to us, Abd al-Malik b. al-Sabbah al-Misma'i narrated to us, Imran informed us, from al-Rudayni b. Abi Mijlaz, from Yahya b. Ya'mar, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, Abu Muhammad said: Most of my thought is that he raised it, he said: Adam and Musa met; Musa said to Adam: You are the father of mankind; Allah settled you in His Paradise, and made His angels prostrate to you, Adam said to Musa: Do you not find it written? He said: So Adam overcame Musa, so Adam overcame Musa."
"244","Abu Khaythama, Harun b. Ma'ruf, and others narrated to us, they said: Abd Allah b. Yazid al-Muqri' narrated to us, Sa'id b. Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Ata' b. Dinar, from Hakim b. Sharik, from Yahya b. Maymun al-Hadrami, from Rabi'ah al-Jurashi, from Abu Hurayrah, from Umar b. al-Khattab, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not sit with the people of qadar nor open discourse with them."
"245","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Yazid narrated to us, with its chain, the like of it."
"246","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Yazid narrated to us, from Haywah b. Shurayh, from Bakr b. Amr, from Abd Allah b. Hubayrah, from Abu Tamim al-Jayshani, from Umar b. al-Khattab, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If you relied upon Allah as He deserves to be relied upon, He would provide for you as He provides for birds; they go out hungry and return full."
"247","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Yazid narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Ziyad narrated to us, from Muslim b. Yasar, from Sufyan b. Wahb al-Khawlani, he said: I heard Umar b. al-Khattab saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"248","Zuhayr b. Harb narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Yazid narrated to us, Haywah informed us, Abu Aqil informed us, from his cousin, from Uqbah b. Amir al-Juhani, that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the campaign of Tabuk, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat one day narrating to his companions, and said: Whoever stands when the sun declines, then performs ablution and perfects his ablution, then stands and prays two rak'ahs, his sins are forgiven, or he said: He is as his mother bore him, Uqbah said: So I said: Praise be to Allah who provided me to hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Umar b. al-Khattab, who was sitting facing me, said: Do you marvel at this? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said something more marvelous than this before you came, I said: So what did he say, may my father be ransomed for you? Umar b. al-Khattab said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution and perfects the ablution, then raises his gaze to the sky, and says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, without partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His slave and His Messenger, eight gates of Paradise are opened for him, entering through whichever he wishes."
"249","Zakariya b. Yahya narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Isa narrated to us, Yunus b. Ubayd narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out at midday, and found Abu Bakr in the mosque, and said: What brought you out at this hour? He said: What brought you out brought me out, O Messenger of Allah, and Umar b. al-Khattab came, so he said: O son of al-Khattab, what brought you out? He said: What brought you two out brought me out, O Messenger of Allah, so Umar sat, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began narrating to them, then said: Have you two strength to go to these palms and obtain food and drink and shade? We said: Yes, he said: Take us to Ibn al-Tayyihan Abu al-Haytham al-Ansari, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went ahead of us and greeted, and sought permission three times, while Umm al-Haytham was behind the door hearing the speech and wanting the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to increase her greeting, then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to leave, Umm al-Haytham came out hastening behind them, and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah I heard your greeting, but I wanted you to increase us of your greeting, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke good to her, and said: Where is Abu al-Haytham, why do I not see him? She said: He is near; he went to fetch us sweet water; enter, for he will come shortly, Allah willing, so she spread for them a mat under a tree, then Abu al-Haytham came and rejoiced at them, and his eyes delighted at them, and climbed a palm and cut for them a bunch, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Enough, O Abu al-Haytham, he said: O Messenger of Allah, you eat of its unripe and its ripe and its dried dates, then he brought them water and they drank upon it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is of the bliss you will be asked about, and Abu al-Haytham stood to slaughter for them a sheep, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Beware of the milch one, and Umm al-Haytham stood kneading for them and baking, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar laid their heads for the midday rest, so they awoke while their food had been prepared, so the food was placed before them and they ate and were satiated and praised Allah, mighty and majestic, and Umm al-Haytham returned to them the remainder of the bunches, so they ate of its ripe and its dried dates, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) greeted them and supplicated for them."
"250","Harun b. Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abd Allah b. Wahb narrated to us, Amr b. al-Harith narrated to me, that Umar b. al-Sa'ib narrated to him, that al-Qasim b. Abi al-Qasim al-Saba'i narrated to him, from the storyteller of the troops at Constantinople, that he heard him narrating that Umar b. al-Khattab said: O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not sit at a table upon which wine is served, he said: And he mentioned the hadith."
"251","Ahmad b. Ibrahim al-Nukri Abu Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Ata' b. Dinar al-Hudhali informed me, that Abu Yazid al-Khawlani narrated to him that he heard Fadalah b. Ubayd saying: I heard Umar b. al-Khattab reporting from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: The martyrs are four: a believing man of good faith, who meets the enemy and is true to Allah until killed, so that is the one to whom people raise their eyes on the Day of Resurrection, like this, and he raised his head until his cap fell — I know not whether Umar's cap or the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and a believing man of good faith, until when he meets the enemy, it is as though his skin is struck with thorns of the gum-tree from cowardice, then a stray arrow comes to him and kills him, so he is in the second rank, and a believing man who mixed a righteous deed and another evil, meets the enemy and is true to Allah until killed, so that is in the third rank, and a believing man who wronged himself, meets the enemy and is true to Allah until killed, so that is in the fourth rank."
"252","Ahmad b. Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, al-Layth b. Sa'd Abu al-Harith narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abd Allah b. Usamah b. al-Had, Abu Uthman al-Walid b. Abi al-Walid narrated to me, from Umar — or Uthman b. Abd Allah b. Suraqah al-Adawi — from Umar b. al-Khattab, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shades the head of a warrior, Allah will shade him on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah with his equipment, he has its reward, and whoever builds a mosque in which the name of Allah is mentioned, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"253","Abd Allah b. Umar b. Aban narrated to us, Hafs b. Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Umar, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed in the pre-Islamic age, then Allah brought Islam, he said: Fulfill your vow."
"254","Abd al-Ghaffar b. Abd Allah al-Mawsili narrated to us, Ali b. Mushir narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah b. Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar — perhaps from Umar — that he carried a horse in the path of Allah, and when we carried in the path of Allah, we brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and handed it to him, and he placed it where Allah showed him, so I came with the horse and handed it to him, and he mounted upon it a man among his companions, then I found him selling it in the market, so I wanted to buy it, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so he said: Do not buy it, and do not return to anything of your charity."
"255","Ahmad b. Ibrahim al-Nukri narrated to us, Shabbabah b. Sawwar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatada, from Salim b. Abi al-Ja'd, that Ma'dan b. Abi Talhah al-Ya'muri said: Umar b. al-Khattab delivered a sermon and said: I saw as though a red rooster pecked me once or twice, and I see that only as the nearness of my term, so if my affair is hastened, then the caliphate is consultation among these six men with whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while pleased with them, and I know that some people will impugn this affair; I fought them with this hand of mine for Islam, and if they do, then those are the enemies of Allah, the disbelievers, the misguided, and I call to witness over the governors of the provinces, for I sent them only to teach the people their religion and the Sunnah of their Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and to divide their fay', and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not harsh with me about anything, or: I did not contend with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about anything concerning the verse of al-Kalalah, until he struck my chest, and said: The summer verse revealed at the end of al-Nisa' suffices you: They ask you for a ruling; say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning al-Kalalah, and no judgment was passed in it known by he who recites and he who does not recite; it is what excludes the father, thus I reckon. Lo, O people, you eat from two trees which I see only as foul: onions and garlic, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to order the man whose smell of them was found to be taken out to al-Baqi', so whoever must eat them, let him kill them by cooking."
"256","Surayj b. Yunus narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Hisham b. Urwah, from his father, from Asim b. Umar, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the night comes and the day departs and the sun sets, the fasting one has broken his fast."
"257","Ahmad b. Ibrahim narrated to us, Bishr narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya b. Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: While Umar b. al-Khattab was addressing the people on Friday, Uthman b. Affan entered the mosque, so Umar alluded to him and said: What is with men who delay after the call? Uthman said: O Commander of the Faithful, I did no more when I heard the call than perform ablution, then come, Umar said: And ablution too! Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you comes to Friday, let him bathe?"
"258","Nasr b. Ali b. Nasr narrated to us, Muslim narrated to us, from al-Dujayn, from Aslam, the freedman of Umar, from Umar b. al-Khattab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"259","Sufyan b. Waki' b. al-Jarrah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Dujayn, from Aslam, the freedman of Umar, he said: I heard Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"260","Abu Ya'la Ahmad b. Ali b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, in the year 306, Abu Khaythama Zuhayr b. Harb narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah Muhammad b. Khazim narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Khaythamah, from Suwayd b. Ghafalah, he said: Ali said: When I narrate to you a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then falling from the sky is dearer to me than lying about him, and when I narrate to you from others, I am but a warrior, and war is deception; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will emerge at the end of time a people young in age, foolish in minds, saying the best speech of creation; their faith will not pass their throats, so wherever you meet them, kill them, for killing them is a reward for whoever kills them on the Day of Resurrection."
"261","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, he said: Abu Musa came to al-Hasan b. Ali visiting him. So Ali said to him: Did you come visiting or gloating? He said: No, rather visiting, he said: If you came visiting, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When a man visits his Muslim brother, he walks in the harvest of Paradise until he sits, then when he sits, mercy covers him; if it is morning, seventy thousand angels pray upon him until evening, and if it is evening, seventy thousand angels pray upon him until morning."
"262","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, he said: Ali addressed us and said: Whoever claims that we have anything we recite besides the Book of Allah and this sheet — a sheet in which are the teeth of camels and some matters of wounds — has lied, he said: And in it: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Medina is a sanctuary between Ayr and Thawr; whoever innovates in it an innovation or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; Allah will not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection an equivalent nor an exchange, and the protection of the Muslims is one, the lowest of them strives with it."
"263","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from al-Qasim b. Mukhaymirah, from Shurayh b. Hani', he said: I asked A'ishah about wiping over the leather socks, so she said: Go to Ali and ask him, for he was more knowledgeable than me about that, so I came to Ali and asked him about wiping, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to order us that the resident wipe a day and a night, and the traveler three."
"264","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Sa'd b. Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you seek select wives among Quraysh and leave us? He said: And do you have anything? He said: We said: Yes, the daughter of Hamzah, he said: So he said: She is not lawful to me; she is the daughter of my brother through nursing."
"265","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah b. Sakhbarah, he said: A funeral passed by Ali, and his companions went to stand, so Ali said to them: What carries you to this? They said: Abu Musa informed us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a funeral passed by him, would stand until it passed him, he said: So he said: Abu Musa says nothing; perhaps the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did that once; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved to resemble the People of the Book in what nothing had been revealed to him about, then when something was revealed to him, he left it."
"266","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Nu'man b. Sa'd, from Ali, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of a month I fast after Ramadan, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you are fasting, then fast al-Muharram, for it is the month of Allah, and in it is a day in which Allah turned to a people, and in which others are turned to."
"267","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-Nu'man b. Sa'd, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise is a market in which there is neither buying nor selling, except images of men and women; when a man desires an image, he enters it, he said: And in it is a gathering for the wide-eyed maidens, he said: They raise voices the like of which creatures never heard, he said: They say: We are the eternal, so we never perish, and we are the blissful, so we never suffer, and we are the pleased, so we never anger; so blessed is he who is for us and we are for him."
"268","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sayf al-Makki narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sacrificed the camels, ordered me to give in charity their meats and their skins and their coverings."
"269","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatada, from Jurayy b. Kulayb al-Nahdi, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the broken-horned and broken-eared sacrificial animal."
"270","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdah b. Sulayman narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatada, from Jurayy b. Kulayb al-Nahdi, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sacrificing the broken-horned and broken-eared."
"271","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi Habib, from Abd al-Aziz b. Abi al-Sa'bah, from Abu Aflah al-Hamdani, from Abd Allah b. Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, he said: Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with gold in one hand and silk in the other, and said: These two are forbidden to the males of my nation."
"272","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, Yahya b. Sa'id and Muhammad b. Amr informed us, from Waqid b. Amr b. Sa'd b. Mu'adh, he said: I went out in a funeral and stood waiting for it to be placed so I may sit, while Nafi' b. Jubayr was near me, then when it was placed, I sat to him, so he said: As though you waited for this funeral to be placed to sit? I said: Yes, because of a hadith that reached me from Abu Sa'id, so he said: Mas'ud narrated to me that he heard Ali saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for a funeral, then sat and ordered us to sit."
"273","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, al-Awwam b. Hawshab informed us, from Amr b. Murrah, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us until he placed his leg between me and Fatimah, and taught us what to say when we take our beds: thirty-three glorifications, and thirty-three praises, and thirty-four magnifications, Ali said: So I never left them after, so a man said to him: Not even the night of Siffin? Ali said: Not even the night of Siffin."
"274","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham b. Amr al-Fazari, from Abd al-Rahman b. al-Harith b. Hisham, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his witr: O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You; I do not encompass praise of You; You are as You praised Yourself."
"275","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, Muhammad b. Amr narrated to us, from Ibrahim b. Abd Allah b. Hunayn, from his father, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me — and I do not say he forbade you — wearing a gold ring, and wearing qassi garments, and reciting while bowing."
"276","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid informed us, Sufyan b. Husayn informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Ubayd, the freedman of Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, he said: I heard Ali saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me keeping the meats of sacrifices beyond three days."
"277","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid b. Harun narrated to us, Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Ali b. Zayd, from Rabi'ah b. al-Nabighah, from his father, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade visiting graves, and vessels, and keeping the meats of sacrifices beyond three days, he said: I used to forbid you visiting graves, so visit them, for they remind you of the Hereafter, and I forbade you vessels, so drink in them and avoid what intoxicates, and I forbade you the meats of sacrifices to keep beyond three days, so keep them as it seems to you."
"278","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Zubayd, from Sa'd b. Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no obedience to a human in disobedience to Allah."
"279","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah b. Mudarrib, from Ali, he said: There was among us no horseman on the day of Badr but al-Miqdad, and I saw us with none standing among us but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying under a tree and weeping until morning."
"280","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim b. Kulayb, from Abu Burdah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me placing the ring in this, or in this: the index and the middle."
"281","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Shu'bah, and Sufyan, and Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake his family in the last ten nights of Ramadan."
"282","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayyah, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution three times three times."
"283","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Amr b. Murrah, from Abd Allah b. Salamah, from Ali: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was ill, and I was saying: O Allah, if my term has come, relieve me, and if it is delayed, raise me, and if it is affliction, make me patient, so he struck my chest with his hand, and said: O Allah, grant him health and heal him, so I never complained of that pain of mine after."
"284","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz b. Abd Allah b. Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Majishun b. Abi Salamah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Ubayd Allah b. Abi Rafi', from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he opened the prayer, would magnify, then say: I have turned my face to Him who originated the heavens and the earth, upright, and I am not of the polytheists; my prayer and my rites and my life and my death are for Allah, Lord of the worlds, without partner to Him, and with that I am commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims, he said: And he mentioned the hadith."
"285","Zuhayr and Ubayd Allah al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, Za'idah b. Qudamah narrated to us, from Khalid b. Alqamah al-Hamdani, from Abd Khayr, he said: Ali entered al-Rahbah after he had prayed Fajr, and sat in al-Rahbah, then said to a boy of his: Bring me purification, so the boy came with a vessel in which was water and a basin, Abd Khayr said: While we were sitting looking at him, so he took with his right the vessel and poured upon his left hand and washed his palms three times, Abd Khayr said: Each time he did not put his hand in the vessel until he had washed them three times, then he put his right hand in the vessel and filled his mouth with water and rinsed and sniffed and blew with his left hand three times, then washed his face three times, then washed his right hand three times to the elbow, then washed his left hand three times, then put his right hand in the vessel until the water covered it, then raised it with what it carried of water, then wiped it with his left hand, then wiped his head with both his hands together, then put his right hand in the vessel, then poured upon his right foot and washed it three times with his left hand, then put his right hand in the vessel and filled it, then poured with his right hand upon his left foot and washed it three times with his left hand, then put his right hand in the vessel and filled it with water and drank from it, then said: This is the purification of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); whoever loves to look at the purification of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him look at this."
"286","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr, from Abd Allah b. Salamah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come out from the privy and recite the Quran, and eat meat with us, and nothing veiled him — or barred him — from the Quran except major impurity."
"287","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad b. al-Munkadir, he said: I heard Mas'ud b. al-Hakam narrating from Ali, he said: We saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand, so we stood, and sit, so we sat. Meaning in the funeral."
"288","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated to us, Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Ya'la b. Ata', from Abd Allah b. Yasar, that Amr b. Hurayth visited al-Hasan b. Ali, so Ali said to him: Do you visit Hasan while in the soul is what is in it? So he said: O Ali, you are not the lord of my heart to turn it where you wish, he said: That does not prevent me from delivering counsel to you; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No Muslim visits a sick one but seventy thousand angels pray upon him whichever hours of the day until evening, and whichever hours of the night it is until morning."
"289","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Isma'il b. Salim, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali, that a married adulterer was brought to him, he said: So he flogged him on Thursday, he said: Then he stoned him on Friday, he said: So it was said to him: You combined upon him two penalties? He said: So he said: I flogged him by the Book of Allah, and stoned him by the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"290","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ubayd Allah b. Musa narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Adi b. Thabit, from Zirr b. Hubaysh, from Ali, he said: By Him who split the seed and created the soul, it is the covenant of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to me that none loves you but a believer, and none hates you but a hypocrite."
"291","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Abu Maryam, he said: Ali narrated to us, he said: I went out at night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we came to the Kabah, and he said to me: Sit, so I sat, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) climbed onto my shoulders, then I stood up with him, and when he saw my weakness under him he said: Sit, so I sat, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came down and sat for me and said: Climb onto my shoulders, then I climbed onto him, then he stood up with me until it seemed to me that if I wished I could reach the horizon of the sky, and I climbed onto the House, and I came to the idol of Quraysh, which was a statue of a man made of brass or copper, and I kept working at it right and left, in front of it and behind it, until I overpowered it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying: Come on, come on, while I worked at it, then he said to me: Throw it down, so I threw it down, and it broke as glass vessels break, then I came down and we hurried away until we hid among the houses fearing someone would learn of us, and nothing was raised upon it afterwards."
"292","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Hubshi, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, you send me to a people of elders with age, and I fear I will not get it right? He said: Indeed Allah will steady your tongue and guide your heart."
"293","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Abu Maryam, from Ali, that the wife of al-Walid ibn Uqbah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining that al-Walid beat her, so he said to her: Go back and say to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has granted me protection. She went and waited a while then came back and said: O Messenger of Allah, he has not desisted from me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut a fringe from his garment and gave it to her and said: Say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has granted me protection, this is a fringe from his garment. She waited a while, then she returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, he has only beaten me more. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands and said: O Allah, deal with al-Walid, two or three times."
"294","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, from Mukhtar al-Tammar, from Abu Matar al-Basri, he said: I was with Ali, and we reached the large market, and he noticed an old man among them and said: O sheikh, sell me well a shirt for three dirhams. He said: Yes, O Commander of the Believers. When he recognized him he did not buy anything from him, and he went to a young boy and bought a shirt from him for three dirhams, and he wore it from the wrists to the ankles, saying as he wore it: Praise be to Allah who provided me from clothing with what I beautify myself with among people and cover my private parts with. The Muslims said: Something you narrate from yourself, or from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that when he wore a garment."
"295","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Ali, he said: We have nothing except the Book of Allah and this sheet from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Indeed Madinah is sacred, between Ayr and Thawr; whoever introduces an innovation in it or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; no obligatory or voluntary deed is accepted from him. And he said: The protection of the Muslims is one, the lowest of them strives to grant it; whoever betrays a Muslim, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; no obligatory or voluntary deed is accepted from him. And whoever takes as allies a people without the permission of his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; Allah does not accept from him any obligatory or voluntary deed."
"296","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, that he forbade a man to recite the Quran while bowing, and said: When you bow, glorify Allah, and when you prostrate, supplicate to Allah, for it is fitting that you be answered."
"297","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to oversee his sacrificial camels, and to distribute their skins and coverings, and he ordered me not to give the butcher anything from them; we give him from our own."
"298","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, raising it, he said: I have exempted you from the charity on horses and slaves."
"299","And with it, from Ali, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He ruled that debt comes before the bequest. He said: And you recite the bequest before the debt."
"300","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Sad, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Ali, he said: The Magians had a book they recited and knowledge they studied, then their leader committed adultery, and they wanted to carry out the hadd on him, so he said to them: Did Adam not marry his sons to his daughters? So they did not carry out the hadd on him, and the book was taken away. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the jizyah from the Magians, and so did Abu Bakr, and I."
"301","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to me, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Ali, that he said: When the fighting grew fierce and the people met, we sought protection with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and none of us was closer to the enemy than him."
"302","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Fitr, from Mundhir Abu Yala, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, that he asked permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that if a son were born to him after him, could he name him by his name and give him his kunyah? He said: So it was a concession from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And his name was Muhammad, and his kunyah was Abu al-Qasim."
"303","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me gold rings, reciting in bowing, and qassi and saffron-dyed garments."
"304","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Ali, he said: There was no cavalryman among us on the day of Badr except al-Miqdad."
"305","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Ibn Abi Layla, my brother narrated to me, from my father, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sneezes let him say: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, in every situation, and let one say: May Allah have mercy on you, and let him say: May Allah guide you and set your affairs right."
"306","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Dili, from Abu al-Aswad, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about the nursing infant: The urine of the boy is sprinkled over, and the urine of the girl is washed. Qatadah said: This is so long as they have not eaten food; if they eat food, both are washed."
"307","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Said, he said: Waqid ibn Amr ibn Sad ibn Muadh al-Ansari informed me, that Nafi ibn Jubayr informed him, that Masud ibn al-Hakam informed him, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up then sat down, meaning for the funeral."
"308","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, he said: Water was brought to Ali and he drank standing, then said: Some people dislike drinking standing, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink standing. Then water was brought and he wiped himself with it, then said: This is the ablution of one who has not broken his purity."
"309","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr, he said: Ali said to al-Abbas: Tell the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to give you the treasurership. So al-Abbas asked him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I will give you what is better for you than that: what neither diminishes you nor you diminish it. So he gave them the watering of pilgrims."
"310","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Khalil, from Ali, he said: Al-Mughirah had a spear, and when we went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a campaign he would plant it, and people would pass by it and carry it off. He said: I said: I will surely inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of it, so he said: Then lost property would not be picked up. So I left it."
"311","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah, from Zayd ibn Ali, from his father, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at Arafah and said: This is Arafah and this is the standing place, and all of Arafah is a standing place. Then he moved on when the sun set, with Usamah riding behind him, while the people struck to his right and left, and he turned to them saying: O people, calmness is upon you. When he came to Jam he prayed the two prayers together there. In the morning he came to Quzah and stood on it and said: This is Quzah, and all of Jam is a standing place. Then he moved on, and when he came to Muhassir he spurred his camel until he crossed the valley. He stopped, then took al-Fadl behind him, then came to the Jamarah, then came to the place of sacrifice and said: This is the place of sacrifice, and all of Mina is a place of sacrifice. He said: And a young woman from Khatham asked him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, my father is a very old man who has become senile, and the obligation of Hajj has reached him; will it suffice if I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father. And he twisted the neck of al-Fadl, and al-Abbas said to him: O Messenger of Allah, why did you twist the neck of your cousin? He said: I saw a young man and a young woman and I did not feel safe from Satan for them. He said: And a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I stoned before shaving. He said: Shave or shorten, no harm. He said: And another came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I sacrificed before stoning. He said: Stone, no harm. He said: Then he came to the House and circumambulated it, then came to Zamzam and said: O sons of Abd al-Muttalib, your watering; were it not that people would overpower you, I would draw water with you."
"312","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Mudrik, he said: I heard Abu Zurah narrate from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from his father, he said: I heard Ali narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Angels do not enter a house in which there is an image, nor one who is junub, nor a dog."
"313","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Waqid al-Kufi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: I was a man who emitted much madhiy, so I ordered al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about madhiy, and he said: From it is ablution, and from semen is bathing."
"314","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from his father, he said - and his father was among the scribes of Ali - from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to recite while bowing, and said: O Ali, the likeness of one who does not straighten his back in his prayer is like a pregnant woman who carries, then when her delivery nears she miscarries, so she is neither pregnant nor a mother."
"315","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr, he said: I heard Abu al-Bakhtari, he said: One who heard Ali informed me, he says: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, I said: You send me while I am a young man, and I have no knowledge of much judgment? He said: So he struck my chest and said: Go, for Allah will steady your tongue and guide your heart. He said: No judgment between two people ever confounded me after that."
"316","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Asim ibn Damrah narrate from Ali that he said: Witr is not obligatory like prayer, but it is a sunnah, so do not leave it. Shubah said: And I found it written with me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed witr."
"317","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray and Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Asim ibn Damrah say: We asked Ali about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the daytime, and he said: You cannot bear that. He said: We said: Whoever among us can bear it. He said: When the sun was from here, like its position from here at Asr time, he prayed two rakahs, and when the sun was from here, like its position from here at Zuhr time, he prayed four, separating between every two rakahs with salutations upon the near angels, the prophets, and those who followed them among the prophets and messengers."
"318","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, narrating from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was gifted a suit of silk, he said: So he clothed me with it. Ali said: So I went out in it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I am not pleased for you with what I dislike for myself. He said: And he ordered me, so I cut it up among my women as headscarves: for Fatimah, and his aunt."
"319","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray and Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Ala, from Abu Jamilah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a slave girl who had committed adultery, and said: Carry out the hadd on her. I found her in her blood, not yet recovered from childbirth. So I came to him and mentioned that to him, and he said: When she recovers from her childbirth and becomes pure, carry out the hadd on her. He said: Then he said: Carry out the hadd upon those whom your right hands possess."
"320","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Aban ibn Salih narrated to me, from Ikrimah, he said: I was raised with al-Husayn ibn Ali from Muzdalifah, and I kept hearing him say: Labbayk, labbayk, until he reached the Jamarah. So I said to him: What is this talbiyah, O Abu Abdullah? He said: I heard my father Ali ibn Abi Talib recite talbiyah until he reached the Jamarah, and he narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited talbiyah until he reached it. He said: So I went back to Ibn Abbas and informed him of Husayn's saying, and he said: He spoke the truth. He said: And my brother al-Fadl ibn Abbas informed me, and he was the riding companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He recited talbiyah until he reached the Jamarah."
"321","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed witr at every part of the night: its beginning, its middle, and its end, and his witr ended at the end of the night."
"322","Ubaydullah narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Saib, from Asbagh ibn Nubatah, from Ali, that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made peace with Banu Taghlib on condition they remain upon their religion and not Christianize their children, but they broke it; and if my rule is completed, I will kill the fighters and take the offspring captive."
"323","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Khaythamah, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, he said: Ali said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will come out at the end of time a people young in age, foolish in minds, speaking from the best speech of creation, reciting the Quran but it does not pass their throats. When you meet them, kill them, for in killing them there is a reward with Allah on the Day of Resurrection for whoever kills them."
"324","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi al-Sabah, from Abu Aflah al-Hamdani, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, he said: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took gold in his right hand and silk in his left and said: These two are forbidden for the males of my ummah."
"325","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: Ali gave a sermon and said: O people, carry out the hadd upon your slaves, those of them who are married and those who are not, for a slave girl of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) committed adultery, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to flog her. I came to her and she had recently given birth, so I feared if I flogged her she would die. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he said: You did well."
"326","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, a sheikh from Kufa called Abu al-Muhayyah al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Abu Matar narrated to me, that Ali came to the sellers of clothes and said to a man: Sell me a shirt for three dirhams. He gave him a garment, and he wore it from his ankle to his wrist. When he wore it he said: Praise be to Allah who clothed me from clothing with what I cover my private parts with and beautify myself with among people. Then he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore a garment, he said like this."
"327","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, this sheikh Abu al-Muhayyah al-Taymi also narrated to us, he said: Abu Matar said: I saw Ali when a man was brought to him, and they said: He stole a camel. He said: I do not see you stole. He said: Yes. He said: Perhaps it was confused for you? He said: Yes, I stole. He said: Take him, O Qanbar, tie his finger, kindle a fire, call the butcher to cut it, then wait until I come. When he came he said to him: Did you steal? He said: No. So he let him go. They said: O Commander of the Believers, why did you let him go when he confessed to you? He said: I took him by his word and I let him go by his word. Then Ali said: A man who had stolen was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered his cutting, then he wept. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you weep? He said: How can I not weep when my ummah is mutilated before you? They said: O Messenger of Allah, would you not pardon him? He said: That is an evil ruler who pardons hadd punishments, but pardon one another among yourselves."
"328","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn narrated to me, from his father, he said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me gold rings, wearing qassi and saffron-dyed garments, reciting the Quran while bowing, and he clothed me with a striped silk suit. I went out in it, and when he saw it on me he said: I did not clothe you with it to wear it. He said: So I returned and gave Fatimah a part of it as if she folds it with me. He said: So I split it in two. She said: May your hands be dusty, what have you done? I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me wearing it, so wear it and clothe your women with it."
"329","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I found with the hilt of the sword of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a tied sheet: The most hostile of people to Allah are the killer of one other than his killer, the striker of one other than his striker, and whoever denies the favor of his masters has disowned what Allah sent down upon Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"330","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yazid Abu Khalid al-Baysari narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not expose your thigh, and do not look at the thigh of the living or the dead."
"331","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman al-Bakrawi narrated to us, al-Kalbi narrated to us, from al-Asbagh ibn Nubatah, from Ali, he said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) make peace with the Christians of Banu Taghlib on condition they not Christianize their children; if they do, the covenant is void from them. He said: So Ali said: By Allah they have done it, so by Allah, if my rule is completed, I will surely kill their fighters and take their offspring captive."
"332","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Said, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujayyah ibn Adi, he said: I asked Ali about the cow, and he said: For seven. He said: The one with broken horn? He said: No harm. He said: The lame? He said: If it reaches the place of sacrifice. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to inspect the eye and ear."
"333","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Duha."
"334","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said and Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Said, from Abu Ishaq - Yahya said in his hadith: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Khalil, from Ali; and Abd al-Rahman said: from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Khalil, from Ali, he said: I heard a man seeking forgiveness for his parents though they were polytheists, so I spoke to him, and he said: Did Ibrahim not seek forgiveness for his father? He said: So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, then Allah sent down: And the seeking of forgiveness of Ibrahim for his father was only because of a promise he had made to him."
"335","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Umayr ibn Said, from Ali, he said: I would never carry out a hadd on anyone and he dies and I feel regret in myself, except the drinker of wine, for if he died I would pay his blood money; because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not establish it as sunnah."
"336","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abidah, he said: Ali mentioned the people of Nahrawan and said: Among them is a man with a deformed hand, or a small-handed man; were it not that you would become arrogant, I would tell you what Allah promised those who kill them upon the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I said: Did you hear it yourself? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kabah."
"337","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Qays ibn Abbad, he said: I went to Ali, I and a man. He said: So I said to him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrust to you something he did not entrust to anyone? He said: No, except what is in this sheath of mine. He said: So he brought out a book, and in that book of his was: The believers, their blood is equal, the lowest of them strives to grant their protection, and they are a hand against others; no believer is killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant while in his covenant; whoever introduces an innovation or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"338","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, he said: A funeral passed by Ali, and people stood. He said: What is this? They said: Abu Musa. So Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood only once, then did not stand."
"339","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Abu Awn, from Abu Salih al-Hanafi, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me on the day of Badr, and to Abu Bakr: With one of you is Jibril, and with the other is Mikail, and Israfil is a mighty angel witnessing the fighting, or being in the fighting."
"340","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abdullah ibn Sabu, he said: It was said to Ali: Will you not appoint a successor? He said: No, but I leave you to what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left you to."
"341","Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Ghundar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, he said: Ali and Uthman gathered, and Uthman used to forbid mutah, or umrah, so Ali said: What do you want with a matter the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did, forbidding it? So Uthman said: Leave us from you. He said: I cannot leave you. He said: When Ali saw that, he entered ihram for both together."
"342","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Masudi informed us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-Hayyaj, he said: Ali said: I send you on what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on: Do not leave a grave except you level it, nor a statue except you efface it."
"343","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Musab ibn Sad, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Ali ibn Abi Talib behind in the campaign of Tabuk, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, do you leave me behind with the women and children? He said: Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me?"
"344","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us until he placed his foot between me and Fatimah, and taught us what to say when we take our beds: thirty-three tasbih, thirty-three tahmid, and thirty-four takbir. He said: Ali said: So I never left it afterwards. A man said to him: Not even the night of Siffin? He said: Not even the night of Siffin."
"345","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, he said: I used to think the inner part of the feet was more deserving of wiping than the outer, until I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe their outer part."
"346","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Mutarrif narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah would not pray a prayer except he prayed two rakahs after it."
"347","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - nothing prevented him from reciting the Quran except being junub."
"348","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Muslim al-Batin, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, he said: We were traveling with Uthman ibn Affan, and he heard a man reciting talbiyah for both together, so he said: Who is this? He said: Ali. So he came to him and said: Did you not know I forbade this? He said: Yes, but I will not leave the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for your saying."
"349","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, that Ali said to Abu al-Hayyaj: I send you on what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on: Do not leave an elevated grave except you level it, nor a statue except you efface it."
"350","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Nuaym ibn Hakim, from Abu Maryam, from Ali, he said: The wife of al-Walid ibn Uqbah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Al-Walid beats me. He said: Say to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has granted me protection. Ali said: She stayed only a short while until she returned and said: He only beat me more. So he took a fringe from his garment and gave it to her and said: Say to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has granted me protection. She stayed only a short while until she returned to him and said: He only beat me more. So he raised his hands and said: O Allah, deal with al-Walid."
"351","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant does not believe until he believes in four: in resurrection after death, and believes in qadar."
"352","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from al-Mundhir ibn Thalabah, from Ilba ibn Ahmar, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib said: I proposed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his daughter Fatimah. He said: So Ali sold his armor and some of what he sold of his goods, and it reached four hundred and eighty dirhams. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that two-thirds be put into perfume, and one-third into clothes, and he spat into a jar of water and ordered them to wash with it. He said: And he ordered her not to precede him in nursing her child. He said: So she preceded him in nursing al-Husayn; as for al-Hasan, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did something in his mouth, we do not know what it was, so he was the more knowledgeable of the two men."
"353","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to us, Abu Hazim narrated to us, Sahl ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will surely give the banner tomorrow to a man through whose hands Allah will grant victory. He said: So the people went in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), each hoping he would give him the banner. He said: Where is Ali ibn Abi Talib? They said: He has sore eyes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Call him. He was brought, and he spat in his eye and supplicated for him, and he healed. Then he gave him the banner. Then he said: Call Ali. He came. Then he said: O Ali, do not turn back until you descend upon the people and call them. He said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I fight them until they say: There is no god but Allah? He said: At your leisure; when you come to them, call them to Allah, for by Allah, that one man accept Islam through your hands is better for you than red camels."
"354","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Yazid al-Rishk narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment and appointed Ali ibn Abi Talib over them. He said to him: O Ali, the detachment. Imran said: When the Muslims returned from a campaign, they would come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before going to their homes and inform him of their journey. He said: So Ali took a slave girl, and four men conspired, and they informed him of their journey. One of the four stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, and Ali took a slave girl. He turned away from him. Then the second stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, Ali did such and such. He turned away from him. Then the third stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, Ali did such and such. He turned away from him. Then the fourth stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, Ali did such and such. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to them angry, anger known on his face, and said: What do you want from Ali? Ali is from me and I am from him, and he is the guardian of every believer after me."
"355","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, that his father prepared a meal for Uthman ibn Affan at Qudayd, and tharid was brought with that partridge upon it. He said to the people: Eat, for it was caught on my account. He said: So the people said: This is Ali, he forbade us eating it. So he sent to Ali, and he came while wiping khabat leaves from his hands. Uthman said to him: Eat it. He said, meaning Ali: I adjure by Allah a man who witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the Bedouin came with a leg of wild donkey, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it and said: Go to the people in hill, for we are in ihram, or as he said. So some people stood and testified. Then he said: I adjure by Allah - or he said: I remind by Allah - a man who witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the Bedouin came with ostrich eggs, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take it to the people in hill, for we are a people in ihram. So some people stood and testified. Then Uthman turned his leg and entered his house, and the people left the food, and the people in hill came and ate it."
"356","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, my father informed me, al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating every fanged beast of prey, and every taloned bird, and the price of carrion, and wine, domestic donkeys, the earnings of the prostitute, and the stud fee of every stallion."
"357","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Shabab narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hakim narrated to me, Abu Maryam narrated to me, Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A people will pass out of Islam as the arrow passes out of the game, reciting the Quran but it does not pass their throats. Blessed is whoever kills them and they kill him. Their sign is a man with a deformed hand."
"358","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Fudayl narrated to us, from Abu Hariz, from al-Shabi, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when I returned from a funeral something I would not love to have the whole world for."
"359","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr, from Ali ibn Abi Talib: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman together with her paternal aunt, or with her maternal aunt."
"360","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man inherits his full brother, to the exclusion of his paternal brothers."
"361","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hasan narrated to us, from Bayan, from Husayn ibn Safwan, from Ali, he said: I was a boy who emitted much madhiy, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the water had harmed me, he said: Bathing is only from gushing water."
"362","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Shurhabil ibn Mudrik informed us, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from his father, that he traveled with Ali, and he was the keeper of his purification water. When he came parallel to Nineveh while going to Siffin, Ali called: Be patient, Abu Abdullah, be patient, Abu Abdullah, at the bank of the Euphrates. I said: And what, O Abu Abdullah? He said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day while his eyes overflowed. He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, has someone angered you? What is with your eyes overflowing? He said: Rather Jibril stood from with me just now, and told me that al-Husayn will be killed at the bank of the Euphrates. He said: So he said: Would you like me to let you smell some of his soil? He said: I said: Yes. He said: So he stretched his hand and took a handful of soil and gave it to me, and I could not hold my eyes back from overflowing."
"363","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Maymun, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah, the judge of Rayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: I heard Amir al-Muminin Ali say: I gathered, I and Fatimah, al-Abbas, and Zayd ibn Harithah. Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, my age has grown, my bones have thinned, and my dependents have increased; if you think, O Messenger of Allah, to order for me such-and-such wasqs of food, then do. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have done it. Fatimah said: O Messenger of Allah, if you think to order for me as you ordered, then do. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have done that. Zayd ibn Harithah said: O Messenger of Allah, you had given me land my livelihood was from, then you took it from me; if you think to return it to me, then do. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have done that. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, if you think to entrust to me this right Allah has made for us in His Book in this fifth, so I distribute it in your lifetime and no one disputes me after you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have done that. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted it to me, and I distributed it in his lifetime. Then Abu Bakr entrusted it to me, and I distributed it in his lifetime. Then Umar entrusted it to me, and I distributed it in his lifetime, until the last year of Umar's years, and much wealth came to him, and he set aside a fifth, then sent and said: O Ali, this is your right, take it. I said: O Commander of the Believers, this year we are free of need of it, and the Muslims need it, so return it to them. So Umar returned it that year. Then no one called me to it after Umar, until I stood in this station of mine. Then al-Abbas met me and said: O Ali, you have today taken from us something that will never be returned to us."
"364","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Aidh ibn Habib narrated to us, Amir ibn al-Simt narrated to me, from Abu al-Gharif, he said: Ablution water was brought to Ali, so he rinsed his mouth and nose three times, then washed his face three times, and washed his hands and arms three times each, then wiped his head, and washed his feet. Then he said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution. Then he recited something from the Quran, then said: Thus for one who is not junub; as for the junub, then no, by Allah."
"365","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, Hakim ibn Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from his father, from his grandfather Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and Fatimah at night and woke us for prayer. He said: Then he returned to his house and prayed part of the night, and we heard no sound from him. He said: So he returned to us and woke us and said: Stand and pray. He said: So I sat while rubbing my eyes, saying: By Allah, we pray only what Allah has written for us; our souls are in Allah's hand, and if He wills to send us He sends us. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away, saying while striking his thigh: We pray only what is written for us, we pray only what Allah has written for us. He said it twice: And man is most argumentative of things."
"366","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, and Muhammad ibn Kab mentioned, from al-Harith ibn Abdullah al-Awar, from Ali, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Jibril came to me and said: O Muhammad, your ummah will differ after you. So I said: Where is the way out, O Jibril? He said: The Book of Allah; Allah breaks every tyrant with it, whoever holds to it is saved, whoever leaves it perishes. It is decisive speech, not jest. Tongues do not wear it out, it is not exhausted by much repetition, its wonders do not end. In it is news of those before you, and tidings of what will be after you."
"367","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abd al-Malik, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, he said: I prayed Zuhr with Ali, then he went to a sitting place he used to sit in Madinah. He sat and we sat around him until Asr came. Water was brought in a vessel, and he took a handful from it, rinsed his mouth, then sniffed, wiped his face and arms, wiped his head, wiped his feet, then stood and drank the remainder of his vessel. Then he said: I was told some men dislike one of them drinking while standing, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do that. And this is the ablution of one who has not broken his purity."
"368","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from Ali, that he described the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: He had a large head, fair with redness, a great beard, large joints, coarse hands and feet. I never saw before him his like nor after him, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him abundantly."
"369","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, al-Hajjaj informed us, from Salim al-Makki, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, that he was asked about the description of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: He was neither short nor tall, with good wavy hair, redness in his face, large joints, coarse hands and feet, a large head, long chest hair. I never saw before him nor after him his like. When he walked he leaned forward as if descending a slope."
"370","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Hanash, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah sent me to a people of age while I was young, and said: When the two disputants come to you, do not listen to one until you hear from the other, for it will clarify the judgment for you. He said: So I learned, and I have been a judge ever since."
"371","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shubah, Sufyan, and Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Ali, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake his family in the last ten nights of Ramadan."
"372","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan and Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake his family in the last ten nights of Ramadan."
"373","Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Hubayrah ibn Maryam, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake his family in the last ten nights and raise the curtains."
"374","Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Mansur, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a funeral, and when we reached Baqi al-Gharqad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and we sat with him. He took a stick and scratched the ground with it, then raised his head and said: There is none of you, no living soul, except Allah knows its place in Paradise and its place in Hell, wretched or happy. He said: So a man from the people stood and said: Shall we not leave deeds and turn to our book? Whoever of us is among the happy will be eased to its deeds, and whoever is among the wretched will go to wretchedness. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather work, for each is eased; whoever is among the happy is eased to its deeds, and whoever is among the wretched is eased to its deeds."
"375","Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi, from a man of Banu Asad, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four things; a man will not taste faith until he believes in them: that there is no god but Allah alone without partner, that I am the Messenger of Allah sent with truth, that he is dead and raised after death, and he believes in all of qadar."
"376","He said: And Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Zubayd, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No obedience to anyone in disobedience to Allah."
"377","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr, and Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, they said: Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment and appointed over them a man from the Ansar, and ordered them to hear and obey. They angered him about something, so he said: Gather firewood for me. Then he said: Kindle it. So they kindled it. Then he said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not order you to hear and obey? He said: Then enter it. Some of them looked at one another and said: We only fled to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Fire. They remained so until his anger subsided and the fire was extinguished. When they returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Had they entered it, they would never have come out of it; obedience is only in what is right."
"378","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you select among Quraysh and leave us? He said: Do you have anything with you? I said: Yes, the daughter of Hamzah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She is not lawful to me; she is the daughter of my brother through nursing."
"379","Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you select among the women of Quraysh and leave us? He said: Do you have anything with you? I said: Yes, the daughter of Hamzah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She is only the daughter of my brother through nursing."
"380","Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ali, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not point you to the most beautiful girl in Quraysh? He said: And where is she? I said: The daughter of Hamzah. He said: Do you not know she is the daughter of my brother through nursing? And Allah has forbidden through nursing what He forbade through lineage."
"381","Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abu Awn, from Abu Salih al-Hanafi, he said: Ali said upon the minbar, and Ibn al-Kawwa asked him about the daughter of the brother through nursing, so Ali said: I mentioned the daughter of Hamzah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Do you not know she is the daughter of my brother through nursing?"
"382","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah Abu Awn, I heard Abu Salih say: Ali went out and said: Ask me. So Ibn al-Kawwa asked him about the daughter of the brother through nursing. So Ali said: I mentioned the daughter of Hamzah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: She is the daughter of my brother through nursing."
"383","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan al-Araj, from Abidah al-Salmani, from Ali, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the polytheists detained him on the day of al-Ahzab from Asr prayer until the sun nearly set, so he said: O Allah, fill their graves and houses with fire as they kept us from the middle prayer, until the sun nearly set."
"384","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abidah, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of al-Khandaq: They kept us from the middle prayer until the sun set; may Allah fill their houses and graves with fire."
"385","Ubaydullah ibn Umar ibn Maysarah al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of al-Khandaq: May Allah fill their houses and graves with fire as they kept us from the middle prayer. Hammad said: I do not know whether from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or from Ali? And it is Asr."
"386","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah fill their graves and hearts with fire, as they kept us from the middle prayer. He said: And it is Asr."
"387","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting on the day of al-Ahzab at an opening of the trench, and said: They kept us from the middle prayer until the sun set; may Allah fill their houses and graves - or: may Allah fill their bellies and graves - with fire."
"388","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash and Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Ali, he said: The polytheists kept us on the day of al-Ahzab from the middle prayer - the middle prayer is Asr prayer - may Allah fill their graves, houses, and bellies with fire."
"389","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim, from Zirr, he said: We ordered Abidah to ask Ali about the middle prayer. So he asked him and he said: I used to think it was Fajr prayer, until I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Ahzab say: They kept us from the middle prayer, the Asr prayer; may Allah fill their graves and bellies with fire."
"390","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Ali, that the polytheists kept the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Asr prayer until he prayed it after the two Ishas, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah fill their houses and graves with fire, as they kept us from the middle prayer."
"391","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of al-Ahzab: They kept us from the middle prayer, the Asr prayer; may Allah fill their graves, houses, and bellies with fire. Then he prayed it between the two Ishas, between Maghrib and Isha."
"392","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abidah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of al-Khandaq: May Allah fill their graves and bellies with fire, as they kept us from the middle prayer, the Asr prayer, until the sun set."
"393","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Jushami and Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, the scribe of Ali, he said: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, I and al-Zubayr and al-Miqdad, and said: Go until you come to Rawdat Khakh, for there is a woman traveler with a letter you will find with her. So we went racing until we came to the Rawdah, and there was the woman traveler. We said: Bring out the letter. She said: I have no letter. We said: You will surely bring out the letter or we will search the clothes. So she brought it out from her braids. We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and in it was: From Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah to the people of Makkah, informing them of some of the affair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Hatib and said: What is this? He said: Do not hasten against me; I was attached among Quraysh and not from themselves, and none of your companions but has in Makkah one who protects him and stays behind for his family except me. So I wanted to make a favor with them. I did not do it as disbelief nor apostasy from my religion, nor pleasure with disbelief after Islam. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He told you the truth. So Umar said: Let me, O Messenger of Allah, strike the neck of this hypocrite. So he said to him: He witnessed Badr, and what makes you know; perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do what you wish, for I have forgiven you."
"394","Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad informed me, that Ubaydullah, the scribe of Ali, informed him, that he heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah sent me, I and al-Zubayr and al-Miqdad - Sufyan said: These are the horsemen of the believers - and said: Go until you come to Rawdat Khakh. And he mentioned similar."
"395","Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, I and al-Zubayr and Abu Marthad al-Sulami, and each of us was a horseman, and said: Go until you reach Rawdat Khakh, for there is a woman with a sheet from Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah to the polytheists, so bring it to me. We found her leaning on her camel where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us. I said: Where is the letter with you? She said: I have no letter. So we made her camel kneel and searched her baggage. My two companions said: We see nothing with her. I said: We know the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not lie to us; by Him we swear by, you will surely bring it out or I will slaughter you - meaning the sword. When she saw seriousness, she reached to her waist-wrapper, upon her a woolen wrap, and brought out the letter. We brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Hatib, what carried you to what you did? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I am nothing but a believer in Allah and His Messenger, but I wanted to have a favor with the people by which Allah repels harm from my family and wealth; and none of your companions but has among his people there one by whom Allah repels harm from his family and wealth. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth, so say nothing to him but good. So Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, he has betrayed Allah, His Messenger, and the believers, so let me strike his neck. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is he not among the people of Badr? And what makes you know, O Umar; perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr: Do what you wish, for Paradise has become due for you."
"396","Ishaq ibn Ismail narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to me, from Abu Sinan, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: When the Messenger of Allah intended Makkah, he sent to some of his companions that he intended Makkah, among them Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah, and it spread among the people that he intended Hunayn. He said: So Hatib wrote to the people of Makkah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intends you. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, I and Abu Marthad, and there was no man with us but with him a horse, and said: Go to Rawdat Khakh, for you will meet there a woman with a letter, so take it from her. He said: So we went until we saw her in the place the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned. We said to her: Bring the letter. She said: I have no letter. He said: So we put down her goods and searched her, and found nothing in her goods. Abu Marthad said: Perhaps there is no letter with her. We said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not lied to, nor did we lie. So we said to her: You will surely bring it out or we will strip you. She said: Do you not fear Allah? Are you not Muslims? We said: You will surely bring it out or we will strip you. Amr ibn Murrah said: So she brought it out from her waist-wrapper - and Habib ibn Abi Thabit said: And she brought it out from her front - So we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the letter was from Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah. So Umar stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, he betrayed Allah, he betrayed His Messenger; permit me to strike his neck. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did he not witness Badr? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. Umar said: Yes, but he broke faith and aided your enemies against you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do what you wish. So Umar's eyes overflowed, and he said: Allah and His Messenger know best. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Hatib and said: What carried you to what you did? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I was a man attached among Quraysh, and my family and wealth were there, and none of your companions but has in Makkah one who protects his family and wealth. So I wrote to them of that. By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I am a believer in Allah and His Messenger. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hatib spoke the truth, so say nothing to Hatib but good. Habib said: So Allah sent down: O you who believe, do not take My enemy and your enemy as allies, extending to them affection."
"397","Zuhayr Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad informed him, that Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi informed him, that Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, and al-Miqdad and al-Zubayr, to Rawdat Khakh, and said: There is a woman there with a letter. He said: So we went with our horses racing, and we came upon the woman. We said: You will surely bring out the letter or we will search the clothes. He said: So she brought out from the braids of her hair a letter, and in it was from Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah to the people of Makkah, informing them of some of the affair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this, O Hatib? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not write it as apostasy from my religion, and he excused himself with something - meaning that he was a stranger there or like this - So Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, let me strike the neck of this hypocrite. He said: And what makes you know, O Umar? Perhaps Allah looked to the people of Badr and said: Do what you wish, for I have forgiven you."
"398","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Minhal, from Abbad ibn Abdullah - or Abdullah ibn Abbad - from Ali, he said: He ascended the minbar on Friday and gave a sermon, then al-Ashath stood to him and said: This red one has overcome you. He said: Who will excuse me from these fat ones? One of them stays behind turning on his bedding, while these come early to the remembrance of Allah. If I drive them away, I would then be among the wrongdoers. By Allah, I heard him say: They will surely strike you upon religion in return, as you struck them upon it at first."
"399","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ubaydullah al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Ali ibn Alqamah al-Anmari, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: When was sent down: O you who believe, when you consult the Messenger, offer charity before your consultation, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What do you think? A dinar? He said: I said: They cannot bear it. He said: Then how much? I said: A barley grain. He said: You are indeed abstemious. He said: Then was sent down: Are you afraid to offer charities before your consultation? He said: So by it Allah lightened upon this ummah."
"400","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, while I was young, with no knowledge of judgment. He said: So he struck my chest and said: Allah will guide your heart and steady your tongue. He said: So I never doubted a judgment between two after that."
"401","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mujalid ibn Said, from al-Shabi, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of riba, its giver, its two witnesses, its writer, the tattooer, the tattooed, the muhallil and the one for whom it is done, and the withholder of charity. And he forbade wailing, and he did not say: cursed."
"402","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani ibn Hani, from Ali, he said: Ammar came seeking permission upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Permit him; welcome to the pure, the purified."
"403","Al-Muqaddami and al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, they said: Aththam ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani ibn Hani, he said: We were sitting with Ali, and Ammar entered. He said: Welcome to the pure, the purified; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Ammar is filled with faith to his bones."
"404","Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala al-Hamdani narrated to us, Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani ibn Abi Hani, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled the daughter of Hamzah for her maternal aunt, and said: The maternal aunt is like the mother. And Ali, Jafar, and Zayd disputed about her."
"405","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, he said: I entered upon Ali ibn Abi Talib, I and two men: a man from my people, and a man from Banu Asad, I think. He sent them off and said: You two are strong men, so strive for your religion. Then he entered the lavatory and relieved himself, then came out, took a handful of water and wiped himself with it, then began reciting the Quran. He said: As if he saw we disapproved of that. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would relieve himself, then come out and recite the Quran, and eat meat with us; nothing prevented him from reciting the Quran, except janabah."
"406","Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, similarly; I memorized it and did not find it afterwards."
"407","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Salamah, he said: I entered upon Ali, I and two men: a man from us, and a man from Banu Asad, I think. He sent them off and said: You two are strong men, so strive for your religion. Then he entered the lavatory, then came out, took a handful of water and wiped himself with it, then came reciting the Quran. He saw we disapproved of that, so Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go to the privy and relieve himself, then come out and eat bread and meat with us; nothing kept him from the Quran - and perhaps he said: nothing barred him - except janabah, or the funeral."
"408","Bundar Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: I was ill, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I said: O Allah, if my term has come, give me rest; if it is delayed, raise me; if it is affliction, make me patient. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: How did you say? He repeated it to him. So he struck him with his foot and said: O Allah, grant him health, O Allah, heal him. He said: So I never complained of my pain after that."
"409","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Ali, he said: I was ill, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I said - similarly."
"410","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan and Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Wahb ibn al-Ajda, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not pray after Asr except you pray while the sun is high."
"411","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Ali, he said: When the fighting came on the day of Badr, we sought protection with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was among the fiercest of people; there was no one. He said: And there was no one closer to the polytheists than him."
"412","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibrahim ibn Hunayn, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to recite while bowing, and from wearing qassi, and gold rings."
"413","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed me, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from his father, that he heard Ali ibn Abi Talib in the courtyard of Kufa say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me - and I do not say he forbade you - from wearing qassi and saffron-dyed garments, from gold rings, and from reciting the Quran while bowing."
"414","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from his father, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me gold rings, wearing qassi, reciting in bowing and prostration, and wearing saffron-dyed garments."
"415","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, al-Numan ibn Sad narrated to me, he said: We were with Ali, and a man asked him: Shall I recite in bowing or prostration? He said: Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am forbidden to recite in bowing or prostration; when you bow, glorify Allah, and when you prostrate, strive in supplication, for it is fitting you be answered."
"416","Masruq narrated to us, Ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Sulayman ibn Suhaym, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Mabad, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"417","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ali, say: O Allah, guide me and make me straight; and recall with guidance Your guiding the path, and recall with straightness Your straightening the arrow. He said: And he forbade me to put the ring on the forefinger and middle finger, and forbade me qassiyyah and mitharah. Abu Burdah said: So we said to Ali: What is qassiyyah? He said: Clothes of Sham and Egypt, striped, with patterns like citrons. He said: And mitharah: something women used to make for their husbands, like blankets."
"418","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Abu Burdah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to put the ring on this, or on this, meaning the forefinger and middle finger."
"419","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn narrated to me, from his father, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me gold rings, reciting in bowing and prostration, and wearing saffron-dyed garments."
"420","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to recite the Quran while bowing, and said: When you bow, glorify Allah, and when you prostrate, supplicate to Allah, for it is fitting you be answered."
"421","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, he said: I heard Ali say: I never heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) join his parents for anyone, except Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, for I heard him say on the day of Uhud: Shoot, may my father and mother be ransom for you."
"422","Abd al-Rahman ibn Sallam narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Najiyah ibn Kab, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: When Abu Talib died, I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your old misguided uncle has died. He said: Go and bury him, and do not do anything until you come to me. So I did what he ordered me, then came to him. He said to me: Wash, and he taught me supplications dearer to me than red camels."
"423","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yazid al-Asamm narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Suddi say: from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, he said: When Abu Talib died, I came to the Prophet and said: Your old uncle has died. He said: Go and bury him, and do not do anything until you come to me. He said: So I buried him, then came to him. He said: Go and wash, and do not do anything until you come to me. He said: So I washed, then came to him, and he supplicated for me with supplications I would not be pleased to have red or black camels for. He said: And Ali, when he washed a dead person, would wash himself."
"424","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my ummah in its early mornings."
"425","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Numan ibn Sad, he said: A man came to Ali and said: O Commander of the Believers, tell me of a month I fast after Ramadan. He said: So he said: You asked me about something I never heard anyone ask about after a man I heard ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said to him: If you fast a month after Ramadan, fast al-Muharram, for it is the month of Allah, and in it is a day Allah turned to a people, and will turn to others in it."
"426","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a month I fast after Ramadan. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you fast a month after Ramadan, fast al-Muharram, for it is the month of Allah, and in it is a day Allah turned to a people and will turn to others in it."
"427","Surayj ibn Yunus Abu al-Harith narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Sad, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there are chambers whose insides are seen from their outsides, and their outsides from their insides. An Arab Bedouin said: For whom are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: For whoever speaks good words, feeds food, spreads peace, and prays at night while people sleep."
"428","And with it, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah said: In Paradise there is a market with no buying or selling except images of men and women; when a man desires an image he enters it. He said: And in it is a gathering of wide-eyed maidens. He said: They raise voices the creation never heard the like of. He said: They say: We are the eternal, we never perish; we are the blissful, we never suffer; we are the pleased, we never anger. Blessed is whoever is for us and we are for him."
"429","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Thalabah ibn Yazid al-Sadi, he said: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Safar, no Hamah, and a healthy one does not infect a sick one. He said: So I said: Did you hear it yourself? He said: Yes, my ears heard it and my eyes saw it."
"430","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah and Ibn Numayr informed us, they said: al-Walid ibn Uqbah narrated to us - Uthman al-Shaybani said, Hamzah al-Zayyat narrated to us - from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Thalabah, in the hadith of Uthman al-Himmani, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Safar, no Hamah, and a healthy one does not infect a sick one."
"431","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, that his father took charge of Uthman's food. My father said: As if I look at the partridges around the bowls. A man came and said to Uthman: Ali dislikes this. So he sent to Ali, and he came with his arms stained from beating leaves. He said: You oppose us much. So Ali said: I remind by Allah a man who witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the hind of a wild donkey was gifted to him, and he said: We are in ihram, so feed it to the people in hill. So men stood and testified. So Ali said: I remind by Allah a man who witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when five ostrich eggs were gifted, and he said: We are in ihram, so feed it to the people in hill. So men stood and testified. So Uthman stood, entered his tent, the people departed, and left the food for the people of the water."
"432","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Imran ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from his father, from Abd al-Karim, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Abbas, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: Game meat was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram, and he did not eat it."
"433","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, he said: I witnessed Ali and Uthman between Makkah and Madinah, and Uthman forbade mutah and did not combine both. When Ali saw that, he entered ihram for both. He said: Labbayk with umrah and Hajj together. So Uthman said: Do you see me forbid people and you do it? So Ali said: I would not leave the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the saying of any man."
"434","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim owes the Muslim six courtesies: He greets him when he meets him, answers him when he invites him, says mercy upon him when he sneezes, visits him when ill, follows his funeral when he dies, and loves for him what he loves for himself."
"435","Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala al-Hamdani narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Hisham, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ali, that he prepared food and invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He came and saw in the house a curtain with images, so he returned. He said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, what turned you back, may my father and mother be ransom for you? He said: In the house is a curtain with images, and angels do not enter a house in which there are images."
"436","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abu 'Awn al-Thaqafi, from Abu Salih al-Hanafi, from 'Ali: that Ukaydir of Duma gifted a garment of silk to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he gave it to 'Ali, and said: Tear it into headscarves among the Fatimas."
"437","'Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed in Paradise there are chambers whose outsides are seen from their insides and whose insides are seen from their outsides. A Bedouin said: For whom are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: For whoever feeds food, spreads peace, and prays at night while people sleep."
"438","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Kufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi Yazid al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Supplication is the weapon of the believer, the pillar of the religion, and the light of the heavens and the earth."
"439","'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Bishr ibn Mansur al-Sulaymi narrated to us, from al-Khalil ibn Murra, from al-Furat ibn Salman, who said: 'Ali said: Will not one of you stand and pray four rak'as before 'Asr, and say in them what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Your light is perfected so You guided, so to You is praise; Your forbearance is great so You pardoned, so to You is praise; You extended Your hand so You gave, so to You is praise; our Lord, Your face is the noblest of faces, Your station the greatest of stations, Your gift the best and most pleasant of gifts; You are obeyed, our Lord, so You give thanks, and You are disobeyed, our Lord, so You forgive; You answer the distressed, remove harm, heal the sick, forgive sin, accept repentance; none can repay Your blessings, and no speaker's words can reach Your praise."
"440","'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Khalid narrated to us, who said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Fadl narrated to me, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It suffices for a passing group that one of them gives greeting, and it suffices for those sitting that one of them returns it."
"441","'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting the month of patience and three days of every month is the fast of a lifetime, and it removes the rancor of the chest."
"442","Bundar Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayra, from 'Ali: that a suit of silk was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So he clothed me with it. 'Ali said: So I went out in it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am not pleased for you with what I dislike for myself. So he ordered me, and I tore it between my women: Fatima and his aunt."
"443","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Sa'd, from Nasr ibn 'Asim: that 'Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took jizya from the Magians, and Abu Bakr, and I."
"444","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Humayd al-Kufi narrated to me, from Abu al-Jarud, from al-Harith al-Hamdani, who said: I saw 'Ali come until he ascended, praised and extolled Him, then said: A decree decreed by Allah upon the tongue of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the unlettered Prophet: that none loves me except a believer, and none hates me except a hypocrite, and he who fabricates has failed. He said: Al-Nadr said: And 'Ali said: I am the brother of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his cousin; none will say it after me."
"445","Abu Hisham and 'Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, both saying: Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from Muslim, from Habba, from 'Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent on Monday, and I became Muslim on Tuesday."
"446","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Ajlah narrated to us, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Habba ibn Juwayn, from 'Ali who said: I know no one of this umma after its Prophet who worshipped Allah before me; I worshipped Him before anyone of them worshipped Him, five years or seven years."
"447","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from 'Ali, who said: We have nothing except the Book of Allah and this — meaning the sheet — from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and he mentioned the hadith."
"448","Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, Harun ibn Salih al-Hamdani narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu al-Jallas, who said: I heard 'Ali saying to 'Abdullah al-Saba'i: Woe to you; by Allah, he did not confide to me anything he concealed from any of the people, and I heard him say: Before the Hour there will be thirty liars, and you are one of them."
"449","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, with its chain, the like of it."
"450","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyayna narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi; Abu Juhayfa informed me, who said: I said to 'Ali: Do you have anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besides the Book of Allah? He said: No, by the One who split the seed and created the soul; we have nothing besides the Book of Allah, except that Allah grants a man understanding of this Qur'an, and what is in this sheet. He said: Blood-money, freeing the captive, and no Muslim is killed for a disbeliever."
"451","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyayna narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Uthay' — Zuhayr said: so he said Zayd ibn Uthay', but it is really Ibn Yuthay' — who said: We asked 'Ali: With what were you sent? He said: I was sent with four: that no naked person shall circumambulate the House, no polytheist shall enter the Sanctuary, whoever had a covenant with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) it stands until its term, whoever has no covenant has a respite of four months, and none shall enter Paradise except a believing soul."
"452","Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sallam and Mahmud ibn Khidash and others narrated to us, saying: Marwan ibn Mu'awiya al-Fazari narrated to us, from al-Azhar ibn Rashid al-Kahili — and in Mahmud's hadith: al-Azhar ibn Rashid narrated to us — from al-Khadir ibn al-Qawwas, from Abu Sukhayla, who said: 'Ali said to us: Shall I not inform you. And in the hadith of al-Jumahi 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sukhayla, from 'Ali, that he said: Shall I not inform you of the best verse in the Book of Allah, which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me? He said: {And whatever calamity befalls you is because of what your hands earned, and He pardons much}. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I shall explain it to you, O 'Ali: whatever befalls you in this world of affliction, illness, or punishment, Allah is more generous than to repeat the punishment upon you in the Hereafter; and whatever He pardoned in this world, Allah is more forbearing than to return after His pardon."
"453","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated to us, from Abu Hashim, the keeper of the pomegranates, from Zadham, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: We entered with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon a man of the Ansar who had swollen, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you not open it for him? He said: So it was lanced while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present."
"454","Shayban narrated to us, Masrur ibn Sa'id al-Tamimi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman al-Awza'i narrated to us, from 'Urwa ibn Ruwaym, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Honor your aunt the date-palm, for it was created from the clay from which Adam was created, and no tree other than it is pollinated. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feed your women who have given birth fresh dates; if there are no fresh dates, then dry dates; and no tree is nobler to Allah than the tree beneath which Maryam daughter of 'Imran descended."
"455","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyayna narrated to us — 'Amr heard 'Ata', from 'A'ish ibn Anas — he heard 'Ali addressing the people on the pulpit. I said to 'Ammar: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me about madhi, for his daughter is under me and I am shy to ask him. So he asked him, and he said: When he finds that, let him perform ablution."
"456","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about madhi? He said: For it is ablution, and he washes it; and for semen is the bath."
"457","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Mundhir, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyya, from 'Ali, who said: He was a man who emitted much madhi, so he was shy to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about madhi. He said: So he said to al-Miqdad: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about madhi. He said: So he asked him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For it is ablution."
"458","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu al-Hasna', from al-Hakam, from Hanash, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to sacrifice on his behalf two rams, so I love to do it."
"459","Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with nine suras: in the first rak'a {Rivalry in increase distracted you}, {Indeed We sent it down in the Night of Decree}, and {When the earth is shaken}; in the second: al-'Asr, {When the help of Allah comes and the conquest}, and {Indeed We gave you al-Kawthar}; and in the third {Say: O disbelievers}, {Perish}, and {Say: He is Allah, One}."
"460","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hakim ibn Hakim ibn 'Abbad ibn Hunayf, from Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam, from his mother, that she narrated to him, saying: As if I look at 'Ali upon the gray mule of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the ravine of the Ansar, saying: O people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These are not days of fasting; they are days of eating and drinking, the days of Mina."
"461","Abu Bakr narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq — Aban ibn Salih narrated to me — from 'Ikrima, who said: I set out with Husayn ibn 'Ali from Muzdalifa, and I kept hearing him say: Labbayk, labbayk, until he reached the Jamra. I said to him: What is this talbiya, O Abu 'Abdullah? He said: I heard my father 'Ali ibn Abi Talib reciting talbiya until when he reached the Jamra; and he narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited talbiya until he reached it."
"462","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Aban ibn 'Abdullah al-Bajali, who said: 'Amr, nephew of 'Ilba', narrated to me, from 'Ilba', from 'Ali, who said: 'Ali said: The charity camels passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he took a hair from the back of a camel and said: I have no more right to this hair than any man of the Muslims."
"463","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn 'Ali, from his father, from his grandfather: that 'Ali would travel until when the sun set and it darkened, he alighted and prayed Maghrib, then ate dinner, then prayed 'Isha right after it, then say: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"464","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Dawud 'Umar ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yasin, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from his father, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Mahdi is of you, the People of the House; Allah will set him right in a night."
"465","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Jabir, from 'Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from 'Ali, who said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he slept, and we mentioned the Dajjal, and he woke with his face red, and said: Other than the Dajjal, what I fear for you more than the Dajjal: misguiding imams."
"466","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu Kudayna narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Minhal, from Nu'aym ibn Dajaja, who said: I was sitting with 'Ali when Abu Mas'ud came to him. 'Ali said: Farrukh has come. He sat, and 'Ali said: You give fatwa to people? He said: Yes, and I tell them the Hereafter is evil. He said: Then tell me, did you hear anything from him? He said: Yes, I heard him say: No year of a hundred comes upon people with an eye blinking on earth. 'Ali said: Your backside missed the pit, and you erred in the beginning of your fatwa; he said that only to those present that day; is relief except after the hundred?"
"467","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Mindal narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam, from Asma' bint 'Abis, from her father, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The miscarried fetus contends with his Lord if He admits his parents to the Fire, until it is said to him: O miscarried one contending with his Lord, return, for I have admitted your parents to Paradise. He said: So he drags them by his cord until he admits them to Paradise."
"468","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Ibrahim, of the offspring of Dhu al-Janahayn, narrated to us, who said: 'Ali ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ali ibn Husayn: that he saw a man coming to a gap near the grave of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), entering it and supplicating, so he forbade him, and said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from my father, from my grandfather, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not take my grave as a festival, nor your houses as graves; your greeting reaches me wherever you are."
"469","Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, al-'Abbas ibn Ja'far ibn Zayd ibn Talq informed me, from his father, from his grandfather, from 'Ali, who said: When I married Fatima, I said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall I sell; my horse or my armor? He said: Sell your armor. So I sold it for twelve uqiyyas, and that was Fatima's dowry."
"470","'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn Aban and Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali who said: On the night Fatima was brought to me, we had nothing to sleep on except a ram's skin."
"471","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba and Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us — and this is the wording of Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, who said: I was sitting with 'Ali while he was engaged in some affair of the people, when a man in travel clothes came to him and said: O Commander of the Believers. But what 'Ali was engaged in of the people's affair kept him busy. He said: I... So I said: What is your matter? He said: He said: I was a pilgrim or performing 'umra — he said: I do not know which of the two he said — and I passed by 'A'isha, and she said: Who are these people who came out before you called al-Haruriyya? He said: I said: In a place called Harura'. He said: So they were named al-Haruriyya for that. He said: So she said: Blessed is he who witnessed their destruction. She said: By Allah, if you asked Ibn Abi Talib he would inform you of their affair. So from there I came to ask him about that. He said: And 'Ali finished and said: Where is the one seeking permission? He stood before him and related to him the like of what he related to me. He said: So 'Ali said the tahlil three times, then said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with none present except 'A'isha. He said: So he said to me: O 'Ali, how will you be with a people who come out in such-and-such place — and he gestured with his hand toward the east — reciting the Qur'an not passing their throats — or: their collarbones — passing through Islam as the arrow passes through the game; among them a man with a defective arm, as if his hand were the breast of an Abyssinian woman. Then he said: I adjure you by Allah besides whom there is no god, did I narrate to you that he is among them? They said: Yes. So you went and sought him, then brought him dragging as I described to you. He said: Then he said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth, three times."
"472","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Siyahi narrated to us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, who said: I came to him and asked him about these people whom 'Ali killed. He said: I said: For what did they separate from him? For what did they deem him lawful? For what did he call them? For what did they separate from him? By what did he deem their blood lawful? He said: When killing intensified among the people of Syria at Siffin, Mu'awiya and his companions resorted to a trick. 'Amr ibn al-'As said to him: Send me the mushaf; by Allah, we shall not return it to you. He said: A man came carrying it and called: Between us and you is the Book of Allah, {Have you not seen those given a share of the Book}, the verse. 'Ali said: Yes, between us and you is the Book of Allah; we are worthier of it than you. Then the Khawarij came — we called them that day al-Qurra' — with their swords on their shoulders, saying: O Commander of the Believers, will you not walk to these people until Allah judges between us and them. Sahl ibn Hunayf stood and said: O people, suspect yourselves. We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hudaybiya, and had we seen fighting we would have fought; that was in the truce between the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the polytheists. 'Umar ibn al-Khattab came and said: O Messenger of Allah, are we not upon truth and they upon falsehood? He said: Yes. He said: Are not our slain in Paradise and their slain in Fire? He said: Yes. He said: Then why do we concede humiliation in our religion and return without Allah judging between us and them? He said: O son of al-Khattab, I am the Messenger of Allah and Allah will never forsake me. 'Umar went off impatient in anger until he came to Abu Bakr and said: O Abu Bakr, are we not upon truth and they upon falsehood? He said: Yes. He said: Are not our slain in Paradise and their slain in Fire? He said: Yes. He said: Then why do we concede humiliation in our religion and return without Allah judging between us and them? He said: O son of al-Khattab, he is the Messenger of Allah and Allah will never forsake him. Then the Qur'an came down upon Muhammad with the conquest, so he sent to 'Umar and read it to him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, is it a conquest? He said: Yes. He said: So his soul was pleased and he returned, and the people returned. Then they came out at Harura' — that band of the Khawarij, some ten-odd thousand — and 'Ali sent to them adjuring them by Allah, but they refused him. Sa'sa'a ibn Sawhan came to them and adjured them, saying: For what do you fight your caliph? They said: For fear of tribulation. He said: Do not hasten this year's misguidance for fear of next year's tribulation. They returned and said: We proceed upon what we came for; if 'Ali accepts the arbitration we shall fight as we fought on the day of Siffin, and if he breaks it we shall fight with him. They marched until they reached al-Nahrawan, and a faction of them split off demolishing people by night. Their companions said: Woe to you, it was not for this we separated from 'Ali. Their affair reached 'Ali, so he stood, addressed the people, and said: What do you think? Do we march to the people of Syria or return to these who stayed behind to your offspring? They said: Rather we return to them. He mentioned their affair and narrated about them what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said of them: A faction will come out at a dissension among people, killed by the party of the two closest to the truth; their mark a man among them whose hand is like a woman's breast. They marched until they met at al-Nahrawan and fought fierce fighting; 'Ali's cavalry could not stand to them. 'Ali stood and said: O people, if you fight for me, by Allah I have nothing to reward you with; if you fight for Allah, let not this be your doing. The people charged one charge, and it cleared from them with them fallen on their faces. 'Ali said: Seek the man among them. The people sought the man but did not find him, until some said: Ibn Abi Talib deluded us about our brothers until we killed them. 'Ali's eye wept. He called for his mount, mounted it, and went until he came to a hollow with slain piled upon one another. He dragged them by their legs until he found the man beneath them, and they informed him. 'Ali said: Allah is Greatest; he rejoiced and the people rejoiced and returned. 'Ali said: I shall not raid this year. He returned to Kufa, was killed, may Allah have mercy on him, Hasan succeeded, followed his father's conduct, then sent allegiance to Mu'awiya."
"473","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Iyad ibn 'Amr al-Qari: that 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad came and entered upon 'A'isha, with us sitting with her, on his return from Iraq in the nights 'Ali ibn Abi Talib was killed. She said to him: O son of Shaddad ibn al-Had, will you tell me truthfully what I ask you? Narrate to me of the people whom 'Ali killed. He said: Why should I not tell you truthfully? She said: Narrate to me their story. He said: When 'Ali ibn Abi Talib corresponded with Mu'awiya and the two arbiters arbitrated, eight thousand of the reciters of the people went out against him and alighted at a land called Harura' on the side of Kufa. They blamed him, saying: You stripped off a shirt Allah clothed you with, and a name Allah named you with, then you went and arbitrated in Allah's religion; judgment belongs only to Allah. When what they blamed him for and separated from him over reached 'Ali, he ordered a caller who called that none shall enter upon the Commander of the Believers except one who carries the Qur'an. When the house filled with reciters, he called for a great imam mushaf; 'Ali placed it before him, striking it with his hand, saying: O mushaf, speak to the people. The people called to him: O Commander of the Believers, what you ask of is but ink on paper; we speak with what we saw of it, so what do you want? He said: These companions of yours who went out — between me and them is the Book of Allah. Allah says in His Book concerning a woman and a man: {If you fear dissension between them, send an arbiter from his folk and an arbiter from her folk; if they desire settlement, Allah will reconcile them}. The umma of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is of greater sanctity — or: covenant — than a woman and a man. They blamed me that I corresponded with Mu'awiya, writing 'Ali ibn Abi Talib; yet Suhayl ibn 'Amr came and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote: In the name of Allah, the Merciful, the Compassionate. He said: Do not write In the name of Allah, the Merciful, the Compassionate. He said: How shall we write? Suhayl said: Write: In Your name, O Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then write: Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah. He said: Had I known you are the Messenger of Allah I would not have opposed you. So he wrote: This is what Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah made peace with Quraysh upon. Allah says in His Book: {You have in the Messenger of Allah a good example for whoever hopes for Allah and the Last Day}. Then he sent to them 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas, and I went out with him until when we reached the midst of their camp, Ibn al-Kawwa' stood and addressed the people, saying: O bearers of the Qur'an, this is 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas; whoever did not know him, let him know him; I but define him from the Book of Allah — this is of those concerning whom and his people {a contentious people} was revealed. Return him to his companion and do not contend with him by the Book of Allah. Their orators stood and said: By Allah, we shall contend with him by the Book; if he brings us a truth we know, we shall follow it, and if he brings falsehood we shall refute him with falsehood, and return him to his companion. They contended with 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas by the Book for three days; four thousand of them returned, all repentant, among them Ibn al-Kawwa', until 'Ali brought them into Kufa. 'Ali sent to the rest of them, saying: What happened between us and the people you have seen; stand where you wish; between us and you: that you shed no inviolable blood, cut no road, nor wrong a covenant; if you do, we have cast war to you equally; {Indeed Allah does not love the treacherous}. He said: 'A'isha said to him: O son of Shaddad, so he killed them? He said: By Allah, he did not send against them until they cut the road, shed blood, and violated the covenant. She said: By Allah? He said: By Allah besides whom there is no god, it was so. She said: What is this I was told of the people of Iraq talking, saying: Dhu al-Thudayya? Twice. He said: I saw him and stood with 'Ali over him among the slain; he called the people and said: Do you know this? How many came saying: I saw him praying in the mosque of such-and-such tribe; they brought no established identification of him except that. She said: What did 'Ali say when he stood over him, as the people of Iraq claim? He said: I heard him say: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. She said: Did you hear him say other than that? He said: O Allah, no. She said: Yes, Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth; may Allah have mercy on 'Ali, for of his speech he would see nothing pleasing except he said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth; so the people of Iraq went fabricating upon him and adding to the hadith."
"474","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, 'Awf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, 'Abida al-Salmani narrated to us, who said: When the people of al-Nahrawan were struck, 'Ali said to us: Seek among them; if they are the people the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned, among them is a man with a defective arm, or a breasted arm. He said: So we sought him and found him, and we called him to him. He stood over him and said: Allah is Greatest. Were it not that you would exult, I would narrate to you what Allah decreed upon the tongue of His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for whoever killed them. He said: I said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'ba; yes, by the Lord of the Ka'ba. He said: That reached one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as if she envied him for it. 'Awf said: I deliberately withheld from her."
"475","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-'Uryan al-Harithi narrated to us, al-Azraq ibn Qays narrated to us, from a man of 'Abd al-Qays, who said: I witnessed 'Ali on the day the people of al-Nahrawan were killed. He said: 'Ali said when they were killed: Bring me Dhu al-Thudayya — or: al-Mukhdaj — he mentioned something of that I do not retain. He said: They sought him, and there he was, an Abyssinian like a camel, on his shoulder like a woman's breast, upon it — 'Abd al-Rahman said: I think he said — hair. Had a man's soul to leave from joy, 'Ali's soul would have left that day. He said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. Whoever narrates to me of the people that he saw him before this death of his, I am a liar."
"476","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from 'Abida, who said: 'Ali mentioned the people of al-Nahrawan, saying: Among them a man with a small hand, or breasted hand, or defective hand. Were it not that you would exult, I would inform you what Allah promised those who kill them upon the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I said: Did you hear it from him? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'ba."
"477","Nasr ibn 'Ali al-Jahdami narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, Abu Kathir, freedman of the Ansar, narrated to us, who said: I was with my master 'Ali ibn Abi Talib when the people of al-Nahrawan were killed. He said: The people seemed to find in themselves about their killing. 'Ali said: O people, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us of peoples passing out of religion as the arrow passes out of the game, not returning to it until the arrow returns to its bow; the sign of that is that among them is a man with a defective arm, one of his hands like a woman's breast, with a nipple like a woman's breast-nipple, upon it seven hairs. Seek him, for I deem him among them. They sought him and found him at the river's edge beneath the slain. They brought him out, and 'Ali exclaimed takbir, saying: Allah is Greatest; Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. The sign of that: girt with an Arab bow of his; he took it in his hand, then thrust with it into his defective part, saying: Allah is Greatest; Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth; Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. The people exclaimed takbir when they saw him and rejoiced, and what they felt departed from them."
"478","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ibn 'Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from 'Abida, that he said: I narrate to you only what I heard from him — meaning 'Ali. He said: Were it not that you would exult, I would inform you of what Allah promised those who kill them upon the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I said: Did you hear it from Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'ba, three times. Among them a man defective, or breasted of arm. He said: I think he said: and small of arm. He said: They sought that man and found here and there like a woman's breast, upon it hairs. Muhammad said: 'Abida swore to me three times he heard it from 'Ali; and 'Ali swore three times he heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"479","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Jamil ibn Murra narrated to us, from Abu al-Wadi', who said: I witnessed 'Ali when he killed the people of al-Nahrawan. He said: Seek al-Mukhdaj. He said: They sought him among the slain and said: We do not find him. He said: Return and seek him; by Allah, I did not lie nor was I lied to. They returned and sought him, then he repeated the like of that times: I did not lie nor was I lied to. They went and found him under slain in mud; they extracted him and he was brought. Abu al-Wadi' said: As if I look at him, an Abyssinian wearing a qartaq, one of his hands like a woman's breast, upon it hairs like hairs on a jerboa's tail."
"480","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from 'Abida, from 'Ali, who said: He mentioned the Khawarij, saying: Among them a man with a defective arm, or small arm, or breasted arm. Were it not that you would exult, I would narrate to you what Allah promised those who kill them upon the tongue of Muhammad. He said: I said: Did you hear it from Muhammad? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'ba; yes, by the Lord of the Ka'ba; yes, by the Lord of the Ka'ba."
"481","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, who said: I was sitting with 'Ali when a man in travel clothes came and said: O Commander of the Believers, permit me to speak? While 'Ali was speaking to people and they speaking to him, and he did not turn to him. I asked him of his news, and he said: I was performing 'umra, and I met 'A'isha, and she said: Who are these people who came out in your land called al-Haruriyya? I said: They came out from a place called Harura', so they were so named. She said: Did you witness their destruction? I do not know, he said: Yes or no. She said: Blessed is he who witnessed their ruin. By Allah, had 'Ali ibn Abi Talib wished he would have informed you of their affair. So I came to ask him of their affair. 'Ali finished and said: Where is the one seeking permission? He related to him what he related to us. 'Ali exclaimed tahlil and takbir twice, then said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with none present but 'A'isha, Mother of the Believers. He said: O 'Ali, how will you be with such-and-such people. I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He gestured with his hand. He said: A people coming out from the east, reciting the Qur'an not passing their collarbones, passing through religion as the arrow passes through the game; among them a defective man, as if his hand were an Abyssinian woman's breast. I adjure you by Allah, did I inform you of them? They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, did I inform you he is of them? They said: Yes. He said: So you informed me he is not of them, and I swore to you he is of them. They said: Yes. So you brought him to me dragging as I described to you? They said: Yes. He said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth."
"482","'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Dawud ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Abu 'Abdullah Maslama al-Razi narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi, from Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Ali, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyya, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah loves the believing servant, oft-tried, oft-repenting."
"483","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Harun ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn 'Ali, from his father, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O 'Ali, perfect ablution though it be hard upon you, do not eat charity, do not mount donkeys upon horses, and do not sit with astrologers."
"484","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn 'Abdullah ibn Usama ibn al-Had, from 'Uthman ibn Suhayb, from his father, who said: 'Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Who is the most wretched of the first? I said: The hamstringer of the she-camel. He said: You spoke truly; then who is the most wretched of the last? I said: I have no knowledge, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The one who strikes you on this — pointing with his hand to his crown — and he used to say: I wish the most wretched of you had risen and dyed this from this, meaning his beard from his head's blood."
"485","Suwayd narrated to us, Salih ibn Musa ibn Ishaq ibn Talha al-Qurashi narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Hasan, from his mother Fatima bint al-Husayn, from her father, from 'Ali: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he entered the mosque said: O Allah, open for me the doors of Your mercy; and when he went out, he said: O Allah, open for me the doors of Your bounty."
"486","Suwayd narrated to us, Salih ibn Musa narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Hasan, from his mother Fatima bint al-Husayn, from her father, from 'Ali: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All grazing livestock is oppressive or unjust."
"487","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Safwan ibn 'Isa al-Zuhri narrated to us, al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perfecting ablution in disliked circumstances, walking on foot to mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer, washes away sins thoroughly."
"488","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Samina al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Hanafi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i narrated to us, from Abu al-Huwayrith, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: I was at a well on the day of Badr drawing water from it, when a strong wind came, then a very strong wind came, I never saw a wind stronger than it except the one before it, then a strong wind came. The first was Mika'il with a thousand angels on the right of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the second Israfil with a thousand angels on the left of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the third Jibril with a thousand angels; Abu Bakr was on his right and I on his left. When Allah routed the disbelievers, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted me on a horse; when I settled on it, it carried me and I came upon its neck, so I supplicated Allah and He steadied me on it, and I thrust with my spear until blood reached my armpit."
"489","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn 'Umar narrated to me, 'Abdullah ibn Wahb ibn Munabbih narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Khalifa, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah is Gentle, loves gentleness, and gives for it what He does not give for harshness."
"490","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn A'yan, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Dili, from his father, from 'Ali, who said: 'Abdullah ibn Salam came to me with my foot in the stirrup, saying to me: Do not proceed to Iraq, for I fear the fly of the sword may strike you there. 'Ali said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me of it. Abu al-Aswad said: I never saw like today a warrior informing of that of himself."
"491","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani' ibn Hani' or Yazid ibn Hani', from 'Ali, who said: 'Ammar sought permission upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Welcome to the pure, perfumed one."
"492","And Ishaq narrated it to us, from Sharik, with its chain, the like of it; and in Ishaq's hadith, he said: The doubt is from Sharik."
"493","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti and Ishaq narrated to us, both saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Dhi Huddan, from 'Ali, who said: Allah named war deception upon the tongue of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"494","'Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Asim ibn Damra, from 'Ali, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night eight rak'as of voluntary prayer, and by day twelve rak'as."
"495","'Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, 'Abthar ibn al-Qasim and Jarir and Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Tha'laba ibn Yazid al-Himmani, from 'Ali, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"496","Wahb ibn Baqiyya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade a man raising his voice with the Qur'an before 'Atama and after it, confusing his companions, while the people pray."
"497","'Isa ibn Salim narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Ibn 'Aqil, from Muhammad ibn 'Ali, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: that he named his eldest son Hamza, and named Husayn after his uncle Ja'far. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called 'Ali; when he came, he said: Did you change the names of these two sons of mine? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. So he named them Hasan and Husayn."
"498","Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayya, who said: I saw 'Ali perform ablution: he washed his palms until he cleaned them, rinsed thrice, inhaled thrice, washed his face thrice, his forearms thrice, wiped his head, washed his feet to the ankles, took the remainder of his water and drank it standing, then said: I loved to show you how the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was."
"499","Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: 'Abd Khayr mentioned, from 'Ali, the like of Abu Hayya's hadith, except 'Abd Khayr said: When he finished his ablution he took a handful of its remainder and drank it."
"500","Abu Ma'mar Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Qasim Abu Ibrahim al-Asadi, from Sa'id ibn 'Ubayd, from 'Ali ibn Rabi'a, from 'Ali, who said: I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When blood is stirred in one of you, let him let it, even with a broad arrowhead."
"501","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Ruman al-Qurazi, from a man he named and I forgot, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: I went out on a cold hungry morning, cold having afflicted me. I took a woolen garment we had, put it about my neck and bound it on my chest to warm myself. By Allah, there was nothing in my house I could eat, and had there been anything in the house of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it would have reached me. I went out to a quarter of Medina to a Jew in his garden, and looked upon him through a gap in his wall. He said: What is with you, O Bedouin, will you take a bucket for a date? I said: Yes; open the garden for me. He opened for me, I entered, and I drew the bucket while he gave me a date, until I filled my palm. I said: Enough from you now. I ate them, drank water, then came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sat with him in the mosque while he was with a group of his companions. Mus'ab ibn 'Umayr came upon us in a cloak of his patched with fur; he had been the most pampered youth of Mecca and easiest in life. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him, he remembered the bliss he had been in, and saw the state he was upon, so his eyes shed tears and he wept. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are you better today, or when a bowl of bread and meat is brought to one of you in the morning and another in the evening, he goes in one suit and returns in another, and you cover your houses as the Ka'ba is covered? We said: Rather we are better that day; we devote ourselves to worship. He said: Rather you are better today."
"502","'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, who said: 'Ali ibn Abi Talib said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me to Fatima for an iron Himyari armor; he had armed me with it, and said: Send it to her to make it lawful for her thereby. So I sent it to her; by Allah, its price was not four hundred dirhams and such."
"503","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar al-Ansari narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Fayruz, Hudayn ibn al-Mundhir al-Raqashi narrated to me, who said: I witnessed 'Uthman ibn 'Affan when al-Walid ibn 'Uqba was brought, having prayed Fajr with the people of Kufa four rak'as, then saying: Shall I add for you? He said: Humran and another man testified against him; one testified he saw him drinking it — meaning wine — and the other testified he saw him vomiting it. 'Uthman said: He did not vomit it until he drank it. He said to 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: Establish the hadd upon him. 'Ali said to his son al-Hasan: Establish the hadd upon him. Al-Hasan said: Entrust its heat to whoever undertook its cool. He said to 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far, his nephew: Establish the hadd upon him. He took a whip and flogged him while 'Ali counted; when he reached forty, he said: Stop. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged forty, Abu Bakr forty, 'Umar eighty, and each is sunna; this is dearer to me."
"504","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Mansur ibn 'Abdullah al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn 'Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The slogan of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O source of all good."
"505","Umayya ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abu al-Muwarri', from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out for a funeral and said: Will not a man go to Medina and leave no grave unleveled, no image unspoiled, no idol unbroken. A man stood but feared the people of Medina. 'Ali stood and said: I, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So he went, then came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not come to you until I left in it no grave unleveled, no image unspoiled, no idol unbroken. He said: Whoever returns to making any of it has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Do not be a tempter, nor arrogant, nor a trader, except a trader in good; those are the foremost in deed."
"506","'Abd al-Ghaffar ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from Sa'id ibn Ashwa', from Hanash al-Kinani, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: that he called his police chief and said: Go and leave no grave unleveled, no ornament unerased. Then he said: Do you know for what I sent you? I sent you for what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me for."
"507","'Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from al-Hakam, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to slaughter the sacrificial camels and give their meat in charity. I returned to him asking about their coverings and skins, and he commanded me to give them in charity."
"508","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Nasr ibn Hajib narrated to us, Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Zadham, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The right of the Muslim upon the Muslim is six: he greets him when he meets him, answers him when he invites him, advises him in absence, says yarhamuk Allah when he sneezes, visits him when ill, and attends his funeral when he dies."
"509","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Thabit, from his father, from Abu Fakhta, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatima: I and you and this — meaning me — and these two: al-Hasan and al-Husayn, shall be on the Day of Resurrection in one place."
"510","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Hudhayl ibn Hilal, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mas'ud al-'Abdi, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to look at a man part of whose limbs precede him to Paradise, let him look at Zayd ibn Sawhan."
"511","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, from Isra'il, from 'Abd al-A'la, from Muhammad ibn 'Ali, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to eat tharid, drink milk, and pray without renewing ablution."
"512","Isma'il ibn bint al-Suddi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not lie upon me, for whoever lies upon me enters the Fire."
"513","Isma'il narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from 'Umayr ibn Sa'id, from 'Ali, who said: I would not doubt whom I established the hadd upon, except the drinker of wine; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laid down nothing in it; it is but something we said ourselves."
"514","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us — Abu Sa'id said: a man asked him of his name; he said: Nadr ibn Mansur — from his father, who said: 'Uqba ibn 'Alqama al-Yashkuri narrated to us, who said: I heard 'Ali, on the day of the Camel, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me saying: Talha and al-Zubayr are my neighbors in Paradise."
"515","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Mujalid, from 'Amir, from al-Harith, from 'Ali: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed ten: the eater of usury, its giver, its scribe, its two witnesses, the tattooer, the tattooed, the withholder of charity, the muhallil, and the muhallal for."
"516","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Mansur ibn Wardan narrated to us, 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from 'Ali, who said: When {To Allah upon people is pilgrimage to the House, whoever can find a way to it} was revealed, the believers said: O Messenger of Allah, every year? Twice. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent. They said: O Messenger of Allah, every year? Twice. He said: No; had I said yes it would be obligatory. So Allah revealed: {O you who believe, ask not of things which if disclosed to you would grieve you}."
"517","Isma'il ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Sahl al-Fazari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Ubayd narrated to me, from 'Ali ibn Rabi'a, who said: I heard 'Ali upon the pulpit, and a man came to him and said: O Commander of the Believers, why do I see you driving people as a man drives his camels; by a covenant from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or something you deemed? He said: By Allah, I did not lie nor was I lied to, I did not stray nor was I led astray; rather a covenant the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) covenanted to me, {And he who fabricates has failed}."
"518","Isma'il ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Sahl narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn 'Ubayd, from 'Ali ibn Rabi'a, who said: I heard 'Ali upon this pulpit of yours saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) covenanted to me to fight the oath-breakers, the unjust, and the renegades."
"519","Isma'il ibn Musa narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from 'Ammar, from Abu Salih, from 'Ali, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in my dream, and I complained to him of what I met from his umma of crookedness and contention. I wept, and he said to me: Do not weep, O 'Ali. I turned and he turned, and there were two men ascending, with boulders crushing their heads until split open, then returning — or he said: coming back. He said: I went early to 'Ali as I went early to him every day, until when I was among the cobblers I met people saying: The Commander of the Believers was killed."
"520","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from 'Ali, who said: He made food and invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He saw in the house something with images, so he returned. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what turned you back, may my father and mother ransom you? He said: In the house is a curtain with images, and angels do not enter a house with images."
"521","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, who said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far saying: I heard 'Ali in Kufa saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best of its women is Maryam daughter of 'Imran; she is the best of its women in her day, and the best of its women is Khadija daughter of Khuwaylid."
"522","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Hubayb ibn Habib, brother of Hamza al-Zayyat, narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Islam is eight shares: Islam a share, prayer a share, zakat a share, hajj a share, jihad a share, fasting Ramadan a share, enjoining good a share, forbidding evil a share; and failed is he who has no share."
"523","Dawud ibn 'Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murra, from 'Abdullah ibn Salima, from 'Ali: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was prevented from reciting the Qur'an by nothing except being junub."
"524","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Hudayj ibn Mu'awiya narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hudhayfa, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he said: I saw the moon on the Night of Decree as if it were half a bowl."
"525","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayra ibn Yarim and Hani' ibn Hani', from 'Ali: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Zayd ibn Haritha when they disputed over the daughter of Hamza: As for you, O Zayd, you are our brother and our freedman."
"526","Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Adhrami narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Yazid al-Suda'i narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Nabhan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade singing women and wailing women, buying them, selling them, and trading in them, saying: Their earnings are unlawful."
"527","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn 'Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Suhbani narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Mu'min, from Abu al-Mughira, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought me and found me sleeping in a rivulet. He said: Rise; I do not blame people calling you Abu Turab. He said: He saw as if I found something in myself of that. He said: Rise; by Allah, I shall please you: you are my brother and the father of my two sons; you fight for my sunna and clear my liability. Whoever dies in my covenant is Allah's treasure; whoever dies in your covenant has fulfilled his vow; whoever dies loving you after your death, Allah seals for him security and faith, as long as sun rose or set; whoever dies hating you dies a jahili death, and is reckoned for what he did in Islam."
"528","Wahb ibn Baqiyya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Muslim, meaning al-A'war, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen and commanded me to forbid dubba', hantam, muzaffat, muqayyar, and naqir."
"529","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abd al-Majid narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhab narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn 'Awn ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, from his father, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: I fought on the day of Badr fiercely, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and there he was prostrating, saying: O Living, O Sustainer. Then I went and fought, then came and there was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating, saying: O Living, O Sustainer. He said: So Allah gave him victory."
"530","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Farwa, from Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from 'Ali: that a man killed his slave deliberately, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged him a hundred, exiled him a year, erased his share from the Muslims, and did not execute him for him."
"531","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj al-Lakhmi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr narrated to us, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabra, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The adornment of prayer is shoes."
"532","Al-Hasan ibn 'Arafa narrated to us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Ali, who said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Abu Bakr and 'Umar came. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These two are the masters of the aged people of Paradise among the first and the last, except the prophets and messengers. O 'Ali, do not inform them."
"533","Al-Hasan ibn 'Arafa narrated to us, 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-Rahman Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Hasira, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabi'a ibn Najid, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: In you is a likeness of 'Isa son of Maryam: the Jews hated him until they slandered his mother, and the Christians loved him until they placed him in a station not his. He said: Then 'Ali said: Two men perish concerning me: an extravagant lover exceeding for me what is not in me, and a fabricating hater whose hatred drives him to slander me."
"534","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, who said: I heard Malik ibn 'Urfuta, who said: I heard 'Abd Khayr, who said: I saw 'Ali rinse thrice with inhaling with one water, then say: Whoever wishes to look at the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this is the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"535","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, 'Asim narrated to us, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, who said: I said to a man: Recite to me thirty verses of al-Ahqaf. He recited to me contrary to what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited to me. I said to another: Recite to me thirty verses of al-Ahqaf. He recited to me contrary to what the first recited to me. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with 'Ali sitting with him. 'Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite as you were taught."
"536","Abu Musa al-Zamin narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn 'Ajlan — Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn Hunayn narrated to me — from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: 'Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me the gold ring, reciting while bowing, qassi and saffron-dyed cloth."
"537","Abu Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan — Sulayman narrated to me — from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba' and muzaffat."
"538","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Mughira, from Umm Musa, who said: I heard 'Ali saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Ibn Mas'ud to climb a tree and bring him something from it. His companions looked at the thinness of his legs and laughed at them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you laugh at? The leg of 'Abdullah on the Day of Resurrection is heavier than Uhud."
"539","Al-Hasan ibn 'Arafa narrated to us, al-Mubarak ibn Sa'id, brother of Sufyan al-Thawri, narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from Habib, from 'Abd Khayr al-Hamdani who said: I heard 'Ali ibn Abi Talib saying upon this pulpit: Shall I not inform you of the best of this umma after its Prophet? He said: He mentioned Abu Bakr. He said: Then he said: Shall I not inform you of the second? He said: He mentioned 'Umar ibn al-Khattab. He said: Then he said: Had I wished, I would inform you of the third. He said: Then he fell silent. He said: Then we thought he meant himself. Habib said: I said to 'Abd Khayr: Did you hear this from 'Ali? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'ba; otherwise let them be deaf."
"540","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Habib informed me, from Nawfal ibn 'Abd al-Malik, from his father, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade bargaining before sunrise, and slaughtering milch animals."
"541","Abu Musa narrated to us, Mansur ibn Wardan al-Asadi narrated to us, 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from 'Ali, who said: When this verse was revealed: {To Allah upon people is pilgrimage to the House, whoever can find a way to it}, they said: O Messenger of Allah, every year? He fell silent. Then they said: Every year? He said: No; had I said yes it would be obligatory. So Allah revealed {O you who believe, ask not of things which if disclosed to you would grieve you}, to the end of the verse."
"542","Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Khalil, from 'Ali who said: Al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba had a spear; when we went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a raid, he planted it and people passed by it and carried it off. I said to him: If I come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I shall inform him. He said: If you do, no lost item shall be lifted."
"543","Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn 'Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'a, from Zayd ibn 'Ali, from his father, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at 'Arafa and said: This is 'Arafa, this is the standing place, and all 'Arafa is a standing place. Then he poured forth when the sun set, mounting Usama behind him, proceeding gently, with people striking right and left, not turning to them, saying: O people, upon you is calm. Then he came to Jam' and prayed with them both prayers together. When morning came he came to Qazah, stood upon it, and said: This is Qazah, this is the standing place, and all Jam' is a standing place. Then he poured forth; when he reached the valley of Muhassir he struck his she-camel and it trotted until it crossed the valley. He stopped and mounted al-Fadl behind him, then came to the Jamra and stoned it, then came to the slaughter place and said: This is the slaughter place and all Mina is a slaughter place. A young woman of Khath'am sought his fatwa, saying: My father is an aged old man, doting, and Allah's obligation of hajj has reached him; does it suffice that I perform hajj for him? He said: Perform hajj for your father. He turned al-Fadl's neck. Al-'Abbas said to him: Why did you turn your cousin's neck? He said: I saw a youth and a young woman, and I did not trust Satan with them. A man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I poured forth before shaving? He said: Shave, and shorten, no harm. Another man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered before stoning. He said: Stone, no harm. Then he came to the House and circumambulated it, then came to Zamzam and said: O sons of 'Abd al-Muttalib, your watering; were it not that people would overpower you, I would draw with it."
"544","Abu Musa narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Amr ibn Murra, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from 'Ali, who said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab said: What do you think of a surplus remaining with us of this wealth? People said: O Commander of the Believers, we kept you from your family, estate, and trade, so it is yours. He said to me: What do you say? I said: They advised you. He said: Speak. I said: Why make your certainty conjecture and your knowledge ignorance? He said: You shall explain what you said, or I shall punish you. I said: Yes, I shall explain it. Do you not remember when the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent you as a collector, and you came to al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib, who withheld his charity from you. You said to me: Come with me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to inform him of what al-'Abbas did. We went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found him heavy-spirited, so we returned. Then we returned to him next day and found him cheerful, and informed him of what al-'Abbas did. He said: Do you not know that a man's uncle is the like of his father. We mentioned to him what we saw of his heaviness the first day and his cheerfulness the second day. He said: You came to me the first day with a dinar of charity remaining with me, and that was what you saw; you came to me today with it disbursed, and that is the cheerfulness you saw. 'Umar said: You spoke truly. By Allah, I shall thank — meaning for you — the first and the last. I said: O Commander of the Believers, why hasten punishment and delay thanks?"
"545","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marwan al-'Uqayli narrated to us, from 'Umara ibn Abi Hafsa, from 'Ikrima who said: 'Ali said: When people dispersed from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud, I looked among the slain and did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: By Allah, he would not flee, and I do not see him among the slain; but I deem Allah angry with us for what we did, so He raised His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). There is no good in me but to fight until I am killed. So I broke my sword's sheath, then charged the people and they made way for me, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among them."
"546","Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab informed me, from 'Ali ibn Husayn, from his father, from 'Ali, who said: I obtained an old she-camel in the spoils of Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me an old she-camel. I made them kneel at an Ansari man's door, intending to load idhkhir upon them to sell, with a goldsmith of Banu Qaynuqa' with me. 'Ali said: To help with Fatima's wedding feast. Hamza ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib was in the house drinking, with a singing girl singing to him, saying: The fat ones. He rose at them with the sword, cut off their humps, ripped their flanks, and took of their livers. He said: I said to Ibn Shihab: And of the hump? He said: He had cut off their humps. He said: I looked at a sight that horrified me, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with Zayd ibn Haritha with me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out with Zayd ibn Haritha, and I went out with him, until he stood over Hamza. He said: He was angry with him. He said: Hamza raised his gaze and said: Are you but the slaves of my fathers? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) withdrew retreating from him."
"547","Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn 'Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather: that 'Ali when he traveled journeyed after the sun set until it almost darkened, then alighted and prayed Maghrib, then called for his dinner and ate, then prayed 'Isha, then departed, saying: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do."
"548","Abu Musa narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Khalid, from Abu 'Ubayd, freedman of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar, who said: I heard 'Ali saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that anything of your sacrificial meat remain with you after three days."
"549","Abu Musa narrated to us, Sahl ibn Hammad Abu 'Attab al-Dallal narrated to us, Mukhtar ibn Nafi' al-Tamimi narrated to us, Abu Hayyan al-Tamimi narrated to me, from his father, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: May Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr: he married me to his daughter, carried me to the abode of emigration, and freed Bilal with his wealth. May Allah have mercy on 'Umar: he speaks truth though bitter; truth left him without friend. May Allah have mercy on 'Uthman: the angels are shy of him. May Allah have mercy on 'Ali: O Allah, turn truth with him however he turns."
"550","Abu Musa narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayra, from 'Ali, who said: I said to Fatima: Would you come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him for a servant, for work has exhausted you. She came to him but did not meet him. He said: Shall I not guide you to better than what you asked? When you go to your bed, glorify thirty-three, praise thirty-three, and exalt thirty-four; that is a hundred upon the tongue and a thousand in the scale."
"551","Abu Musa narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-'Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, 'Amr ibn Murra narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us until he placed his foot between me and Fatima, and taught us what to say when we take our beds: thirty-three glorifications, thirty-three praises, thirty-four exaltations. 'Ali said: I did not leave them after. A man said to him: Not even the night of Siffin? He said: Not even the night of Siffin."
"552","Abu Musa narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub narrating from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad, from Hassan ibn Kurayb, from 'Ali: that he used to say: The utterer of obscenity and its listener are equal in sin."
"553","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayra ibn Yarim and Hani' ibn Hani', from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Zayd ibn Haritha when they disputed over the daughter of Hamza: As for you, O Zayd, you are our brother and our freedman."
"554","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Jamil ibn Murra narrated to us, from Abu al-Wadi', who said: We were with 'Ali when the people of al-Nahrawan were killed. He said: Seek for me al-Mukhdaj. The people went but did not find him. He said: Return and seek him. They went but did not find him. He said: Return and seek him; by Allah, I was not lied to nor did I lie. He said: They went and extracted him from beneath the slain in mud. They brought him; as if I look at him, an Abyssinian wearing a qartaq, one of his hands like a woman's nipple, upon it hairs like hairs on a jerboa's tail."
"555","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib: that 'Ali made food, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came until when he looked at the house he returned. 'Ali said: What turned you back, O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother ransom you? He said: I saw in your house a curtain with images, and angels do not enter a house with images."
"556","And with it, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from 'Ali, that he said: Maternal brothers do not inherit the blood-money of their maternal brother when he is killed."
"557","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, Harun ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abu Salih al-Ju'fi, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to blind its wells, meaning on the day of Badr."
"558","'Ubaydullah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, who said: 'Ali said: When I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), falling from heaven is dearer to me than to say of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did not say; but war is deception."
"559","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Yunus ibn Arqam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymira, from Shurayh ibn Hani', who said: I came to 'Ali and asked him of wiping over the khuffs. He said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and we wiped three days and their nights; for the resident, a day."
"560","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, 'Umar ibn 'Amir narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are exempted from the charity of horses and slaves; but bring the charity of silver: of every forty dirhams, a dirham; nothing is taken from you until it be two hundred dirhams; when it is two hundred dirhams, therein are five dirhams."
"561","'Ubaydullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, 'Umar ibn 'Amir narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Hassan al-A'raj, from 'Ali: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believers' bloods are equal, they are one hand against others; the lowest of them grants their protection. No believer is killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant during his covenant."
"562","'Ubaydullah narrated to us, al-Sakan ibn Ibrahim al-Burjumi Abu 'Amr narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrated to us, from Ibn Ashwa', from Hanash al-Kinani, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: that he sent his police officer, saying to him: Do you know upon what I send you? I send you upon what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me upon: to carve away for him every ornament — meaning every image — and level every grave."
"563","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Ubaydullah al-'Abdi narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Khalid al-'Abdi — my father narrated to me — from my grandfather, from 'Ali: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed people one day, saying: The rulers are of Quraysh; the rulers are of Quraysh; the rulers are of Quraysh, so long as they uphold three: when they judge they are just, when they covenant they fulfill, when mercy is sought from them they show mercy. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"564","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Harami ibn 'Umara narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn 'Umayra Abu Qutayba al-Qaysi narrated to us, who said: Maymun al-Kurdi Abu Nusayr narrated to me, from Abu 'Uthman, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held my hand, walking in a lane of Medina, we came upon a garden. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how fine a garden! He said: For you in Paradise is finer than it. Then we passed another, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, how fine a garden. He said: For you in Paradise is finer than it. Until we passed seven gardens, each time I saying: How fine! and he saying: For you in Paradise is finer than it. When the road cleared for him, he embraced me then broke weeping. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what makes you weep? He said: Rancors in the breasts of peoples, which they will not disclose to you except after me. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, in safety of my religion? He said: In safety of your religion."
"565","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Qays, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from 'Ali who said: The first of creatures to be clothed is Ibrahim, with two Qibti garments; and Muhammad is clothed with a Hibara cloak. He said: And he is at the right of the Throne."
"566","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yunus ibn Arqam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: I witnessed 'Ali in al-Rahba adjuring people: I adjure by Allah whoever heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying on the day of Ghadir Khumm: Whomsoever I am his master, 'Ali is his master, to stand and testify. 'Abd al-Rahman said: Twelve Badris stood, as if I look at one of them wearing trousers, saying: We testify we heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying on the day of Ghadir Khumm: Am I not worthier of the believers than themselves, and my wives their mothers? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So whomsoever I am his master, 'Ali is his master. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, oppose whoever opposes him."
"567","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, al-Furat ibn Salman narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to the butcher slaughtering his sacrificial camels, commanding me to give their meats, skins, and coverings in charity, and give nothing thereof, saying: We give him from other than that."
"568","'Ubaydullah narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam informed me, from Abu Sinan Yazid ibn Umayya al-Dili, who said: 'Ali ibn Abi Talib fell severely ill until he neared death and we feared for him. Then he recovered and convalesced. We said: Congratulations, Abu al-Hasan; praise to Allah who healed you; we feared for you. He said: But I did not fear for myself. The truthful, believed one informed me I shall not die until I am struck upon this — pointing to the front-left of his head — and this dyed from it with blood, taking his beard. He said to me: The most wretched of this umma shall kill you, as the she-camel of Allah was hamstrung by the most wretched of such-and-such tribe of Thamud. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascribed him to his nearer clan, apart from Thamud."
"569","'Ubaydullah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam, from 'Ali, who said: We saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand, so we stood; he sat, so we sat — meaning at the funeral."
"570","'Ubaydullah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayya, from 'Ali: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution three times three times."
"571","'Ubaydullah narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, 'Abda ibn Abi Lubaba narrated to me, who said: I heard Shaqiq ibn Salama saying: I saw 'Ali perform ablution three times three times, saying: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution."
"572","'Ubaydullah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Asim ibn Damra, from 'Ali: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray after every prescribed prayer two rak'as, except 'Asr and Fajr."
"573","'Ubaydullah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Salama narrated to us, my uncle al-Majishun ibn Abi Salama narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from 'Ali: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he opened prayer said takbir, then said: I turned my face to the One who originated the heavens and the earth, upright, and I am not of the polytheists. My prayer, my rites, my life, my death are for Allah, Lord of the worlds, no partner to Him; thus I was commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the King, no god but You; You are my Lord and I am Your servant; I wronged myself and confessed my sin, so forgive me all my sins; none forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best morals; none guides to the best of them but You. Turn from me their evil; none turns from me their evil but You. At Your service, blessed service; all good is in Your hands, evil is not to You; we are by You and to You; blessed and exalted are You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. When he bowed, he said: O Allah, to You I bowed, to You I submitted, in You I believed; humbled to You are my hearing, sight, bones, marrow, sinews. When he raised his head from bowing, he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him; our Lord, to You is praise filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling what You will of a thing after. When he prostrated, he said: O Allah, to You I prostrated, to You I submitted, in You I believed; my face prostrated to the One who created it, fashioned it, perfected its form, split its hearing and sight; blessed is Allah, best of creators. When he gave salam, he said: O Allah, forgive me what I advanced, delayed, concealed, disclosed, and what You know of me better than I; You are the Advancer, You are the Delayer; no god but You."
"574","'Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Majishun narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it, except in his hadith he said: You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer."
"575","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Hasan and 'Abdullah, sons of Muhammad ibn 'Ali, from their father, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He forbade mut'a marriage on the day of Khaybar, and the meat of domestic donkeys."
"576","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyayna narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Mujahid, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to stand over his sacrificial camels, distribute their skins and coverings, and commanded me to give the butcher nothing thereof, saying: We give him from ourselves."
"577","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyayna narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Ali, who said: Fatima came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking a servant. He said: Shall I guide you — or: teach you — to what is better for you than that? When you go to your bed, glorify thirty-three, exalt, and praise, one of them thirty-three and the other thirty-four. 'Ali said: I did not leave them after I heard them. It was said to him: Not even the night of Siffin? He said: Not even the night of Siffin."
"578","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyayna narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to me, from 'Amr ibn Murra, from 'Abdullah ibn Salima, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that nothing prevented him from reciting the Qur'an except janaba."
"579","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyayna narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have exempted you from the charity of horses and slaves."
"580","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Wahb ibn al-Ajda', from 'Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not pray after 'Asr except the sun be white, high."
"581","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, who said: We were at a funeral in Baqi al-Gharqad, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and sat, and we sat around him, and he had a short stick with him, and he lowered his head and began tapping with his stick, then he said: There is none among you, there is no living soul, except that Allah has written its place in Paradise and its place in Hell, and it has been written whether it is wretched or blessed. He said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we then rest upon our writing and abandon deeds? For whoever is among the people of blessedness will end up doing the deeds of the people of blessedness, and whoever is among the people of wretchedness will end up doing the deeds of the people of wretchedness. He said: Act, for each is facilitated. As for the people of blessedness, they are facilitated to the deeds of the people of blessedness, and as for the people of wretchedness, they are facilitated to the deeds of the people of wretchedness. Then he recited: As for he who gives and fears Allah, and believes in the best reward, We will facilitate for him the easy way. But as for he who withholds and considers himself free of need, and denies the best reward, We will facilitate for him the difficult way."
"582","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant believes until he believes in four: that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner, and that I am the Messenger of Allah, He sent me with the truth, and he believes in the resurrection after death, and he believes in the decree."
"583","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abd al-Malik, from Nuaym ibn Dajajah al-Asadi, who said: I was with Ali, and Abu Masud came to him, and Ali said to him: O Farrukh, are you the one who says: There shall not come upon people one hundred years while on the earth an eye blinks? Your posterior has missed the hole in error! He only said: There shall not come upon people one hundred years while on the earth an eye blinks among those who are alive today, and the prosperity of this ummah and its joy is after the hundred."
"584","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Odd and loves the odd, so pray witr, O people of the Quran."
"585","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Ishaq, from Ali ibn Rabiah al-Asadi, who said: I saw Ali when an animal was brought to him, and he placed his foot in the stirrup and said: In the name of Allah, then when he sat straight upon it he said: Praise be to Allah, then he said: Glory be to Him who has subjected this to us, and we could never have it by our efforts, and indeed to our Lord we will return. Then he said Allahu Akbar three times, then he said: Glory be to You, I have wronged myself, so forgive me, for none forgives sins except You. Then he laughed. So I said: Why did you laugh? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day the like of what I said, then he laughed, so I said: Why did you laugh, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Our Lord marvels at the saying of His servant: Glory be to You, I have wronged myself, so forgive me, for none forgives sins except You. He said: My servant knew that he has a Lord who forgives sins."
"586","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Zibyan, who said: A woman who had committed adultery was brought to Umar, and he ordered that she be stoned. She was passed by Ali, and he recognized her, so he set her free. Umar was told: Ali took her from our hands and released her. He said: Call him to me. So he came to him, and he said: Why did you release her? He said: By Allah, you know, O Commander of the Believers, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pen has been lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, and from the child until he reaches puberty, and from the insane until he recovers. And this is the insane woman of the sons of so-and-so, and perhaps the one who committed adultery with her came to her while she was in her affliction."
"587","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Thalabah al-Himmani, who said: I heard Ali saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And I bear witness that he was among what he used to point to me: This will surely be dyed with blood from this. Meaning his beard from the blood of his head."
"588","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fermenting drinks in gourds and varnished vessels."
"589","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abdullah ibn Sabu, who said: Ali ibn Abi Talib addressed us and said: By Him who split the grain and created the soul, this will surely be dyed from this, meaning his beard from the blood of his head. He said: A man said: By Allah, none says that except that we will destroy his kin. He said: I remind you by Allah, or: I adjure you by Allah, that none be killed for me except my killer. A man said: Will you not appoint a successor, O Commander of the Believers? He said: No, but I leave you to what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left you to. They said: What will you say to Allah when you meet Him? He said: I will say: O Allah, You left me among them as long as You willed, then You took me, and I left You among them; if You will, You set them right, and if You will, You corrupt them."
"590","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, who said: Ali said: When I narrate to you a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then think of it that which is most fitting, most guiding, and most God-fearing."
"591","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Harith, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, Abdullah ibn Nujayy narrated to us, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: I had a time with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the last part of the night when I would come to him, and when I came I would ask permission; if I found him praying he would glorify Allah and I would enter, and if I found him free he would permit me. I came to him one night and he permitted me, and he said: An angel came to me, or he said: Gabriel, and I said: Enter. He said: In the house is what I cannot enter. He said: So I looked and said: I find nothing. So I searched, and he said to me: Look. So I looked, and there was a puppy of al-Husayn ibn Ali tied to the leg of the bed in the house of Umm Salamah. He said: The angels, or: We, the company of angels, do not enter a house in which there is an image, or a dog, or one who is in major impurity."
"592","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Umm Musa, who said: I heard Ali saying: I have neither had ophthalmia nor headache since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped my face and spat in my eye on the day of Khaybar, when he gave me the banner."
"593","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Umm Musa, who said: The killer of al-Zubayr asked permission to see Ali, and he said: Let him enter the Fire. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: For every prophet there is a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr."
"594","With the same chain, from Umm Musa, who said: Abdullah ibn Masud was mentioned in the presence of Ali, and he mentioned something of his virtue, then he said: He once climbed a tree wanting to pick for his companions, and his companions laughed at the thinness of his leg. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What are you laughing at? It is surely heavier on the Scale on the Day of Resurrection than Uhud."
"595","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Mughirah narrated to us, from Umm Musa, from Ali, who said: The last words of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were: Prayer, prayer; fear Allah regarding what your right hands possess."
"596","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr in the beginning of the night, in its middle, and in its end, then he fixed the witr for him at its end."
"597","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Abdullah al-Danaj, from Husayn Abu Sasan, that some people from the people of Kufa rode to Uthman ibn Affan and told him about what al-Walid had done, meaning he drinks wine. So Ali spoke to him about that, and Uthman said to him: Take your cousin and carry out the hadd upon him. He said: Stand, O Hasan, and flog him. He said: What have I to do with this? Appoint another. He said: Rather you have become weak and feeble. Stand, O Abdullah ibn Jafar, and flog him. So he began flogging him while Ali counted, until he reached forty. Then he said: Stop, or: Release him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged forty, and Abu Bakr forty, and Umar completed it eighty, and each is a sunnah."
"598","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Abu Jafar, who said: Ali flogged a man from Quraysh for the hadd for wine forty lashes with a whip that had two ends."
"599","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah narrated to me, from Ubaydullah al-Khawlani, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I entered upon Ali in his house after he had urinated, and he called for water for ablution, and we brought him a large cup holding a mudd or close to it until it was placed before him. He said: Shall I not perform for you the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes, may my father and mother be ransom for you. He said: The vessel was placed for him, and he washed his hands, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, then took with his hands and struck them upon his face, and made his thumbs meet what faces of his ears, then repeated the like of that three times. Then he took a handful of water with his right hand and poured it upon his forehead, then let it flow down his face. Then he washed his right hand to the elbow three times, then his other hand the like of that. Then he wiped his head and his ears from their backs. Then he took with his palms some water and struck them upon his feet while on them were sandals, then turned them, then upon the other the like of that. I said: In the sandals? He said: In the sandals, three times."
"600","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibrahim ibn Hunayn, from his grandfather Hunayn, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me from wearing saffron-dyed clothes, and from qassi garments, and from a gold ring, and from reciting in bowing. Ayyub said: Or he said: And that I recite while bowing. Abu Khaythamah said: Ismail retracted his saying from his grandfather, and said afterwards: From Ibrahim son of so-and-so son of Hunayn, from his father."
